{"id": "VisionFive2_OpenPLC.pdf_p47_chunk_0", "source": "VisionFive2_OpenPLC.pdf", "page": 47, "text": "| 7 - SCADA\nAdd other I/O points in the same way to observe the values of each point in real-time:\n7.1.3.5. Build a Real-Time GUI Scada/HMI Dashboard\nClick the option in the lower left corner to enter the Editor interface. The PLC program used in this document is traffic light \ncontrol, so the HMI of the traffic light scene is drawn. The drawing process is omitted here, and the main interface is as follows, \ndescribing how to connect the input and output points. First, edit the circular space Property that serves as the traffic light, taking the white circular control that indicates the red light is \noff as an example:\nFigure  7-10 Example Circular Control\nSelect Actions , this PLC program traffic light has two states: on and off, so need to add another action.", "snippet": "| 7 - SCADA\nAdd other I/O points in the same way to observe the values of each point in real-time:\n7.1.3.5. Build a Real-Time GUI Scada/HMI Dashboard\nClick the option in the lower left corner to enter"}
{"id": "VisionFive2_OpenPLC.pdf_p47_chunk_1", "source": "VisionFive2_OpenPLC.pdf", "page": 47, "text": "rol that indicates the red light is \noff as an example:\nFigure  7-10 Example Circular Control\nSelect Actions , this PLC program traffic light has two states: on and off, so need to add another action.\nBind both Actions with \nO_LEDRed point and set Bitmask to 0, which only has two values of 0/1. Therefore, set the Min and Max of the two actions to \n0/0 and 1/1, and select Type Hide and Show to indicate that the white component will be displayed when O_LEDRed is 0. When \nO_LEDRed is 1, this component is hidden, and then the red circle component is set to the opposite logic, and the logic of yellow \nand green is set. After editing, the following figure is shown:\n47 © 2018-2025 StarFive Technology \nAll rights reservedwww.starfivetech.com", "snippet": "rol that indicates the red light is \noff as an example:\nFigure  7-10 Example Circular Control\nSelect Actions , this PLC program traffic light has two states: on and off, so need to add another action."}
