{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p89_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 89, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock.\n• Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries.\nCHECK CONNECTIONS\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).\n(2) Check for loose or corroded \nconnections.\n(a) If loose or corroded, clean and \ntighten cable connections (Para 8-42).\n(b) If not loose or corroded, go to \nStep 2 of this fault.\n(3) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).CONNECTIONSCOVER\nCOVER\nCONNECTIONS\nTR01082", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical "}
