{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p93_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 93, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-41SCREWCONNECTOR P2\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9ACCESS\u001f\nPANELCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 8 of this fault. (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (7) Connect connector J2 to connector P2. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel.(2) Set multimeter to volts dc.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-41SCREWCONNECTOR P2\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9ACCESS\u001f\nPANELCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p93_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 93, "text": "onnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (7) Connect connector J2 to connector P2. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel.(2) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). TR01084", "snippet": "onnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (7) Connect connector J2 to connector P2. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel.(2) Set multimeter to volts dc."}
