{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p95_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 95, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-43SCREWCONNECTOR J2\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9\nWIRE 1ACCESS\u001f\nPANELCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 1 where wire 1 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB6. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to ohms.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-43SCREWCONNECTOR J2\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9\nWIRE 1ACCESS\u001f\nPANELCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p95_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 95, "text": "t breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB6. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J2-1.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 8 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (6) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel. TR01085", "snippet": "t breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to ohms."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p96_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 96, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-441. 24 VDC CIRCUITS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBattery connections OK.\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.Connector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.\nWire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector P2 faulty.8\nIs continuity present on wire 9 \nbetween starter motor \nsolenoid and connector P2-1?\nYESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector P2 (Para 8-49).\nReplace alternator \n(Para 8-2).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-441. 24 VDC CIRCUITS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBattery connections OK.\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.Connector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.\nWire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nPO"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p97_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 97, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-45CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to starter \nmotor solenoid.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P2-1.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nalternator (Para 8-2).\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49).\n(5) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.\n(6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(7) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01086", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-45CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multim"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p98_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 98, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-462\n2. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10. KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nHorn faulty. Wire 22 faulty. Horn switch faulty.Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-462\n2. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p98_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 98, "text": " Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, horn faulty or \nwire 2 faulty.1\nIs 24 vdc present at horn \nwhere wire 22 connects with \nhorn button pressed?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 2 of this \nfault. Go to Step 12 of this fault.", "snippet": " Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p99_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 99, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47CONNECTOR H1\nWIRE 2WIRE 22\nHORN BUTTON• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Batteries can explode from a spark. Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always wear eye protection when working with \nbatteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Disconnect connector H1 from horn.(5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 22 of connector H1. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47CONNECTOR H1\nWIRE 2WIRE 22\nHORN BUTTON• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and c"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p99_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 99, "text": ") Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Disconnect connector H1 from horn.(5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 22 of connector H1. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (8) Push horn button and note reading of \nmultimeter.(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 12 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 2 of this fault. (9) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). TR00947", "snippet": ") Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Disconnect connector H1 from horn.(5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 22 of connector H1. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p100_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 100, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-482. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 22 faulty. Horn switch Faulty.Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, wire 22 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nHorn switch Faulty.Wire 20 faulty.Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-482. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 22 faulty. Horn switch Faulty.Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Relay K4 f"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p100_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 100, "text": "Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, horn switch \nfaulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at horn \nswitch where wire 22 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 3 of this \nfault. 3\nIs 24 vdc present at horn \nswitch where wire 20 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault. Replace horn switch (Para 8-7).Repair wire 22 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p101_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 101, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49SCREW\nINSTRUMENT\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 22\nWIRE 20HORN BUTTONVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and instrument \npanel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nhorn switch where wire 22 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (6) Press horn switch and note reading of \nmultimeter. (a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 22 \n(Para 8-48). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nhorn switch where wire 20 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49SCREW\nINSTRUMENT\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 22\nWIRE 20HORN BUTTONVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and instrument \npanel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+)"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p101_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 101, "text": "Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nhorn switch where wire 20 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, replace horn \nswitch (Para 8-7). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (6) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. TR00948", "snippet": "Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nhorn switch where wire 20 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p102_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 102, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-502. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, wire 20 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. Wire 20 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-502. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p102_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 102, "text": "Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, circuit breaker \nCB10 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB10 where wire 20 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 5 of this \nfault. 5\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB10 where wire 29 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 6 of this \nfault.Repair wire 20 \n(Para 8-48). Replace circuit breaker CB10 \n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p103_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 103, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51SCREW\nWIRE 20WIRE 29CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER\u001f\nCB10ACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB10 where wire 20 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 20 \n(Para 8-48). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB10 where wire 29 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51SCREW\nWIRE 20WIRE 29CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER\u001f\nCB10ACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+)"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p103_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 103, "text": " Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB10 where wire 29 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).\n(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 6 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, replace circuit \nbreaker CB10 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).TR00949", "snippet": " Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB10 where wire 29 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p104_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 104, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-522. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, wire 29 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, relay K4 \nfaulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K4 \nwhere wire 29 connects?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-522. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 f"}
