{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p105_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 105, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-53SCREWRELAY\u001f\nK4\nWIRE 29\nWIRE 1ACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nrelay K4 where wire 29 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable (Para \n8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 29 \n(Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nrelay K4 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 8 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-53SCREWRELAY\u001f\nK4\nWIRE 29\nWIRE 1ACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nrelay K4 where wire 29 connects. (3) Connect"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p105_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 105, "text": "lay K4 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 8 of this fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is present, replace relay \nK4 (Para 8-23). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).TR00950", "snippet": "lay K4 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 8 of this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p106_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 106, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-542. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, repair wire 1. KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, replace circuit \nbreaker CB6.8\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 9 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-542. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty.Cir"}
