{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p107_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 107, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-55SCREW\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6 WIRE 1WIRE 9ACCESS \u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable (Para \n8-44). (a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 9 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 1 \n(Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 10 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-55SCREW\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6 WIRE 1WIRE 9ACCESS \u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 c"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p107_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 107, "text": " CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 10 of this fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is present, replace circuit \nbreaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). TR00951", "snippet": " CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 10 of this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p108_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 108, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-562. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-562. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p108_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 108, "text": ".Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.10\nIs 24 vdc present on \nconnector J2-1? YESNOGo to Step 11 of \nthis fault. 11\nIs 24 vdc present at starter \nsolenoid where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 16 of \nthis fault. Go to Step 13 of this fault.Go to Step 15 of this fault.", "snippet": ".Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p109_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 109, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J2-1. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 11 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 15 \nof this fault. (6) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect mult"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p109_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 109, "text": "s dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).\n(a) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 13 of this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 16 \nof this fault. (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). TR00952", "snippet": "s dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p110_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 110, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-582. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nHorn faulty. Wire 22 faulty.Horn switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Relay K4 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is present, horn faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-582. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nHorn faulty. Wire 22 faulty.Horn switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p110_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 110, "text": "CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2.12\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween negative (–) battery cable and wire 2 on horn? YESNOGo to Step 13 of \nthis fault. 13\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween connector P2-2 and \nwire 2 on horn? YESNORepair wire 2 \n(Para 8-49).Replace horn (Para \n8-41).", "snippet": "CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p111_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 111, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59NEGATIVE \u001f\nBATTERY \u001f\nCABLE\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-2CONNECTOR H1\nWIRE 2HORN CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector H1 from horn. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 2 at horn. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nnegative battery cable. (a) If continuity is not present, go to \nStep 13 of this fault. (b) If continuity is present, replace \nhorn (Para 8-41). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 2 at horn connector H1. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nconnector P2-2.(a) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 (Para 8-49). (b) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 14 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59NEGATIVE \u001f\nBATTERY \u001f\nCABLE\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-2CONNECTOR H1\nWIRE 2HORN CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector H1 from horn. (2) Set multimeter to ohms"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p111_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 111, "text": "horn connector H1. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nconnector P2-2.(a) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 (Para 8-49). (b) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 14 of this fault.\nTR00953", "snippet": "horn connector H1. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nconnector P2-2.(a) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 (Para 8-49). (b) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 14 of this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p112_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 112, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-602. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Connector J2-1 OK. Connector P2-1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2-2 faulty. Connector P2-2 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-602. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHorn OK. Wire 22 OK. Horn switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.C"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p112_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 112, "text": "rcuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector P2 faulty.14\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween connector J2-2 and \nnegative battery cable? YESNORepair \nconnector J2 (Para 8-48). 15\nIs continuity present on wire 9 \nbetween connector P2-1 and \nwire 9, where wire 9 connects \nto circuit breaker CB6? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector P2 (Para 8-49).Replace horn (Para 8-41).", "snippet": "rcuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 29 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p113_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 113, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-61SCREW\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6NUT\nLOCKWASHERWIRE 9ACCESS \u001f\nPANELNEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1J2-2\nCONNECTOR J2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J2-2. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nnegative battery cable. (a) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J2 and perform Step (4) \nbelow. (b) If continuity is present, replace \nhorn and perform Step (4) below. (4) Connect connector J2 to connector P2 \nand negative battery cable to negative side of battery (Para 8-44). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Remove one nut and lockwasher from \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-61SCREW\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6NUT\nLOCKWASHERWIRE 9ACCESS \u001f\nPANELNEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1J2-2\nCONNECTOR J2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimet"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p113_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 113, "text": " (Para 8-44). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Remove one nut and lockwasher from \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6.\n(4) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 9. (5) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nconnector P2-1.(a) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 and perform \nStep (6) and Step (7) below. (b) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault. (6) Connect connector J2 to connector P2 \nand negative battery cable to negative \nside of battery (Para 8-44). (7) Connect wire 9 to circuit breaker CB6 \nand install lockwasher and nut. (8) Install access panel and four screws. TR00954", "snippet": " (Para 8-44). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Remove one nut and lockwasher from \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p114_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 114, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-622. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHorn OK.\nWire 22 OK.\nHorn switch OK.Wire 20 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB10 OK.\nWire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.Connector P2 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector J2-1 faulty.16\nIs continuity present on wire 9 \nbetween connector J2-1 and \nwhere wire 9 connects to starter solenoid?\nYESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector J2 \n(Para 8-48).\nService or replace batteries (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-622. HORN DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHorn OK.\nWire 22 OK.\nHorn switch OK.Wire 20 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB10 OK.\nWire 29 OK.Relay K4 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.C"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p115_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 115, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-63CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J2-1.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 9 at starting motor solenoid.\n(a) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J2 or wire 9.\n(b) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 11 of this fault and perform Step (4) and Step (5) below.\n(4) Connect connector J2 to connector P2 \nand negative battery cable to negative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(5) Connect wire 9 to circuit breaker CB5 \nand install lockwasher and nut.\n(6) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR00955", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-63CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J2-1.\n(3) "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p116_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 116, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-642\n3. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Auxiliary fuel shut -off switch OFF\nParking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10. KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBack-up alarm faulty. Wire 21 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Back-up switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty.Circuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-642\n3. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultime"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p116_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 116, "text": "lty. Back-up switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty.Circuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs 24 vdc present at wire 21 of \nthe back-up alarm?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 2 of this \nfault. Go to Step 14 of \nthis fault.", "snippet": "lty. Back-up switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty.Circuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p117_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 117, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-65WIRE 21BACK-UP ALARM WIRE 2\nENGINE START SWITCHTRAVEL\nSELECTLEVER• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (3) Disconnect wire 21 and wire 2 from \nback-up alarm. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-65WIRE 21BACK-UP ALARM WIRE 2\nENGINE START SWITCHTRAVEL\nSELECTLEVER• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p117_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 117, "text": " wire 21 and wire 2 from \nback-up alarm. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (8) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-\n673-10). (9) Place travel select lever in reverse “R” \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 14 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 2. (10) Place travel select lever in neutral “N” \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). TR01094", "snippet": " wire 21 and wire 2 from \nback-up alarm. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p118_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 118, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-663. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 21 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Back-up switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty.Circuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 21 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBack-up switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-663. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 21 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Back-up switch faulty. Wire 20"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p118_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 118, "text": "1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 21 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBack-up switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, back-up switch \nfaulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at back-up \nswitch where wire 21 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 3 of this \nfault. 3\nIs 24 vdc present at back-up \nswitch where wire 20 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault.Go to Step 17 of this fault. Replace back-up switch (Para 8-40).", "snippet": "1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 21 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBack-up switch faulty. Wire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p119_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 119, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-67\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from left-hand \ninstrument panel and lift selector panel \nout to get to back-up alarm switch. (2) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (3) Disconnect wire 21 from back-up \nswitch. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc.(5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 21 where wire 21 connects to \nback-up switch. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (7) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (8) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Place travel select lever in reverse “R” \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 17 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-67\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from left-hand \ninstrument panel and lift selector panel \nout to get to back-up alarm switch. (2) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p119_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 119, "text": "0-673-10). (9) Place travel select lever in reverse “R” \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 17 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault.\n(10) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Place travel select lever in neutral “N” \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (12) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect wire 20 from back-up \nswitch. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 20. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, replace back-\nup switch (Para 8-40). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition engine start switch(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).", "snippet": "0-673-10). (9) Place travel select lever in reverse “R” \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 17 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p119_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 119, "text": "0). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition engine start switch(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).\nTR01095", "snippet": "0). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition engine start switch(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p120_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 120, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-683. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 20 faulty. Circuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 20 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 21 OK.Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-683. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 20 faulty. Circuit"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p120_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 120, "text": "re 20 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, circuit breaker \nCB2 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB2 where wire 20 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 5 of this \nfault. 5\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB2 where wire 5 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 6 of this \nfault.Repair wire 20 (Para 8-48). Replace circuit \nbreaker CB2 \n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "re 20 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p121_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 121, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-69WIRE 20\nWIRE 5CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER \u001f\nCB2SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Remove four screws and access panel. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB2 where wire 20 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 20 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-69WIRE 20\nWIRE 5CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER \u001f\nCB2SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Remove four screws and access panel. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p121_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 121, "text": " wire 20 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB2 where wire 5 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, replace circuit \nbreaker CB2 (Para 8-11). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 6 of this fault. (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44).TR01096", "snippet": " wire 20 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p122_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 122, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-703. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 5 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 5 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 21 OK.Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-703. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. POSSIB"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p122_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 122, "text": "tch OK. Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, relay K2 faulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 5 connects? YESNOGo to Step 7 of this \nfault. 7\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 3 connects? YESNOGo to Step 8 of this \nfault.Repair wire 5 (Para 8-48). Replace relay K2 (Para 8-23).", "snippet": "tch OK. Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 3 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty."}
