{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p126_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 126, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-743. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 1 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 21 OK.Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK.Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-743. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p126_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 126, "text": "breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK.Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, circuit breaker \nCB6 faulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 11 of \nthis fault. 11\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 12 of \nthis fault.Repair wire 1 (Para 8-48). Replace circuit \nbreaker CB6 \n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK.Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p127_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 127, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-75CIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 1WIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 1 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 11 of this fault. (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-75CIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 1WIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p127_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 127, "text": "ive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(a) If 24 vdc is present, replace circuit \nbreaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). TR01099", "snippet": "ive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p128_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 128, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-763. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 21 OK.Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK.Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-763. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p128_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 128, "text": "1 OK.Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK.Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R 89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.12\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector P2-1? YESNORepair connector \nP2 or wire 9 \n(Para 8-49). 13\nIs 24 vdc present at starter \nmotor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNOService or replace \nbattery cable(Para 8-44). Go to Step 20 of this fault.Go to Step 19 of this fault.", "snippet": "1 OK.Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK.Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p129_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 129, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-77STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1‘\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector P2-1. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 19 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nconnector P2 or wire 9 (Para 8-49). (6) Connect connector J2 to connector P2. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to starter \nmotor solenoid. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-77STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1‘\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect mult"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p129_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 129, "text": "ST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to starter \nmotor solenoid. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 20 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, service or \nreplace battery cable (Para 8-44). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). TR01100", "snippet": "ST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to starter \nmotor solenoid. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p130_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 130, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-783. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is present, back-up \nalarm faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-783. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p130_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 130, "text": " OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R 91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 or connector J2.14\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween negative battery \ncable and wire 2 at back-up \nalarm? YESNOGo to Step 15 of \nthis fault. 15\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween connector J2-2 and \nwire 2 on back-up alarm? YESNOReplace back-up \nalarm (Para 8-39). Repair connector J2 or wire 2 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": " OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. Wire 1 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p131_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 131, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-79WIRE 21BACK-UP ALARM WIRE 2NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nnegative cable at battery. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 2 at back of back-up alarm. (a) If continuity is present, replace \nback-up alarm (Para 8-39). (b) If continuity is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J2-2. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 2 where it connects to back-up alarm.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-79WIRE 21BACK-UP ALARM WIRE 2NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter posit"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p131_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 131, "text": "nect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J2-2. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 2 where it connects to back-up alarm.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). TR01101", "snippet": "nect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J2-2. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 2 where it connects to back-up alarm.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p132_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 132, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-803. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 9 OK. Connector J2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R 91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 2 \nor connector P2 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 9 OK. Connector J2 OK. Connector P2 OK.Wire 2 OK.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-803. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p132_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 132, "text": "alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 9 OK. Connector J2 OK. Connector P2 OK.Wire 2 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.Wire 21 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R 91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 21 \nor connector J1 faulty.16\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween connector P2-2 and \nnegative battery cable? YESNORepair wire 2 or \nconnector P2 (Para 8-49). 17\nIs continuity present on \nwire 21 between \nconnector J1-19 and where \nwire 21 connects at back-up switch? YESNORepair wire 21 or \nconnector J1 (Para 8-48).Replace back-up alarm (Para 8-39).", "snippet": "alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK. Wire 20 OK.Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 9 OK. Connector J2 OK. Connector P2 OK.Wire 2 OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p133_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 133, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-81CONNECTOR J1J1-19\nCONNECTOR J1\nCONNECTOR P1NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2P2-2WIRE 21BACK-UP ALARM WIRE 2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nnegative battery cable. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nconnector P2-2. (a) If continuity is present, replace \nback-up alarm (Para 8-39). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (4) Connect connector J2 to connector P2. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J1-19. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 21 where wire 21 connects to back-up switch.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-81CONNECTOR J1J1-19\nCONNECTOR J1\nCONNECTOR P1NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2P2-2WIRE 21BACK-UP ALARM WIRE 2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect m"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p133_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 133, "text": "Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J1-19. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 21 where wire 21 connects to back-up switch.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 18 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 21 or connector J1 (Para 8-48). TR01102", "snippet": "Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector J1-19. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 21 where wire 21 connects to back-up switch."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p134_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 134, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-823. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 9 OK. Connector J2 OK.Connector P2 OK. Wire 2 OK. Connector J1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P1 faulty. Wire 21 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 21 \nor connector P1 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Connector J1 OK\nWire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-823. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK. Wire 21 OK. Back-up switch OK.Wire 20 OK. Circuit breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p134_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 134, "text": "breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector J2 faulty.18\nIs continuity present on \nwire 21 between connector P1-19 and where \nwire 21 connects to back-up \nalarm? YESNORepair wire 21 or \nconnector P1 \n(Para 8-49). Go to Step 3 of this \nfault. 19\nIs continuity present between \nconnector J2-1 and wire 9 at \ncircuit breaker CB6? YESNOReplace wire 9 or \nconnector J2(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "breaker CB2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Relay K2 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K1 OK.Wire 1 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p135_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 135, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-83WIRE 21 BACK-UP ALARM\nCONNECTOR J1 P1-19\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR J2CONNECTOR P2J2-1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nconnector P1-19. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 21 where wire 21 connects at \nback-up alarm. (a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 21 or connector P1 (Para 8-49). (4) Connect connector J1 to connector P1. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J2-1. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nwire 9. (a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 20 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-83WIRE 21 BACK-UP ALARM\nCONNECTOR J1 P1-19\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR J2CONNECTOR P2J2-1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter p"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p135_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 135, "text": "(2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J2-1. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nwire 9. (a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 20 of this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (5) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel. TR01103", "snippet": "(2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J2-1. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nwire 9. (a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 20 of this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p136_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 136, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-843. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK.\nConnector J1 OK\nWire 21 OK.Back-up switch OK.\nWire 20 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK.\nRelay K2 OK.\nWire 3 OK.Relay K1 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.Connector J2 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector P2 faulty.20\nIs continuity present between \nstarter motor solenoid wire 9 \nand connector P2-1?\nYESNOReplace wire 9 or \nconnector P2 (Para 8-49).\nService or replace batteries (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-843. BACK-UP ALARM DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBack-up alarm OK.\nConnector J1 OK\nWire 21 OK.Back-up switch OK.\nWire 20 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB2 OK.Wire 5 OK.\nRelay K2 OK.\n"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p137_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 137, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-85CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarter motor solenoid where wire 9 connects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P2-1.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42).\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49).\n(4) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.\n(5) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01104", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-85CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarter motor solenoi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p138_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 138, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-862\n4. CAB DEFROSTER FAN(S) DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Auxiliary fuel shut -off switch OFF\nParking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10. KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFan(s) faulty. Wire 80 faulty. Circuit breaker CB8 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, fan or switch \nfaulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-862\n4. CAB DEFROSTER FAN(S) DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMu"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p138_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 138, "text": "re 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, fan or switch \nfaulty.\nGo to Step 3 of this fault.1\nIs 24 vdc present at wire 80 of \nnon-operational fan?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNO", "snippet": "re 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, fan or switch \nfaulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p139_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 139, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-87\n• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, neckl ace, and any other jewelry before worki ng around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover(s) (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (3) Disconnect wire 80 female connector \nfrom male connector. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc.(5) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 80 female end. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-87\n• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, neckl ace, and any other jewelry before worki ng around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electric"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p139_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 139, "text": "onnect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 80 female end. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(8) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 2 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault. (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). TR01087", "snippet": "onnect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nwire 80 female end. (6) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p140_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 140, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-884. CAB DEFROSTER FAN(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFan(s) faulty. Wire 80 faulty.Circuit breaker CB8 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K1 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, fan \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nFan OK. Ground OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 80 faulty.Circuit breaker CB8 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 80 faulty.2\nIs continuity present between \nfan ground and fan guard?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-884. CAB DEFROSTER FAN(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFan(s) faulty. Wire 80 faulty.Circuit breaker CB8 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K1 faulty.Wire "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p140_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 140, "text": "ty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 80 faulty.2\nIs continuity present between \nfan ground and fan guard?\nYESNOReplace faulty fan \n(Para 17-6). 3\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB8 where wire 80 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault. Repair wire 80 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "ty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 80 faulty.2\nIs continuity present between \nfan ground and fan guard?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p141_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 141, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-89\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nfan ground. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nfan guard. (a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, replace \nfaulty fan (Para 17-6). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB8 where wire 80 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 80 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-89\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nfan ground. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nfan guard. (a) If continuity "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p141_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 141, "text": "t negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 80 \n(Para 8-48).\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-42). TR01088", "snippet": "t negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 80 \n(Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p142_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 142, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-904. CAB DEFROSTER FAN(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nFan OK. Ground OK. Wire 80 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB8 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K1 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, circuit breaker \nCB8 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nFan OK. Ground OK. Wire 80 OK. Circuit breaker CB8 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Relay K1 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 3 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB8 where wire 3 \nconnects?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-904. CAB DEFROSTER FAN(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nFan OK. Ground OK. Wire 80 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB8 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K1 faulty.Wire 1 fau"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p142_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 142, "text": "ector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 3 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB8 where wire 3 \nconnects?\nYESNOGo to Step 5 of this \nfault. 5\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K1 \n(run relay) where wire 3 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 6 of this \nfault.Replace circuit breaker CB8 (Para 8-11). Repair wire 3 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "ector J2 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is present, wire 3 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB8 where wire 3 \nconnects?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p143_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 143, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-91WIRE 3CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER\u001f\nCB8\nRELAY K1\nWIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB8 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, replace faulty \ncircuit breaker CB8 (Para 8-11). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault. (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nrelay K1 where wire 3 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-91WIRE 3CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER\u001f\nCB8\nRELAY K1\nWIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \ncircuit breaker CB8 where wire 3 connects. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p143_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 143, "text": "ition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nrelay K1 where wire 3 connects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch ON, BUT DO \nNOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 3 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 6 of this fault. (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). TR01089", "snippet": "ition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable \n(Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive (+) lead to \nrelay K1 where wire 3 connects."}
