{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p156_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 156, "text": "tinues. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.\nWire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty. Wire 13 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 is faulty.5\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6 \n(Para 8-11)4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 connects? YESNOGo to Step 15 of \nthis fault.", "snippet": "tinues. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p157_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 157, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-105WIRE 9\nWIRE 1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault. (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-105WIRE 9\nWIRE 1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead ("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p157_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 157, "text": "LTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01146", "snippet": "LTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p158_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 158, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1065. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty.Wire 13 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test. STE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 1 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1065. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p158_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 158, "text": " Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty.\nWire 13 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, run relay is \nfaulty.7\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nwhere wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay \n(Para 8-23).6\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nwhere wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1 (Para \n8-48).", "snippet": " Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p159_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 159, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-107RELAY K1\nWIRE 3 WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nthe run relay where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-107RELAY K1\nWIRE 3 WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negativ"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p159_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 159, "text": " positive lead (+) to \nthe run relay where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(6) (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01147", "snippet": " positive lead (+) to \nthe run relay where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p160_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 160, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1085. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty.Wire 13 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test. STE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 3 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty. Wire 13 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1085. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. POSSI"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p160_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 160, "text": " CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty. Wire 13 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB4 is faulty.9\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB4 where wire 40 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB4\n(Para 8-11).8\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB4 where wire 3 connects? YESNORepair wire 3\n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": " CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty. Wire 13 faulty.Connector J1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p161_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 161, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-109WIRE 40 WIRE 3\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB4VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 3 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-109WIRE 40 WIRE 3\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB4VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 3 \nconnects. (3) Con"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p161_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 161, "text": "8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 40 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB4 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (para 8-44).TR01144", "snippet": "8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p162_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 162, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1105. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB4 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 40 faulty.\nBlackout light switch faulty.\nAuxiliary light switch faulty.Wire 13 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 40 is \nfautly.10\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J3-F where wire 40 \nconnects?\nYESNORepair wire 40\n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1105. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p163_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 163, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-111SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove connector J3 from blackout \nlight switch. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-F where wire 40 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-111SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove connector J3 from blackout \nlight switch. (2) Set multimeter to volts d"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p163_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 163, "text": "24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(9) Connect connector J3 to blackout light \nswitch. TR01145", "snippet": "24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p164_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 164, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1125. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty.Auxiliary light switch faulty.Wire 13 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.11\nIs 24 vdc present at female \nconnector where wire 13 \nconnects?\nYESNOGo to Step 12 of \nthis fault.\nGo to Step 13 of \nthis fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1125. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p165_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 165, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-113ENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nMALE\nCONNECTORWIRE 13FEMALECONNECTORWIRE 13VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove gage light from instrument \npanel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfemale connector where wire 13 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-113ENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nMALE\nCONNECTORWIRE 13FEMALECONNECTORWIRE 13VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove gage light from instrument \npanel. (2) Set multime"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p165_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 165, "text": "10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (11) Connect female to male connector for \nwire 13. TR01148", "snippet": "10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p166_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 166, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1145. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Auxiliary light switch faulty. Wire 13 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test. STE/ICE-R #88\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, blackout \ncontrol switch or wire 13 are faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. Auxiliary light switch OK. Wire 13 OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1145. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p166_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 166, "text": "ire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. Auxiliary light switch OK. Wire 13 OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nSocket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test. STE/ICE-R #88\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, gage \nlight socket is faulty.13\nIs continuity present between \ngage light center conductor \nand wire 13 male connector? YESNOReplace gage light \nsocket (Para 8-6).12\nIs continuity present between \nconnector J3-B and wire 13 female connector? YESNORepair wire 13\n(Para 8-48). Replace blackout light switch (Para 8-13).", "snippet": "ire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. Auxiliary light switch OK. Wire 13 OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p167_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 167, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-115BLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHJ3-B\nCONNECTOR J3\nMALE\nCONNECTORWIRE 13FEMALECONNECTORWIRE 13CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove connector J3 from blackout \nlight switch. (2) Disconnect female from male \nconnector on wire 13. (3) Set multimeter to ohms. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-B where wire 13 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nfemale connector of wire 13.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nblackout light switch (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 13 (Para 8-48). (6) Connect connector J3 to blackout light \nswitch. (7) Connect female to male connector of \nwire 13. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect female from male \nconnector on wire 13.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-115BLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHJ3-B\nCONNECTOR J3\nMALE\nCONNECTORWIRE 13FEMALECONNECTORWIRE 13CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove connector J3 from blackout \nli"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p167_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 167, "text": "epair \nwire 13 (Para 8-48). (6) Connect connector J3 to blackout light \nswitch. (7) Connect female to male connector of \nwire 13. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect female from male \nconnector on wire 13.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nsocket center conductor where wire 13 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nmale connector of wire 13.(a)  If continuity is present, go to \nStep 14 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, replace \ngage light socket (Para 8-6). (5) Connect female to male connector of \nwire 13. TR01149", "snippet": "epair \nwire 13 (Para 8-48). (6) Connect connector J3 to blackout light \nswitch. (7) Connect female to male connector of \nwire 13. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect female from male \nconnector on wire 13."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p168_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 168, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1165. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK. Wire 13 OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nSocket(s) faulty. Faulty GroundTEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf grounding fins are not evenly \nspread out and applying pressure to side of gage, adjust for proper \nfit for ground. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK.Wire 13 OK. Socket(s) OK.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1165. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p168_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 168, "text": "NOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK.Wire 13 OK. Socket(s) OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFautly Wire 9\nFaulty Connector J2\nFaulty Connector P2TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test. STE/ICE-R #88\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector P2 are faulty.15\nIs continuity present on wire 9 \nbetween starter motor \nsolenoid and connector P2-1? YESNORepair wire 9 or\nconnector P2(Para 8-49).14\nIs spacing of grounding fins \ncorrect for proper ground? YESNOAdjust grounding \nfins (Para 8-6). Replace bulb \n(Para 8-6).", "snippet": "NOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK.Wire 13 OK. Socket(s) OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p169_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 169, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-117LIGHT\u001f\nSOCKET\nGROUNDING\u001f\nFINSBULBINSTRUMENT\u001f\nPANEL SCREW\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Lift instrument panel out to remove \ngage light from gage. (a) If grounding fins fit properly, \nreplace bulb (Para 8-6). (b) If grounding fins are not fitting \nproperly, adjust by performing \nSteps (2) and (3) below. (2) Remove bulb from socket. (3) Use small common screwdriver to \nadjust ground fins inward or outward \nfor proper fit. (4) Connect female to male connector.(5) Install gage light into gage.(6) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-117LIGHT\u001f\nSOCKET\nGROUNDING\u001f\nFINSBULBINSTRUMENT\u001f\nPANEL SCREW\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Lift instrument panel out to r"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p169_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 169, "text": "rument panel and four \nscrews. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P2-1. (a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). TR01150", "snippet": "rument panel and four \nscrews. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p170_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 170, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1185. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nRun relay OK.Wire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB4 OK.\nWire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK.\nWire 13 OK.\nSocket(s) OK.Connector P2 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFautly Wire 9Faulty Connector J2TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #88\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector J2 are faulty.16\nIs continuity present between \ncircuit breaker CB6 where \nwire 9 connects and \nconnector J2?\nYESNORepair wire 9 or\nconnector J2\n(Para 8-48).\nService or replace \nbattery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1185. INSTRUMENT PANEL GAGE LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nRun relay OK.Wire 3 OK.\nCircu"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p171_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 171, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-119WIRE 1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWPANELCONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J2-1.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42).  \n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48).\n(5) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel.\n(6) Connect connector P2 to connector J2.\n(7) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01151", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-119WIRE 1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWPANELCONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(3)"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p172_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 172, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1202\n6. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb(s) faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1202\n6. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\n"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p172_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 172, "text": "uit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.\nSocket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, bulb is \nfaulty.1\nIs continuity present on faulty \nheadlight?START\nYESNOReplace bulb \n(Para 8-31).", "snippet": "uit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p173_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 173, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-121MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORBULBHEADLIGHT\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty headlight \n(Para 8-31).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale connector.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother male connector.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 2 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-31).\nTR01738", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-121MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORBULBHEADLIGHT\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty headlight \n(Para 8-31).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p174_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 174, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1226. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1226. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. W"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p174_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 174, "text": "nnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty.\nWire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, service or \nreplace battery cable.3\nIs 24 vdc present at starter \nmotor solenoid where wire 9 connects? YESNOService or replace \nbattery cable \n(Para 8-42).2\nIs 24 vdc present at headlight \nsocket?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page. YESNOGo to Step 3 of this \nfault. Go to Step 14 of this fault.", "snippet": "nnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p175_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 175, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-123STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9FEMALE CONNECTORWIRE 49HEADLIGHT• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfemale connector of faulty socket \nwhere wire 49 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-123STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9FEMALE CONNECTORWIRE 49HEADLIGHT• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p175_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 175, "text": "o \nfemale connector of faulty socket \nwhere wire 49 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 14 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault. (6) Turn blackout light switch OFF position \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery covers (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarter motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault.", "snippet": "o \nfemale connector of faulty socket \nwhere wire 49 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p175_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 175, "text": "ects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, service or \nreplace battery cable (Para 8-42). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01739", "snippet": "ects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p176_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 176, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1246. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1246. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. W"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p176_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 176, "text": "OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 is faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present on circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 connects? YESNOGo to Step 15 of \nthis fault. 5\nIs 24 vdc present on circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 connects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p177_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 177, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-125SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault. (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-125SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead ("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p177_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 177, "text": "). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a)  If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b)  If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01740", "snippet": "). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p178_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 178, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1266. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 1 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1266. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Ru"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p178_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 178, "text": " CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nSocket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, run relay is \nfaulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at the run \nrelay where wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1\n(Para 8-48). 7\nIs 24 vdc present at the run \nrelay where wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay \n(Para 8-23).", "snippet": " CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p179_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 179, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-127RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-127RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negat"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p179_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 179, "text": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01741", "snippet": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p180_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 180, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1286. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 3 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1286. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PR"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p180_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 180, "text": "ire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB4 is faulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB4 where wire 3 connects? YESNORepair wire 3\n(Para 8-48). 9\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB4 where wire 40 connects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB4(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "ire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p181_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 181, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-129CIRCUIT BREAKER CB4WIRE 3 WIRE 40VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-129CIRCUIT BREAKER CB4WIRE 3 WIRE 40VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 3 connects. (3) Conne"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p181_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 181, "text": "-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 40 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB4 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01742", "snippet": "-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p182_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 182, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1306. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 40 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1306. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p182_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 182, "text": " Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, blackout \nlight switch or wire 49 are faulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J3-F where wire 40 connects? YESNORepair wire 40\n(Para 8-48). 11\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J1-2 where wire 49 connects? YESNOGo to Step 12 of \nthis fault. Go to Step 13 of this fault.", "snippet": " Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 49 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p183_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 183, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-131SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3\nJ1-2\nCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) Lift instrument panel out to remove \nconnector J3 from blackout light switch. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-F where wire 40 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-131SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3\nJ1-2\nCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) L"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p183_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 183, "text": "rn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48).\n(8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (10) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (11) Install four screws to secure instrument \npanel. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J1-2 where wire 49 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER.", "snippet": "rn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p183_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 183, "text": "nect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER.\nDRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01743", "snippet": "nect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p184_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 184, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1326. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty.Wire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, blackout \nlight switch or wire 49 is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1326. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p184_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 184, "text": "n relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 49 is \nfaulty.12\nIs continuity present between \nconnector J3-M and connector J1-2? YESNORepair wire 49 \n(Para 8-48). 13\nIs 24 vdc present at headlight \nmale connector where wire 49 connects? YESNORepair wire 49\n(Para 8-48).Replace blackout \nlight switch\n(Para 8-13).", "snippet": "n relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 49 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p185_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 185, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-133BLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nJ3-M\nCONNECTOR J3\nJ1-2\nCONNECTOR J1\nMALE CONNECTORSCREW\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) Lift instrument panel out to remove \nconnector J3 from blackout light switch. (3) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (4) Set multimeter to ohms. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-M where wire 49 connects. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-2 where wire 49 connects.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nblackout light switch (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 49 (Para 8-48). (7) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (8) Connect connector J1 to connector P1.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-133BLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nJ3-M\nCONNECTOR J3\nJ1-2\nCONNECTOR J1\nMALE CONNECTORSCREW\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p185_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 185, "text": "h (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 49 (Para 8-48). (7) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (8) Connect connector J1 to connector P1.\n(9) Install four screws to secure instrument \npanel. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nheadlight male connector where wire 49 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 14 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 49 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "h (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 49 (Para 8-48). (7) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (8) Connect connector J1 to connector P1."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p185_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 185, "text": "ult. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 49 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01744", "snippet": "ult. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 49 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p186_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 186, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1346. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK. Wire 49 OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nSocket(s) faulty. Ground faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present wire 2 \nground or headlight socket is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. Wire 49 OK. Socket(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1346. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p186_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 186, "text": ".Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. Wire 49 OK. Socket(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present wire 9 or \nconnector P2 are faulty.14\nIs continuity present between \nheadlight socket female conductor ground (wire 2) \nand ground cable? YESNORepair wire 2\n(Para 8-49). 15\nIs continuity present between \nstarter motor solenoid and connector P2-1? YESNORepair wire 9 or\nconnector P2\n(Para 8-49).Replace bulb\n(Para 8-31).", "snippet": ".Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. Wire 49 OK. Socket(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p187_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 187, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-135CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1GROUND CABLEFEMALE\u001f\nCONNECTORMALE\u001f\nCONNECTOR\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect ground female connector \nfrom male ground connector. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground female connector at headlight \nsocket. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground cable.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-31). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 (Para 8-49). (5) Connect ground female connector to \nmale connector. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-135CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1GROUND CABLEFEMALE\u001f\nCONNECTORMALE\u001f\nCONNECTOR\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect ground female connector \nfrom mal"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p187_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 187, "text": "connector to \nmale connector. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P2-1.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49).", "snippet": "connector to \nmale connector. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p188_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 188, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1366. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK.\nBlackout light switch OK.\nWire 49 OK.Socket(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector J2 is faulty.16\nIs continuity present between \ncircuit breaker CB6 and \nconnector J2?\nYESNORepair wire 9 or\nconnector J2\n(Para 8-48).\nService or replace battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1366. ONE OR BOTH HEADLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire 3 OK.\n"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p189_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 189, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-137CONNECTOR P2P2-1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. \n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6. \n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J2-1.(a) If continuity is present, service \nbattery (Para 8-42). \n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48).\n(4) Install access panel and four screws.(5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegtive side of battery.\n(6) Install battery covers (Para 8-42).(7) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.\nTR01746", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-137CONNECTOR P2P2-1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. \n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at"}
