{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p222_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 222, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1708. TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulbs OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB4 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 40 faulty.\nBlackout light switch faulty.\nWire 46 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.\nSocket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 40 \nfaulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J3-F (wire 40)?\nYESNORepair wire 40 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1708. TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulbs OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nCircuit brea"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p223_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 223, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-171SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) Lift instrument panel out to remove \nconnector J3 from blackout light switch. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-F (wire 40). (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-171SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) Lift instrument panel out to re"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p223_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 223, "text": "M 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (10) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (11) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. TR01709", "snippet": "M 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p224_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 224, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1728. TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulbs OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty.Wire 46 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, blackout \nlight switch or wire 46 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulbs OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 46 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICER #88.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1728. TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulbs OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit brea"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p224_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 224, "text": "ircuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 46 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICER #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, blackout \ncontrol switch or wire 46 faulty.11\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J1-8 (wire 46)? YESNOGo to Step 12 of \nthis fault. 12\nIs continuity present between \nconnector J3-H and \nconnector J1-8? YESNORepair wire 46 \n(Para 8-48).Go to Step 13 of \nthis fault. Replace blackout light switch \n(Para 8-13).", "snippet": "ircuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 46 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICER #88."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p225_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 225, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-173SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-H\nCONNECTOR J3\nJ1-8\nCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J1-8 (wire 46). (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-173SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-H\nCONNECTOR J3\nJ1-8\nCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Disconnect conne"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p225_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 225, "text": "10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and instrument \npanel. (2) Lift instrument panel out to remove \nconnector J3 from blackout light switch. (3) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (4) Set multimeter to ohms.(5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-H (wire 46). (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-8 (wire 46). (a) If continuity is present, replace \nblackout light switch (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 46 (Para 8-48). (7) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch.", "snippet": "10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p225_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 225, "text": " is present, replace \nblackout light switch (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 46 (Para 8-48). (7) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch.\n(8) Connect connector J1 to connector P1.(9) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. TR01710", "snippet": " is present, replace \nblackout light switch (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 46 (Para 8-48). (7) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch."}
