{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p234_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 234, "text": "OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 is faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 connects? YESNOGo to Step 15 of \nthis fault. 5\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 connects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p235_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 235, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-183SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault. (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-183SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead ("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p235_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 235, "text": "TAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a)  If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b)  If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01731", "snippet": "TAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p236_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 236, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1849. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 1 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1849. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p236_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 236, "text": " CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nSocket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, run relay \nK1 is faulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1\n(Para 8-48). 7\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nwhere wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay\nK1 (Para 8-23).", "snippet": " CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p237_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 237, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-185RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-185RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negat"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p237_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 237, "text": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01732", "snippet": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p238_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 238, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1869. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 3 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1869. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nW"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p238_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 238, "text": "ire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB4 is faulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB4 where wire 3 connects? YESNORepair wire 3\n(Para 8-48). 9\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB4 where wire 40 connects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB4(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "ire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty.Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p239_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 239, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-187CIRCUIT BREAKER CB4WIRE 3 WIRE 40VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-187CIRCUIT BREAKER CB4WIRE 3 WIRE 40VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 3 connects. (3) Conne"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p239_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 239, "text": "-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB4 where wire 40 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB4 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01733", "snippet": "-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p240_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 240, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1889. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 40 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1889. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p240_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 240, "text": " Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, blackout \nlight switch or wire 48 are faulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J3-F (wire 40)? YESNORepair wire 40\n(Para 8-48). 11\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J1-4 (wire 48)? YESNOGo to Step 12 of \nthis fault. Go to Step 13 of this fault.", "snippet": " Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty. Wire 48 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p241_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 241, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-189J1-4\nCONNECTOR J1SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3\nCONNECTOR P1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) Lift instrument panel out to remove \nconnector J3 from blackout light switch. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-F (wire 40). (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-189J1-4\nCONNECTOR J1SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-F\nCONNECTOR J3\nCONNECTOR P1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) L"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p241_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 241, "text": " 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (10) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (11) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews to secure instrument panel. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J1-4 (wire 48). (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault.", "snippet": " 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 40 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p241_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 241, "text": "t switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01734", "snippet": "t switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p242_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 242, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1909. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlackout light switch faulty.Wire 48 faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 48 \nis faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 48 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1909. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p242_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 242, "text": " 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 48 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 48 is \nfaulty.12\nIs continuity present between \nconnector J3-L and connector J1-4? YESNORepair wire 48\n(Para 8-49). 13\nIs 24 vdc present at parking \nlight female connector where wire 48 connects? YESNORepair wire 48\n(Para 8-49).Replace blackout \nlight switch \n(Para 8-13).", "snippet": " 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 48 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p243_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 243, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-191SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-L\nCONNECTOR J3J1-4\nCONNECTOR J1\nCONNECTORS\nTO PARKING LIGHTCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) Lift instrument panel out to remove \nconnector J3 from blackout light switch. (3) Set multimeter to ohms. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J3-L (wire 48). (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-4 (wire 48). (a) If continuity is present, replace \nblackout light switch (Para 8-13). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 48 (Para 8-49). (6) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (7) Connect connector J1 to connector P1.(8) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews to secure instrument panel.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-191SCREWBLACKOUT\nLIGHT SWITCH\nINSTRUMENT\nPANELENGINE START\nSWITCH\nJ3-L\nCONNECTOR J3J1-4\nCONNECTOR J1\nCONNECTORS\nTO PARKING LIGHTCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instru"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p243_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 243, "text": "49). (6) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (7) Connect connector J1 to connector P1.(8) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews to secure instrument panel.\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nparking light female connector where \nwire 48 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Turn blackout light switch to SER. DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 14 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 48 (Para 8-49). (7) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "49). (6) Lift instrument panel out to connect \nconnector J3 to blackout light switch. (7) Connect connector J1 to connector P1.(8) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews to secure instrument panel."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p243_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 243, "text": "light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(10) Connect female connector to male \nconnector for parking light. TR01735", "snippet": "light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p244_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 244, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1929. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB4 OK.Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK. Wire 48 OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nSocket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.STE/ICE-R #88\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 2 \nground or brake light socket is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK.Wire 48 OK. Socket(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1929. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p244_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 244, "text": "Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK.Wire 48 OK. Socket(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #88\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector P2 is faulty.14\nIs continuity present between \nparking light socket outside conductor ground and ground \ncable? YESNORepair wire 2\n(Para 8-49). 15\nIs continuity present between \nstarter motor solenoid and connector P2-1? YESNORepair wire 9 or\nconnector P2(Para 8-49).Replace bulb(Para 8-33).", "snippet": "Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB4 OK. Wire 40 OK. Blackout light switch OK.Wire 48 OK. Socket(s) OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p245_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 245, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-193CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORMALE\u001f\nCONNECTOR\nGROUNDFEMALE\u001fCONNECTOR\nWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect ground female connector \nfrom male ground connector. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground outside conductor at parking \nlight socket. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground cable.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-33). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 (Para 8-49). (5) Connect ground female connector to \nground male connector. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-193CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1\nSTARTER SOLENOIDCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORMALE\u001f\nCONNECTOR\nGROUNDFEMALE\u001fCONNECTOR\nWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect ground female connecto"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p245_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 245, "text": "or to \nground male connector. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P2-1. (a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). TR01736", "snippet": "or to \nground male connector. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at starter motor solenoid."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p246_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 246, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1949. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nRun relay OK.Wire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB4 OK.\nWire 40 OK.Blackout light switch OK.\nWire 48 OK.\nSocket(s) OK.Connector P1 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #88\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector J2 are faulty.16\nIs continuity present between \ncircuit breaker CB6 and \nconnector J2?\nYESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector J2(Para 8-48).\nService or replace \nbattery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1949. PARKING LIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBulb(s) OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nRun relay OK.Wire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB4"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p247_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 247, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-195CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. \n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6. \n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J2-1.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42). \n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nrelay wire 9 or connector J2 \n(Para 8-48).\n(4) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.\n(5) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel.\n(6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(7) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01737", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-195CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. \n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) t"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p248_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 248, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1962\n10. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-1962\n10. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMult"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p248_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 248, "text": "Wire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs 24 vdc present at faulty turn \nsignal connector and ground \nfor turn signal?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 3 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "Wire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p249_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 249, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-197FEMALE\u001f\nCONNECTORTURN\u001f\nSIGNAL\nGROUNDMALE\u001fCONNECTOR• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of  battery (Para 8-42). (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfemale connector at faulty turn signal. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground for turn signal. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-197FEMALE\u001f\nCONNECTORTURN\u001f\nSIGNAL\nGROUNDMALE\u001fCONNECTOR• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p249_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 249, "text": "e lead (+) to \nfemale connector at faulty turn signal. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground for turn signal. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 2  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault. (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01721", "snippet": "e lead (+) to \nfemale connector at faulty turn signal. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground for turn signal. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p250_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 250, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-19810. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Relay K4 faulty. Wire 29 faulty.Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty.Wire 26 faulty. Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty.Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, ground \nwire faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-19810. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p250_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 250, "text": "ctor P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, service or \nreplace battery cable.2\nIs continuity present at turn \nsignal outside conductor and \nknown good ground? YESNORepair ground wire \n(Para 8-49). 3\nIs 24 vdc present at starting \nmotor solenoid connector \nwhere battery cable \nconnects? YESNOService or replace \nbattery cable (Para 8-42).Replace bulb \n(Para 8-33).", "snippet": "ctor P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p251_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 251, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-199OUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTORTURN\u001f\nSIGNAL\u001f\nSOCKETGROUND\nBATTERY \u001f\nCABLE\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noutside conductor at faulty turn signal. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nturn signal ground.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-33). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nground wire (Para 8-49). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where battery \ncable connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-199OUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTORTURN\u001f\nSIGNAL\u001f\nSOCKETGROUND\nBATTERY \u001f\nCABLE\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p251_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 251, "text": "42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where battery \ncable connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of  battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nservice battery cable (Para 8-42). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01722", "snippet": "42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where battery \ncable connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p252_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 252, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20010. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at P2-1, \nwire 9 and/or connector P2 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20010. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p252_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 252, "text": "SSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at circuit \nbreaker CB6, wire 9 and/or connector J2 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector P2-1 and known \ngood ground? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector P2 \n(Para 8-49). 5\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects and known good \nground? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector J2 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "SSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p253_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 253, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-201CONNECTOR P2\nP2-1\nCONNECTOR J2\nSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 and/or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-201CONNECTOR P2\nP2-1\nCONNECTOR J2\nSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p253_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 253, "text": "and/or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 and/or connector J2 \n(Para 8-48). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01723", "snippet": "and/or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p254_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 254, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20210. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 connects, circuit breaker CB6 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20210. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty.Relay"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p254_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 254, "text": "or P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at relay K4 \nwhere wire 1 connects, wire 1 faulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects and known good \nground? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6 (Para 8-11). 7\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K4 \nwhere wire 1 connects and \nknown good ground? YESNORepair wire 1 (Para \n8-48).", "snippet": "or P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty.Relay K4 faulty.Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p255_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 255, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-203WIRE 1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6\nRELAY K4WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K4 where wire 1 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-203WIRE 1\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6\nRELAY K4WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Con"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p255_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 255, "text": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K4 where wire 1 connects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). TR01724", "snippet": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K4 where wire 1 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p256_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 256, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20410. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K4 faulty. Wire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty.Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at relay K4 \nwhere wire 29 connects, relay K4 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20410. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K4 fa"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p256_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 256, "text": "onnector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at circuit \nbreaker CB10 where wire 29 connects, wire 29 faulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K4 \nwhere wire 29 connects and \nknown good ground? YESNOReplace relay K4 \n(Para 8-23). 9\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB10 where wire 29 \nconnects and known good \nground? YESNORepair wire 29 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "onnector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 29 faulty. Circuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty.Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p257_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 257, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-205WIRE 29CIRCUIT BREAKER CB10RELAY K4WIRE 29 VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K4 where wire 29 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nrelay K4 (Para 8-23). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-205WIRE 29CIRCUIT BREAKER CB10RELAY K4WIRE 29 VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) C"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p257_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 257, "text": " vdc is not present, replace \nrelay K4 (Para 8-23). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB10 where wire 29 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10  \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 29 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01725", "snippet": " vdc is not present, replace \nrelay K4 (Para 8-23). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p258_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 258, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20610. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 29 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB10 faulty. Wire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at circuit \nbreaker CB10 where wire 24 connects, circuit breaker CB10 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 29 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20610. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 29 OK. POSSI"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p258_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 258, "text": "und OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 29 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty.\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at turn \nsignal flasher where wire 24 connects, wire 24 faulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB10 where wire 24 \nconnects and known good \nground? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB10 (Para 8-11). 11\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal flasher where wire 24 \nconnects and known good \nground? YESNORepair wire 24 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "und OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 29 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 24 faulty. Flasher faulty. Wire 26 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p259_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 259, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-207CIRCUIT BREAKER CB10\nWIRE 24\nTURN SIGNAL\u001f\nFLASHER\nWIRE 24VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB10 where wire 24 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11  \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB10 (Para 8-11). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-207CIRCUIT BREAKER CB10\nWIRE 24\nTURN SIGNAL\u001f\nFLASHER\nWIRE 24VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to v"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p259_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 259, "text": "10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11  \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB10 (Para 8-11). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal flasher where wire 24 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 12  \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair wire \n24 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01726", "snippet": "10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11  \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB10 (Para 8-11). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p260_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 260, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20810. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 29 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK.Wire 24 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFlasher faulty.Wire 26 faulty.Wire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at turn \nsignal flasher where wire 26 or 25 connects, turn signal flasher \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 29 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 24 OK.Turn signal flasher OK.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-20810. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Relay K4 OK. Wire 29 OK. Circu"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p260_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 260, "text": "flasher \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 29 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 24 OK.Turn signal flasher OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty.Wire 26 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 26 or 25 connects, wire 25 or wire 26 \nfaulty.12\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal flasher where wire 26 \nor 25 connect and known \ngood ground? YESNOReplace turn signal \nflasher (Para 8-24). 13\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch wire 26 or 25 \nconnect and known good \nground? YESNORepair wire 25 or \nwire 26 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "flasher \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Relay K4 OK.Wire 29 OK. Circuit breaker CB10 OK. Wire 24 OK.Turn signal flasher OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p261_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 261, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-209TURN SIGNAL\u001f\nFLASHER\nWIRE 25\nWIRE 26VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Disconnect wire 25 or 26 from turn \nsignal flasher. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale blade connector of flasher where wire 25 or wire 26 connect. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn on turn signal for appropriate turn \nsignal wire (right wire 26, left wire 25 [TM 10-3930-673-10]). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13  \nof this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-209TURN SIGNAL\u001f\nFLASHER\nWIRE 25\nWIRE 26VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Disconne"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p261_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 261, "text": "START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn on turn signal for appropriate turn \nsignal wire (right wire 26, left wire 25 [TM 10-3930-673-10]). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13  \nof this fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal flasher (Para 8-24). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (11) Connect wire 25 or 26 to turn signal \nflasher. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Disconnect wire 25 or 26 from turn \nsignal flasher. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfemale blade receptacle of wire 25 or \nwire 26. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn on turn signal for appropriate turn \nsignal wire (right wire 26, left wire 25 [TM 10-3930-673-10]). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13  \nof this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p261_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 261, "text": "lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(7) Turn on turn signal for appropriate turn \nsignal wire (right wire 26, left wire 25 [TM 10-3930-673-10]).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 14  \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair wire \n25 or wire 26 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (10) Connect wire 25 or 26 to turn signal \nflasher.TR01727", "snippet": "lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p262_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 262, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21010. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Relay K4 OK.\nWire 29 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB10 OK.Wire 24 OK.\nTurn signal flasher OK.\nWire 25 OK.Wire 26 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nTurn signal switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at wire 27 \nor wire 28, turn signal switch faulty.14\nIs 24 vdc present at wire 27 or \nwire 28 male blade connector \nand known good ground?\nYESNOReplace turn signal \nswitch (Para 8-12).\nRepair wire 27 or wire 28(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21010. ALL TURN SIGNALS DO  NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Relay K4 OK.\nWire 29 OK.\nCircu"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p263_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 263, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-211WIRE 27WIRE 28VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Disconnect wire 27 or 28 from turn \nsignal switch. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale blade connector of wire 27 or \nwire 28. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn on turn signal for appropriate turn \nsignal wire (right wire 28, left wire 27 [TM 10-3930-673-10]). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 27 \nor wire 28. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-211WIRE 27WIRE 28VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Disconnect wire 27 or 28 from "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p263_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 263, "text": "priate turn \nsignal wire (right wire 28, left wire 27 [TM 10-3930-673-10]). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 27 \nor wire 28. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12).\n(9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (11) Connect wire 27 or 28 to turn signal \nswitch. (12) Install access panel and four screws. (13) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (14) Install battery cover (Para 8-42) .TR01728", "snippet": "priate turn \nsignal wire (right wire 28, left wire 27 [TM 10-3930-673-10]). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 27 \nor wire 28. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p264_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 264, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2122\n11. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2122\n11. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMu"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p264_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 264, "text": "12&P. KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs continuity present between \nbulb center conductor and \noutside conductor ground?START\nYESNOReplace bulb \n(Para 8-34).", "snippet": "12&P. KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p265_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 265, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-213REAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove turn signal bulb from faulty \nturn signal assembly (Para 8-34).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nbulb center conductor.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \noutside conductor ground.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 2  \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-34).\nTR01717", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-213REAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove turn signal bul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p266_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 266, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21411. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty.Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21411. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty.Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p266_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 266, "text": "ontinues. KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 25 connects, wire 25 faulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal flasher where wire 25 connects and known good \nground?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page. YESNO\n3\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 25 \nconnects and known good \nground? YESNORepair wire 25 \n(Para 8-48).Replace turn signal flasher (Para 8-24).", "snippet": "ontinues. KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 25 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p267_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 267, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-215TURN SIGNAL\u001f\nFLASHER\nWIRE 25WIRE 25\nSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws and access panel.(4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal flasher male blade \nconnector where wire 25 connects. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-215TURN SIGNAL\u001f\nFLASHER\nWIRE 25WIRE 25\nSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \n"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p267_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 267, "text": "t multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal flasher male blade \nconnector where wire 25 connects. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (8) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn ON left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal flasher (Para 8-24). (10) Turn OFF left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (12) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal switch where wire 25 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "t multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal flasher male blade \nconnector where wire 25 connects. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p267_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 267, "text": "2). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal switch where wire 25 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Turn ON left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 25 (Para 8-48). (7) Turn OFF left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01718", "snippet": "2). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal switch where wire 25 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p268_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 268, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21611. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. Wire 25 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nTurn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 27 connects, turn signal switch \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK.Wire 25 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 27 \nconnects and known good \nground?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21611. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. Wire 25 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nTurn signal switch faulty. Wire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Co"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p268_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 268, "text": "EASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 27 \nconnects and known good \nground?\nYESNOReplace turn signal \nswitch (Para 8-12). 5\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal socket center \nconductor? YESNOGo to Step 7 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "EASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 27 \nconnects and known good \nground?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p269_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 269, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-217REAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKETFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKET\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORWIRE 27VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal switch male blade connector \nwhere wire 27 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn ON left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-217REAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKETFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKET\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORWIRE 27VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (P"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p269_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 269, "text": "E \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn ON left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12).\n(8) Turn OFF left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal socket center conductor. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Turn ON left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (7) Turn OFF left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "E \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn ON left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p269_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 269, "text": " turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (7) Turn OFF left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01719", "snippet": " turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (7) Turn OFF left turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p270_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 270, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21811. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. Wire 25 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 27 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J1 or wire 27 (Para 8-48). KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. Wire 25 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 27 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 27 (Para 8-49).6\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal switch wire 27 and \nconnector J1-9? YESNORepair wire 27 or \nconnector J1 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-21811. LEFT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nRight turn signal OK. Wire 25 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 27 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connec"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p270_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 270, "text": "ntinuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 27 (Para 8-49).6\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal switch wire 27 and \nconnector J1-9? YESNORepair wire 27 or \nconnector J1 \n(Para 8-48).\n7\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal socket center \nconductor and \nconnector P1-9? YESNORepair wire 27 or \nconnector P1 (Para 8-49). Replace bulb \n(Para 8-33).", "snippet": "ntinuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 27 (Para 8-49).6\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal switch wire 27 and \nconnector J1-9? YESNORepair wire 27 or \nconnector J1 \n(Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p271_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 271, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-219REAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULBCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR \u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDJ1-9P1-9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal switch wire 27. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-9.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 7  \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J1 or wire 27 (Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-219REAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULBCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR \u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDJ1-9P1-9CONTINUIT"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p271_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 271, "text": "Step 7  \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J1 or wire 27 (Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal socket center conductor. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-9.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-33). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 27 \n(Para 8-49). (5) Connect connector J1 to connector P1. (6) Install four screws to secure access \npanel. (7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42) . (8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42). TR01720", "snippet": "Step 7  \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J1 or wire 27 (Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p272_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 272, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2202\n12. RIGHT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 26 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 28 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2202\n12. RIGHT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nM"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p272_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 272, "text": "-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 26 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 28 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs continuity present between \nbulb center conductor and \noutside conductor ground?START\nYESNOReplace bulb \n(Para 8-33).", "snippet": "-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 26 faulty. Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 28 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p273_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 273, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-221FRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORREAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove turn signal bulb from faulty \nturn signal assembly (Para 8-33).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nbulb center conductor.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \noutside conductor ground.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 2  \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-33).\nTR01713", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-221FRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORREAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULB\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove turn signal bul"}
