{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p274_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 274, "text": "continues. KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 26 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 28 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 26 connects, wire 26 faulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal flasher where wire 26 connects and known good \nground?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page. YESNO\n3\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 26 \nconnects and known good \nground? YESNORepair wire 26 \n(Para 8-48).Replace turn signal flasher (Para 8-24).", "snippet": "continues. KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 26 faulty.Turn signal switch faulty. Wire 28 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
