{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p276_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 276, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-22412. RIGHT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. Wire 26 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nTurn signal switch faulty. Wire 28 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 28 connects, turn signal switch \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK.Wire 26 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 28 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 28 \nconnects and known good \nground?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-22412. RIGHT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. Wire 26 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nTurn signal switch faulty. Wire 28 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Co"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p276_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 276, "text": "EASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 28 \nconnects and known good \nground?\nYESNOReplace turn signal \nswitch (Para 8-12). 5\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal socket center \nconductor? YESNOGo to Step 6 of this \nfault. Replace bulb (Para 8-33).", "snippet": "EASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs 24 vdc present at turn \nsignal switch where wire 28 \nconnects and known good \nground?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p277_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 277, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-225FRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKETREAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKET\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORWIRE 28VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal switch male blade connector where wire 28 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Turn ON right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12). (7) Turn OFF right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-225FRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKETREAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL SOCKET\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORWIRE 28VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p277_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 277, "text": "is fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12). (7) Turn OFF right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal socket center conductor. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Turn ON right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, replace bulb \n(Para 8-33). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (7) Turn OFF right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "is fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nturn signal switch (Para 8-12). (7) Turn OFF right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p277_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 277, "text": "ce bulb \n(Para 8-33). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (7) Turn OFF right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01715", "snippet": "ce bulb \n(Para 8-33). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (7) Turn OFF right turn signal \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p278_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 278, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-22612. RIGHT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. Wire 26 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 28 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J1 or wire 28 (Para 8-48). KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. Wire 26 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 28 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 28 (Para 8-49).6\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal switch wire 28 and \nconnector J1-26? YESNORepair wire 28 \nor connector J1 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-22612. RIGHT TURN SIGNAL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLeft turn signal OK. Wire 26 OK. Turn signal switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 28 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connec"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p278_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 278, "text": "tinuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 28 (Para 8-49).6\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal switch wire 28 and \nconnector J1-26? YESNORepair wire 28 \nor connector J1 \n(Para 8-48).\n7\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal socket center \nconductor and \nconnector P1-26? YESNORepair wire 28 or \nconnector P1 (Para 8-49). Replace bulb \n(Para 8-33).", "snippet": "tinuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 28 (Para 8-49).6\nIs continuity present between \nturn signal switch wire 28 and \nconnector J1-26? YESNORepair wire 28 \nor connector J1 \n(Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p279_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 279, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-227CENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDJ1-26 P1-26\nREAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULBFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULBCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal switch wire 28. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-26.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 7  \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector J1 or wire 28 \n(Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal socket center conductor. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-26.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-227CENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTORCONNECTOR J1CONNECTOR P1\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\u001f\nGROUNDJ1-26 P1-26\nREAR TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULBFRONT TURN\u001f\nSIGNAL BULBCONTINU"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p279_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 279, "text": "\n(Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal socket center conductor. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-26.\n(a) If continuity is present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-33). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nconnector P1 or wire 28 (Para 8-49). (4) Connect connector J1 to connector P1.(5) Install four screws to secure access \npanel. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Install battery cover (Para 8-42). TR01716", "snippet": "\n(Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nturn signal socket center conductor. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-26."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p280_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 280, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2282\n13. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2282\n13. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMulti"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p280_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 280, "text": "faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs 24 vdc present at starting \nmotor solenoid connector \nwhere battery cable connects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 2 of this \nfault. Go to Step 3 of this fault.", "snippet": "faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p281_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 281, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-229NEGATIVE \u001f\nBATTERY \u001f\nCABLE\nBATTERY\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-229NEGATIVE \u001f\nBATTERY \u001f\nCABLE\nBATTERY\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p281_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 281, "text": "(Para 8-44). (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 2 of this fault. (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). TR01075", "snippet": "(Para 8-44). (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p282_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 282, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23013. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nnegative battery cable faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23013. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p282_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 282, "text": " faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present at P2-1, \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49) faulty.2\nIs continuity present on \nnegative battery cable? YESNORepair negative \nbattery cable (Para 8-44). 3\nIs 24 volts dc present at \nconnector P2 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector  P2(Para 8-49).Service or replace \nbattery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": " faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p283_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 283, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-231NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLECOVER\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nend of negative battery cable. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother end of negative battery cable.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nnegative battery cable (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-231NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLECOVER\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-4"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p283_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 283, "text": "\nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects.\n(5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (3) (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (7) Connect connector J2 to connector P2. TR01076", "snippet": "\nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p284_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 284, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23213. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 \nfaulty or connector J2 (Para 8-48). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23213. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p284_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 284, "text": "OBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector J2 \n(Para 8-48). 5\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6 (Para 8-11).", "snippet": "OBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p285_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 285, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-233SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9 WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Remove four screws and access panel. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 connects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-233SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9 WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Remove four screws and ac"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p285_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 285, "text": "vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). TR01077", "snippet": "vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p286_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 286, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23413. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 1 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23413. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run Relay"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p286_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 286, "text": "uit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, run relay \nK1 faulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1 (Para \n8-48). 7\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay \n(Para 8-23).", "snippet": "uit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun Relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p287_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 287, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-235RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknow good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-235RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negat"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p287_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 287, "text": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-39390-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01078", "snippet": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p288_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 288, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23613. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run Relay K1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 3 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run Relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, relay K2 \nfaulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 3 connects?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23613. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run Relay K1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLE"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p288_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 288, "text": "uit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, relay K2 \nfaulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 3 connects?\nYESNORepair wire 3 (Para \n8-48). 9\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 5 connects? YESNOReplace relay K2 \n(Para 8-23).", "snippet": "uit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, relay K2 \nfaulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 3 connects?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p289_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 289, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-237RELAY K2WIRE 5WIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-237RELAY K2WIRE 5WIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative l"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p289_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 289, "text": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nrelay K2 (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01079", "snippet": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p290_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 290, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23813. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run Relay K1 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 5 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run Relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 5 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB7 faulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB7 where wire 5 \nconnects?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-23813. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run Relay K1 OK. Wire 3 OK. Rela"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p290_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 290, "text": "Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB7 faulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB7 where wire 5 \nconnects?\nYESNORepair wire 5 (Para \n8-48). 11\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB7 where wire 70 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB7 (Para 8-11).", "snippet": "Wire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB7 faulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB7 where wire 5 \nconnects?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p291_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 291, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-239CIRCUIT BREAKER CB7WIRE 70\nWIRE 5VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB7 where wire 5 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 5 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-239CIRCUIT BREAKER CB7WIRE 70\nWIRE 5VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB7 where wire 5 connects. (3) Conne"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p291_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 291, "text": " 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 5 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB7 where wire 70 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 12 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB7 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01080", "snippet": " 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 5 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p292_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 292, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-24013. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run Relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nRelay K2 OK.Wire 5 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB7 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 70 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, male or \nfemale connector for wire 70 faulty.12\nIs 24 vdc present at male \nconnector for wire 70?\nYESNORepair wire 70 and/\nor male connector \nfor wire 70 \n(Para 8-48).\nRepair wire 70 and/or female connector for \nwire 70 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-24013. ALL FLOODLIGHTS DO NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run Relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nRela"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p293_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 293, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-241SCREW\nMALE\u001f\nCONNECTOR\u001fWIRE 70FEMALE\u001fCONNECTOR\u001fWIRE 70ACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale connector for wire 70. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative batter cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 70 \nand/or female connector for \nwire 70 (Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 70 and/or male connector for wire 70 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel. (8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-241SCREW\nMALE\u001f\nCONNECTOR\u001fWIRE 70FEMALE\u001fCONNECTOR\u001fWIRE 70ACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale connector for"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p293_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 293, "text": "tor for wire 70 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel. (8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01081", "snippet": "tor for wire 70 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel. (8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p294_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 294, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2422\n14. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORW ARD) DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2422\n14. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORW ARD) DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, A"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p294_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 294, "text": ". Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs continuity present on one \nor both floodlight bulbs?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-31).", "snippet": ". Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p295_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 295, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-243MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORSBULB• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock.\n• Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries.\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale connector of bulb.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother male connector of bulb.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 2 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nfaulty bulb (Para 8-31).\nTR01561", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-243MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORSBULB• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or sh"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p296_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 296, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-24414. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty.\nRun relay K1 faulty.\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.\nWire 5 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.\nFront floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, light \nconnection and/or ground faulty.2\nIs continuity present between \nground of light connection \nand known good ground?\nYESNORepair connection \nand/or light ground \nwire.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-24414. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit br"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p297_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 297, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-245LIGHT\u001f\nCONNECTION\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground of light connection.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nlight connection and/or light ground wire.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-245LIGHT\u001f\nCONNECTION\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground of light connec"}
