{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p299_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 299, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-247VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 connects.\n(5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. \n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault.\nTR01563\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-247VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p300_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 300, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-24814. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nnegative battery cable is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-24814. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p300_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 300, "text": "or P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.\nFront floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 or \nconnector P2 is faulty.5\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector P2 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector P2  \n(Para 8-49).4\nIs continuity present on \nnegative battery cable? YESNORepair negative \nbattery cable \n(Para 8-44). Service or replace battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "or P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p301_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 301, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-249CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nend of negative battery cable. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother end of negative battery cable.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42). (b) If continuity is not present, replace \nnegative battery cable (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-249CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nend "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p301_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 301, "text": "2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (7) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.TR01564NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLECOVER\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1", "snippet": "2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p302_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 302, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25014. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 or \nconnector J2 are faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25014. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 fa"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p302_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 302, "text": "ty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 is faulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector J2(Para 8-48). 7\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6 \n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "ty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p303_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 303, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-251VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair wire \n9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-251VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p303_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 303, "text": "). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01565SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6", "snippet": "). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p304_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 304, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25214. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 1 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25214. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p304_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 304, "text": "POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, run relay \nK1 faulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1 \n(Para 8-48). 9\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay \nK1 (Para 8-23).", "snippet": "POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p305_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 305, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-253VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-253VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknow"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p305_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 305, "text": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay K1 (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01566RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1", "snippet": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p306_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 306, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25414. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 3 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25414. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p306_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 306, "text": "ire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, relay K2 is \nfaulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 3 connects? YESNORepair wire 3\n(Para 8-48). 11\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 5 connects? YESNOReplace relay K2 \n(Para 8-23).", "snippet": "ire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p307_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 307, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-255VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-255VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown go"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p307_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 307, "text": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 12 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nrelay K2 (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01567RELAY K2WIRE 5WIRE 3", "snippet": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects."}
