{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p310_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 310, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25814. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK.Wire 5 OK. Circuit breaker CB7 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 70 faulty. Front floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 70 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Circuit breaker CB7 OK. Wire 70 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFront floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-25814. FRONT FLOODLIGHT (OR FORWAR D) DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p310_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 310, "text": "aker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Circuit breaker CB7 OK. Wire 70 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFront floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, front \nfloodlight switch is faulty.14\nIs 24 vdc present at front \nfloodlight switch where wire \n70 connects? YESNORepair wire 70\n(Para 8-48). 15\nIs 24 vdc present at front \nfloodlight switch where wire \n72 connects? YESNOReplace front \nfloodlight switch \n(Para 8-7). Repair wire 72\n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "aker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 5 OK.Circuit breaker CB7 OK. Wire 70 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFront floodlight switch faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p311_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 311, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-259VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Remove four screws and instrument \npanel. (3) Lift instrument panel out to get to male \nconnector at floodlight switch. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale connector for wire 70. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 15 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 70 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-259VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Remove four screws and instrument \npanel. (3) Lift instrument panel out to get to male \nconnector at floodlight switch. (4) Co"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p311_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 311, "text": "24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 70 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Lift instrument panel out to get to front \nfloodlight switch where wire 72 connects to front floodlight switch. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfront floodlight switch where wire 72 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 72 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nfloodlight switch (Para 8-7). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews to secure instrument panel.", "snippet": "24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 70 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p311_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 311, "text": " vdc is not present, replace \nfloodlight switch (Para 8-7). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews to secure instrument panel.\n(9) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).SCREW\nWIRE 70\nWIRE 72FRONT\u001f\nFLOODLIGHT\u001fSWITCHENGINE\u001f\nSTART\u001f\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\u001f\nPANELFRONT\u001fFLOODLIGHT\u001fSWITCH", "snippet": " vdc is not present, replace \nfloodlight switch (Para 8-7). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews to secure instrument panel."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p312_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 312, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2602\n15. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Boom floodlight switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2602\n15. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMult"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p312_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 312, "text": "n relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Boom floodlight switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty.\nConnector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs continuity present on boom \nfloodlight bulb?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-31).", "snippet": "n relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Boom floodlight switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p313_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 313, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-261MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORSBULB• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock.\n• Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries.\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from boom floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale connector of bulb.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother male connector of bulb.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 2 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nfaulty bulb (Para 8-31).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-261MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORSBULB• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or sh"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p314_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 314, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26215. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty.\nRun relay K1 faulty.\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.\nWire 5 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.\nBoom floodlight switch faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nConnector J4 faulty.\nConnector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is no present, light \nconnection and/or ground faulty.2\nIs continuity present between \nground of light connection \nand known good ground?\nYESNORepair connection \nand/or light ground \nwire.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26215. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 fau"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p315_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 315, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-263LIGHT\u001f\nCONNECTION\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from boom floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground of light connection.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nlight connection and/or light ground \nwire.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-263LIGHT\u001f\nCONNECTION\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from boom floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground of light connecti"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p316_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 316, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26415. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty.\nRun relay K1 faulty.\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.\nWire 5 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.\nBoom floodlight switch faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nConnector J4 faulty.\nConnector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs 24 vdc present at starting \nmotor solenoid where battery cable connects?\nYESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault.\nGo to Step 5 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26415. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 fau"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p317_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 317, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-265STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects.\n(5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5  of \nthis fault. \n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault.\n(7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nTR01576", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-265STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(3) Set multimeter t"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p318_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 318, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26615. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty. Boom floodlight switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nnegative battery cable is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26615. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNone. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 fau"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p318_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 318, "text": "is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.\nWire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Boom floodlight switch faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty.Connector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 or \nconnector P2 are faulty.4\nIs continuity present on \nnegative battery cable? YESNORepair negative \nbattery cable\n(Para 8-42). 5\nIs 24 volts dc present at \nconnector P2 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector P2 \n(Para 8-49).Service or replace battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p319_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 319, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-267NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLECOVER\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nend of negative battery cable. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother end of negative battery cable. (a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nnegative battery cable (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-267NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLECOVER\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of (Para 8-42). (2) "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p319_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 319, "text": "\nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects.\n(5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (8) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.TR01577", "snippet": "\nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p320_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 320, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26815. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Boom floodlight switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 or \nconnector J2 are faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-26815. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 f"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p320_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 320, "text": ". Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.\nBoom floodlight switch faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty.Connector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 is faulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector J2\n(Para 8-48). 7\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6\n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": ". Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p321_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 321, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-269SCREWPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Remove four screws and access panel. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-269SCREWPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Remove four screws and access pan"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p321_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 321, "text": "(b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-44).TR01578", "snippet": "(b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p322_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 322, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-27015. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Boom floodlight switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 1 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-27015. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run re"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p322_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 322, "text": "or P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.\nBoom floodlight switch faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty.Connector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, run relay \nK1 is faulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1\n(Para 8-48). 9\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay \nK1 (Para 8-23).", "snippet": "or P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p323_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 323, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-271RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9  of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-271RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter posi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p323_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 323, "text": "ara 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10  \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay K1 (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01579", "snippet": "ara 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
