{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p333_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 333, "text": ". (8) Turn boom floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 17 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 71 or connector J1 (Para 8-48).\n(9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01584", "snippet": ". (8) Turn boom floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 17 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 71 or connector J1 (Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p334_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 334, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-28215. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nRelay K2 OK.Wire 5 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB7 OK.\nWire 70 OK.Boom floodlight switch OK.\nConnector J1 OK.\nConnector P1 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J4 faulty.\nConnector P4 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 71 or \nconnector J4 are faulty.17\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector J4-W where wire 71 \nconnects?\nYESNORepair wire 71 or \nconnector J4\n(Para 8-50).\nRepair wire 71 or \nconnector P4(Para 8-50).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-28215. BOOM FLOODLIGHT DO ES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nR"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p335_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 335, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-283CONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR P4J4-W VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Disconnect connector J4 from \nconnector P4. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J4-W where wire 71 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn boom floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 71 \nor P4 connector (Para 8-50). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 71 or connector J4 (Para 8-50).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-283CONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR P4J4-W VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Disconnect con"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p335_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 335, "text": " floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 71 \nor P4 connector (Para 8-50). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 71 or connector J4 (Para 8-50).\n(9) Turn boom floodlight switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (12) Connect connector J4 to connector P4.(13) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (14) Install battery cover (Para 8-42). TR01585", "snippet": " floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 71 \nor P4 connector (Para 8-50). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 71 or connector J4 (Para 8-50)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p336_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 336, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2842\n16. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-2842\n16. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMult"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p336_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 336, "text": "Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs continuity present on faulty \nfloodlight?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-31).", "snippet": "Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #88."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p337_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 337, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-285MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORS\nBULB• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock.\n• Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries.\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nmale connector of bulb.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother male connector of bulb.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 2 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nfaulty bulb (Para 8-31).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-285MALE\u001f\nCONNECTORS\nBULB• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or s"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p338_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 338, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-28616. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty.\nRun relay K1 faulty.\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.\nWire 5 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.\nRear floodlight switch faulty.\nWire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #88.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, light \nconnection and/or ground faulty.2\nIs continuity present between \nground of light connection \nand known good ground?\nYESNORepair connection \nand/or light ground \nwire.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-28616. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 fault"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p339_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 339, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-287LIGHT\u001f\nCONNECTION\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground of light connection.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nlight connection and/or light ground \nwire.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-287LIGHT\u001f\nCONNECTION\nGROUNDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty floodlight.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nground of light connec"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p340_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 340, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-28816. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty.\nRun relay K1 faulty.\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.\nWire 5 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty.\nRear floodlight switch faulty.\nWire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs 24 vdc present at starting \nmotor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects?\nYESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault.\nGo to Step 5 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-28816. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty.\nWire 9 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB6 fault"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p341_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 341, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-289STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover.\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarting motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects.\n(5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault.\nTR01568", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-289STARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover.\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(3) Set multimeter to volts dc.("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p342_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 342, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29016. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty.Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test. STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nnegative battery cable is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29016. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nGround faulty. Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wir"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p342_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 342, "text": "or P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.\nRear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 or \nconnector P2 is faulty.4\nIs continuity present on \nnegative battery cable? YESNORepair negative \nbattery cable(Para 8-44). 5\nIs 24 vdc present at \nconnector P2 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector P2 \n(Para 8-49)Service or replace \nbattery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "or P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p343_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 343, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-291NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLECOVER\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nend of negative battery cable. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nother end of negative battery cable.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nnegative battery cable (Para 8-44). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-291NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLECOVER\nBATTERY\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-4"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p343_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 343, "text": "J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Connect connector J2 to connector P2. TR01569", "snippet": "J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P2-1 where wire 9 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p344_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 344, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29216. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 or \nconnector J2 is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29216. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 fa"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p344_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 344, "text": ". Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.\nRear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 is faulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNO\n7\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6\n(Para 8-11).Repair wire 9 or connector J2(Para 8-48).", "snippet": ". Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p345_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 345, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-293SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-293SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead ("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p345_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 345, "text": "). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01570", "snippet": "). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p346_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 346, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29416. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 1 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29416. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run rel"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p346_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 346, "text": "EMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, run relay \nK1 is faulty.8\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1\n(Para 8-48). 9\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nK1 where wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay \nK1 (Para 8-23).", "snippet": "EMS\nRun relay K1 faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Relay K2 faulty. Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p347_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 347, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-295RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 9 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-295RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negat"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p347_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 347, "text": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay K1 (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01571", "snippet": "r positive lead (+) to \nrun relay K1 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p348_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 348, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29616. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Relay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 3 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29616. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK. POSSIBLE PROB"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p348_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 348, "text": "relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, relay K2 is \nfaulty.10\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 3 connects? YESNORepair wire 3\n(Para 8-48). 11\nIs 24 vdc present at relay K2 \nwhere wire 5 connects? YESNOReplace relay K2\n(Para 8-23).", "snippet": "relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRelay K2 faulty.Wire 5 faulty.Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p349_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 349, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-297RELAY K2WIRE 5WIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 11 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-297RELAY K2WIRE 5WIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative l"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p349_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 349, "text": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 12 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nrelay K2 (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01572", "snippet": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrelay K2 where wire 5 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p350_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 350, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29816. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK. Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 5 faulty. Circuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty.Rear floodlight switch faulty. Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 5 is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 5 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-29816. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGround OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK. Wire 3 OK. Re"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p350_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 350, "text": ". Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 5 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB7 is faulty.12\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB7 where wire 5 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 5\n(Para 8-48). 13\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB7 where wire 70 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB7\n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": ". Run relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK. Relay K2 OK. Wire 5 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB7 faulty. Wire 70 faulty. Rear floodlight switch faulty.Wire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p351_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 351, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-299CIRCUIT BREAKER CB7WIRE 70\nWIRE 5SCREWACCESS \u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB7 where wire 5 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 5 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-299CIRCUIT BREAKER CB7WIRE 70\nWIRE 5SCREWACCESS \u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB7 where wire 5 "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p351_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 351, "text": " 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 5 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB7 where wire 70 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 14 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB7 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (8) Install access panel and four screws to \nsecure access panel.TR01573", "snippet": " 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 5 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p352_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 352, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30016. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nRelay K2 OK.Wire 5 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB7 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 70 faulty.\nRear floodlight switch faulty.\nWire 72 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 70 is \nfaulty.14\nIs 24 vdc present at rear \nfloodlight switch where wire \n70 connects?\nYESNORepair wire 70\n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30016. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nRe"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p353_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 353, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-301SCREW\nWIRE 70\nREAR\nFLOODLIGHTSWITCHENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\nPANELREARFLOODLIGHTSWITCH\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (3) Lift instrument panel out to get to rear \nfloodlight switch where wire 70 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrear floodlight switch where wire 70 connects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 15 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 70 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-301SCREW\nWIRE 70\nREAR\nFLOODLIGHTSWITCHENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\nPANELREARFLOODLIGHTSWITCH\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Remove four screws from instrument "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p353_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 353, "text": "urn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 15 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 70 (Para 8-48).\n(8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01574", "snippet": "urn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 15 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 70 (Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p354_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 354, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30216. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nRelay K2 OK.Wire 5 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB7 OK.\nWire 70 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRear floodlight switch faulty.\nWire 73 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, rear \nfloodlight switch is faulty.15\nIs 24 vdc present at rear \nfloodlight switch where wire \n73 connects?\nYESNOReplace rear \nfloodlight switch \n(Para 8-7).\nRepair wire 73\n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30216. REAR FLOODLIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGround OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Wire 9 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.Run relay K1 OK.\nWire 3 OK.\nRe"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p355_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 355, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-303SCREW\nWIRE 73REAR\u001f\nFLOODLIGHT\u001fSWITCHENGINE\u001f\nSTART\u001f\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\u001f\nPANELREAR\u001fFLOODLIGHT\u001fSWITCH\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Lift instrument panel out to get to rear \nfloodlight switch where wire 73 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrear floodlight switch where wire 73 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn rear floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 73 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nrear floodlight switch (Para 8-7).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-303SCREW\nWIRE 73REAR\u001f\nFLOODLIGHT\u001fSWITCHENGINE\u001f\nSTART\u001f\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\u001f\nPANELREAR\u001fFLOODLIGHT\u001fSWITCH\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Lift instrument panel out to "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p355_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 355, "text": "0). (7) Turn rear floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 73 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nrear floodlight switch (Para 8-7).\n(8) Turn rear floodlight switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Install four screws to secure instrument \npanel. (11) Install battery cover (Para 8-42). TR01575", "snippet": "0). (7) Turn rear floodlight switch to ON \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 73 \n(Para 8-48). (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \nrear floodlight switch (Para 8-7)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p356_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 356, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-3042\n17. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb(s) faulty.Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty.Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-3042\n17. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p356_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 356, "text": ". Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty.Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #88. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, replace \nbulb(s).1\nIs continuity present on faulty \nblackout taillight or marker \nlight bulb?START\nYESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-33).", "snippet": ". Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty.Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p357_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 357, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-305BLACKOUT\u001f\nTAILLIGHTBLACKOUT\u001fMARKER\u001fLIGHT\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTORCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty blackout \ntaillight or marker light (Para 8-33).\n(2) Set the multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nthe center conductor.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–)to \nthe outside conductor.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 2 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-33).\nTR01695", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-305BLACKOUT\u001f\nTAILLIGHTBLACKOUT\u001fMARKER\u001fLIGHT\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTORCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove bulb from faulty blackout \ntaillight or marker light (Para 8-33).\n(2) S"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p358_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 358, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30617. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30617. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p358_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 358, "text": "g continues. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty.Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, service or \nreplace battery cable.2\nIs 24 vdc present at faulty \nblackout taillight or marker light socket?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page. YESNO\n3\nIs 24 vdc present at the \nstarter motor solenoid where \nwire 9 connects? YESNOService or replace \nbattery cable (Para 8-42).Go to Step 3 of this fault. Go to Step 14 of this fault.", "snippet": "g continues. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p359_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 359, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-307CENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of faulty socket. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn blackout light switch to \nBLACKOUT DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-307CENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p359_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 359, "text": "ad (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn blackout light switch to \nBLACKOUT DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(6) Depress brake pedal \n(TM  10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 14 \nof this fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 3 of this fault. (7) Turn blackout light switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery covers (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nthe starter motor solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault.", "snippet": "ad (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn blackout light switch to \nBLACKOUT DRIVE position (TM 10-3930-673-10). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p359_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 359, "text": "ects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, service or \nreplace battery cable (Para 8-42). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01696", "snippet": "ects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p360_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 360, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30817. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulbs OK. Turn signals OK. Floodlights OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty. Wire 9 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-30817. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nBulbs OK. Turn signals OK. Floodlights OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty. Connector "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p360_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 360, "text": "ubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty.Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 faulty.4\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects? YESNOGo to Step 15 of \nthis fault. 5\nIs 24 vdc present at circuit \nbreaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6 \n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "ubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p361_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 361, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-309SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB6 where wire 9 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault. (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-309SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nWIRE 1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws and access panel. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead ("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p361_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 361, "text": "TAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01697", "snippet": "TAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect the multimeter positive lead \n(+) to circuit breaker CB6 where wire 1 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \na known good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p362_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 362, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-31017. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 1 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-31017. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circui"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p362_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 362, "text": "OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.\nBlackout light switch faulty.Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, run relay \nfaulty.6\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nwhere wire 1 connects? YESNORepair wire 1 (Para \n8-48). 7\nIs 24 vdc present at run relay \nwhere wire 3 connects? YESNOReplace run relay \n(Para 8-23).", "snippet": "OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p363_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 363, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-311RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nthe run relay where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-311RELAY K1\nWIRE 3WIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nrun relay where wire 1 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p363_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 363, "text": " positive lead (+) to \nthe run relay where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 8 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01698", "snippet": " positive lead (+) to \nthe run relay where wire 3 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p364_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 364, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-31217. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty.Blackout light switch faulty. Wire 45 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Socket(s) faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 24 vdc is not present, wire 3 \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB4 faulty. Wire 40 faulty. Blackout light switch faulty.Wire 45 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-31217. BLACKOUT MARKER LIGHT(S) AND/OR TAILLIGHT(S) DO NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nTurn signals OK. Floodlights OK. Bulbs OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Wire 9 OK.Circui"}
