{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p421_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 421, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-369CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 at circuit breaker CB6.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J2-1 (4).(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 18 of this fault  \n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48).\n(5) Install access panel and four screws.\n(6) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01653", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-369CONNECTOR J2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1WIRE 9\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p422_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 422, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-3702\n20. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Parking brake switch faulty.Wire 23 faulty. Wire 2 faulty. Resistor faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-3702\n20. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, A"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p422_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 422, "text": "rking brake ON. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Parking brake switch faulty.Wire 23 faulty. Wire 2 faulty. Resistor faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs 12 vdc present at parking \nbrake indicator light socket?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 7 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "rking brake ON. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Parking brake switch faulty.Wire 23 faulty. Wire 2 faulty. Resistor faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p423_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 423, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-371PARKING BRAKE\nINDICATOR\nCENTER\nCONDUCTOR• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove lens/bulb from parking brake \nindicator. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of parking brake indicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-371PARKING BRAKE\nINDICATOR\nCENTER\nCONDUCTOR• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p423_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 423, "text": "round. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of parking brake indicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If 12 vdc is present, go to Step 2 of \nthis fault. (b) If 12 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). TR01620", "snippet": "round. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of parking brake indicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p424_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 424, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37220. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LI GHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty. Parking brake switch faulty. Wire 23 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, replace \nbulb. KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. 12 vdc present at socket. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nParking brake switch faulty. Wire 23 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question determines where \ntroubleshooting continues.2\nIs continuity present across \nparking brake lens/bulb? YESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-9).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37220. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LI GHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty. Parking brake switch faulty. Wi"}
