{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p425_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 425, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-373PARKING BRAKE\u001f\nINDICATOR\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\nBULB GROUNDCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of bulb.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nbulb ground.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nlens/bulb (Para 8-9).\nCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Turn parking brake switch ON.(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noutside conductor of parking brake \nindicator.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nlens/bulb (Para 8-9).\n(b) If continuity is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault.\nTR01621", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-373PARKING BRAKE\u001f\nINDICATOR\nOUTSIDE\u001f\nCONDUCTORCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR\nBULB GROUNDCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conduc"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p426_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 426, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37420. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LI GHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gage lights work. 12 vdc present at socket.Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nParking brake switch faulty.Wire 23 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, parking \nbrake switch is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gages work. 12 vdc present at socket. Bulb OK.Parking brake switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 23 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present across \nwire, wire is faulty.4\nIs continuity present across \nparking brake switch while \nparking brake switch is \nturned ON? YESNOReplace parking \nbrake switch (Para 8-7).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37420. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LI GHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gage lights work. 12 vdc present at socket.Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nParking br"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p426_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 426, "text": "If continuity is not present across \nwire, wire is faulty.4\nIs continuity present across \nparking brake switch while \nparking brake switch is \nturned ON? YESNOReplace parking \nbrake switch (Para 8-7).\n5\nIs continuity present across \nwire 23? YESNOReplace or repair \nwire 23 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "If continuity is not present across \nwire, wire is faulty.4\nIs continuity present across \nparking brake switch while \nparking brake switch is \nturned ON? YESNOReplace parking \nbrake switch (Para 8-7)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p427_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 427, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-375PARKING\u001f\nBRAKE\u001fLIGHT\u001fSOCKETWIRE 10\nSCREW\nPANELPANELSCREW\nPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nSWITCHPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nINDICATORWIRE 23\nWIRE 2WIRE 23CONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Remove four screws and panel. (2) Turn parking brake switch ON. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 23 at parking brake switch \nterminal. (4) Connect multimeter negative (–) lead to \nwire 2 at parking brake switch terminal.(a) If continuity is not present, replace \nparking brake switch (Para 8-7). (b) If continuity is present, go to Step 5  \nof this fault. CONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Remove four screws and panel. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 23 at parking brake indicator \nterminal. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nwire 23 at parking brake light switch terminal.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-375PARKING\u001f\nBRAKE\u001fLIGHT\u001fSOCKETWIRE 10\nSCREW\nPANELPANELSCREW\nPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nSWITCHPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nINDICATORWIRE 23\nWIRE 2WIRE 23CONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Remove four screws and panel. ("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p427_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 427, "text": "crews and panel. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 23 at parking brake indicator \nterminal. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nwire 23 at parking brake light switch terminal.\n(a) If continuity is not present, replace \nwire 23 (Para 8-48). (b) If continuity is present, go to Step 6 \nof this fault. TR01622", "snippet": "crews and panel. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 23 at parking brake indicator \nterminal. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nwire 23 at parking brake light switch terminal."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p428_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 428, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37620. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LI GHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gages work. 12 vdc present at socket.Bulb OK. Parking brake switch OK. Wire 23 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gages work. 12 vdc not measured at socket. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nResistor faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 1500 ohms are not measured, \nresistor is faulty.6\nIs continuity present between \nwire 2 at parking brake switch \nand known good ground? YESNOReplace or \nrepair wire 2 (Para 8-48). 7\nAre 1500 ohms present \nacross resistor?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-37620. PARKING BRAKE INDICATOR LI GHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nParking brake ON. Other gages work. 12 vdc present at socket.Bulb OK. Parking brake switch OK. Wire 23 O"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p428_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 428, "text": "sured, \nresistor is faulty.6\nIs continuity present between \nwire 2 at parking brake switch \nand known good ground? YESNOReplace or \nrepair wire 2 (Para 8-48). 7\nAre 1500 ohms present \nacross resistor?\nYESNOReplace resistor \n(Para 8-9).Repeat Step 3 through Step 6 of this fault. Repair or replace \nwire 10 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "sured, \nresistor is faulty.6\nIs continuity present between \nwire 2 at parking brake switch \nand known good ground? YESNOReplace or \nrepair wire 2 (Para 8-48). 7\nAre 1500 ohms present \nacross resistor?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p429_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 429, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-377PARKING BRAKE\u001f\nLIGHT SOCKET\nWIRE 10RESISTORCOVER\nTO CIRCUIT\u001fBREAKER CB-1\nSCREW\nPANELPANELSCREW\nPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nSWITCHPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nINDICATORWIRE 23\nWIRE 2WIRE 23CONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 2 at parking brake switch terminal. (2) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (a) If continuity is not present, repair or \nreplace wire 2 (Para 8-48). (b) If continuity is present, repeat \nStep 3 through Step 6 of this fault. RESISTANCE TEST\n(1) Remove cover and disconnect resistor \nfrom connector. (2) Attach multimeter positive lead (+) to \nresistor at circuit breaker side. (3) Attach multimeter negative lead (–) to \nresistor at light side.(a) If 1500 ohms resistance is \nmeasured, replace wire 10 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-377PARKING BRAKE\u001f\nLIGHT SOCKET\nWIRE 10RESISTORCOVER\nTO CIRCUIT\u001fBREAKER CB-1\nSCREW\nPANELPANELSCREW\nPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nSWITCHPARKING BRAKE\u001f\nINDICATORWIRE 23\nWIRE 2WIRE 23CONTINUITY CHE"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p429_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 429, "text": "imeter positive lead (+) to \nresistor at circuit breaker side. (3) Attach multimeter negative lead (–) to \nresistor at light side.(a) If 1500 ohms resistance is \nmeasured, replace wire 10 (Para 8-48).\n(b) If 1500 ohms resistance is not \nmeasured, replace resistor (Para 8-9). TR01623", "snippet": "imeter positive lead (+) to \nresistor at circuit breaker side. (3) Attach multimeter negative lead (–) to \nresistor at light side.(a) If 1500 ohms resistance is \nmeasured, replace wire 10 (Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p430_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 430, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-3782\n21. LOW BRAKE PRESSURE INDICA TOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nLow brake pressure. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Brake hydraulic pressure switch \nfaulty. Wire 11 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.Resistor faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-3782\n21. LOW BRAKE PRESSURE INDICA TOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p430_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 430, "text": "e. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Brake hydraulic pressure switch \nfaulty. Wire 11 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.Resistor faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs 12 vdc present at low brake \npressure indicator light \nsocket?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 7 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "e. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Brake hydraulic pressure switch \nfaulty. Wire 11 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.Resistor faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p431_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 431, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-379LOW BRAKE\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nINDICATOR\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove lens/bulb from low brake \npressure indicator. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of low brake pressure indicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-379LOW BRAKE\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nINDICATOR\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p431_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 431, "text": ". (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of low brake pressure indicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If 12 vdc is present, go to Step 2 of \nthis fault. (b) If 12 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 7 of this fault. (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). TR01611", "snippet": ". (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of low brake pressure indicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p432_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 432, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-38021. LOW BRAKE PRESSURE INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLow brake pressure. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty. Brake hydraulic pressure switch \nfaulty. Wire 11 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, replace \nbulb. KNOWN INFO\nOther gages work. 12 vdc present at socket. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBrake hydraulic pressure switch \nfaulty. Wire 11 faulty. Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question determines where \ntroubleshooting continues.2\nIs continuity present across \nlow brake pressure indicator \nlens/bulb? YESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-9).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-38021. LOW BRAKE PRESSURE INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLow brake pressure. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty. Brake hydraulic pressure "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p432_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 432, "text": "/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question determines where \ntroubleshooting continues.2\nIs continuity present across \nlow brake pressure indicator \nlens/bulb? YESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-9).\n3\nIs continuity present between \nlow brake pressure indicator \nlight socket outside conductor and known good \nground? YESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault. Go to Step 1 of this fault.", "snippet": "/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question determines where \ntroubleshooting continues.2\nIs continuity present across \nlow brake pressure indicator \nlens/bulb? YESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-9)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p433_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 433, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-381LOW BRAKE\nPRESSURE\nINDICATORBULB GROUNDCENTER\nCONDUCTOR\nOUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of bulb.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nbulb ground.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nbulb (Para 8-9).\nCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noutside conductor of low brake \npressure indicator light socket.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nlens/bulb (Para 8-9).\n(b) If continuity is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault.\nTR01612", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-381LOW BRAKE\nPRESSURE\nINDICATORBULB GROUNDCENTER\nCONDUCTOR\nOUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter condu"}
