{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p439_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 439, "text": "nd. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of high water temp \nindicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If 12 vdc is present, go to Step 2 of \nthis fault. (b) If 12 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 6 of this fault. (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).TR01601", "snippet": "nd. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of high water temp \nindicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p440_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 440, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-38822. HIGH WATER TEMP INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty. Engine water temperature switch \nfaulty. Wire 14 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, replace \nbulb. KNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp. Other gages work. 12 vdc present at socket. Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nEngine water temperature switch \nfaulty. Wire 14 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question determines where \ntroubleshooting continues.2\nIs continuity present across \nhigh water temp indicator \nlens/bulb? YESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-9).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-38822. HIGH WATER TEMP INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty. Engine water temperature switch"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p440_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 440, "text": "STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question determines where \ntroubleshooting continues.2\nIs continuity present across \nhigh water temp indicator \nlens/bulb? YESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-9).\n3\nIs continuity present between \nhigh water temp indicator \nlight socket outside \nconductor and known good ground while parking brake \nswitch is on? YESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault. Go to Step 1 of this fault.", "snippet": "STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question determines where \ntroubleshooting continues.2\nIs continuity present across \nhigh water temp indicator \nlens/bulb? YESNOReplace faulty bulb \n(Para 8-9)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p441_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 441, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-389HIGH WATER TEMP\nINDICATORBULB GROUNDCENTER\nCONDUCTOR\nOUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of bulb.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nbulb ground.\n(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nlens/bulb (Para 8-9).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noutside conductor of high water temp indicator.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nlens/bulb (Para 8-9).\n(b) If continuity is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault.\nTR01602", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-389HIGH WATER TEMP\nINDICATORBULB GROUNDCENTER\nCONDUCTOR\nOUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conducto"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p442_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 442, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-39022. HIGH WATER TEMP INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp. Other gage lights work. 12 vdc present at socket.Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nParking brake switch faulty.Wire 14 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, parking \nbrake switch is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp.Other gages work. 12 vdc present at socket. Bulb OK.Engine water temp switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 14 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity check.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present across \nwire, wire is faulty.4\nIs continuity present across \nengine water temp switch \nwhile switch sensor \ntemperature is 225°F (161°C) or higher? YESNOReplace engine \nwater temp switch (Para 8-15).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-39022. HIGH WATER TEMP INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp. Other gage lights work. 12 vdc present at socket.Bulb OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nParking br"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p442_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 442, "text": " across \nwire, wire is faulty.4\nIs continuity present across \nengine water temp switch \nwhile switch sensor \ntemperature is 225°F (161°C) or higher? YESNOReplace engine \nwater temp switch (Para 8-15).\n5\nIs continuity present across \nwire 14? YESNOReplace or repair \nwire 14 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": " across \nwire, wire is faulty.4\nIs continuity present across \nengine water temp switch \nwhile switch sensor \ntemperature is 225°F (161°C) or higher? YESNOReplace engine \nwater temp switch (Para 8-15)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p443_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 443, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-391HIGH WATER\nTEMP\nINDICATORHIGH WATER\nTEMPINDICATORLIGHT SOCKETENGINE WATERTEMP SWITCH\nWIRE 10\nWIRE 14\nPANELSCREWWIRE 14BUSHINGCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Remove wire 14 and engine water \ntemp switch from bushing. (2) Hang engine water temp switch in pan \nof water. Position switch completely \nunder water. Do not let switch make \ncontact with pan. (3) Place a thermometer in water. (4) Put heat to pan of water and stir water \nfor consistent temperature of minimum 225°F (161°C). Do not allow fingers or skin to contact hot water or hot parts. Serious burns to personnel could result. (5) Set multimeter to ohms.(6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of engine water temp switch. (7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground of engine water temp switch.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-391HIGH WATER\nTEMP\nINDICATORHIGH WATER\nTEMPINDICATORLIGHT SOCKETENGINE WATERTEMP SWITCH\nWIRE 10\nWIRE 14\nPANELSCREWWIRE 14BUSHINGCONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Remove wire 14 and engine wat"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p443_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 443, "text": ". (5) Set multimeter to ohms.(6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of engine water temp switch. (7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground of engine water temp switch.\n(a) If continuity is not present, replace \nswitch (Para 8-15). (b) If continuity is present, install \nswitch (Para 8-15) and go to \nStep 5 of this fault. CONTINUITY CHECK\n(1) Remove four screws and panel. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 14 at high water temp indicator \nterminal. (3) Using a known good jumper wire, \nconnect multimeter negative lead (–) to wire 14 at engine water temp switch \nterminal. (a) If continuity is not present, replace \nwire 14 (Para 8-48). (b) If continuity is present, repeat \nStep 3 through Step 5 of this fault. TR01603", "snippet": ". (5) Set multimeter to ohms.(6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of engine water temp switch. (7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nground of engine water temp switch."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p444_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 444, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-39222. HIGH WATER TEMP INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp.\nOther gages work.\n12 vdc not measured at socket.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nResistor faulty.\nWire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf 1500 ohms are not measured, \nresistor is faulty.6\nAre 1500 ohms present \nacross resistor?\nYESNOReplace resistor \n(Para 8-9).\nRepair or replace wire 10 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-39222. HIGH WATER TEMP INDICATOR LIGHT DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHigh water temp.\nOther gages work.\n12 vdc not measured at socket.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nResistor faulty.\nWi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p445_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 445, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-393HIGH WATER\nTEMP\nINDICATORHIGH WATER TEMP\nINDICATOR\nSOCKET\nWIRE 10WIRE 14\nPANELSCREWRESISTOR COVERRESISTANCE CHECK\n(1) Remove cover and disconnect resistor \nfrom connector.\n(2) Attach multimeter positive lead (+) to \nresistor at circuit breaker side.\n(3) Attach multimeter negative lead (–) to \nresistor at light side.\n(a) If 1500 ohms resistance is \nmeasured, replace wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).\n(b) If 1500 ohms resistance is not \nmeasured, replace resistor (Para 8-9).\nTR01604", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-393HIGH WATER\nTEMP\nINDICATORHIGH WATER TEMP\nINDICATOR\nSOCKET\nWIRE 10WIRE 14\nPANELSCREWRESISTOR COVERRESISTANCE CHECK\n(1) Remove cover and disconnect resistor \nfrom connector.\n(2)"}
