{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p446_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 446, "text": "pressure. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Engine oil pressure switch faulty.Wire 16 faulty. Wire 2 faulty. Resistor faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs 12 vdc present at low oil \npressure indicator light \nsocket?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 6 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "pressure. Other gage lights work. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBulb faulty.Engine oil pressure switch faulty.Wire 16 faulty. Wire 2 faulty. Resistor faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p447_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 447, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-395LOW OIL\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nINDICATOR\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove lens/bulb from low oil pressure \nindicator. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of low oil pressure \nindicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-395LOW OIL\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nINDICATOR\nCENTER\u001f\nCONDUCTOR• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipmen"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p447_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 447, "text": "d. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of low oil pressure \nindicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If 12 vdc is present, go to Step 2 of \nthis fault. (b) If 12 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 6 of this fault. (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). TR01132", "snippet": "d. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of low oil pressure \nindicator light socket. (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
