{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p520_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 520, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-4682\n32. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nLight faulty. Wire 50 faulty. Auto-level lamp socket faulty.Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-4682\n32. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMu"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p520_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 520, "text": "lamp socket faulty.Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual Inspection.STE/ICE-R\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues1\nIs green light illuminated \nwhen auto-level is on?START\nYESNOGo to Step 2 of this \nfault. Go to Step 3 of this fault.", "snippet": "lamp socket faulty.Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p521_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 521, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-469AUTOMATIC\nFORK LEVEL\nINDICATOR\nLIGHTAUTOMATIC\nFORK LEVEL\nSWITCH\nENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(2) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If green light is illuminated, go to \nStep 3 of this fault.\n(b) If green light is not illuminated, go \nto Step 2 of this fault.\n(3) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(4) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\nTR01747", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-469AUTOMATIC\nFORK LEVEL\nINDICATOR\nLIGHTAUTOMATIC\nFORK LEVEL\nSWITCH\nENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p522_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 522, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47032. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nLight faulty. Wire 50 faulty.Auto-level light socket faulty. Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty.Connector P4 faulty. Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test\nSTE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, light is \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 50 faulty.Auto-level light socket faulty.Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47032. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nLight faulty. Wire 50 faulty.Auto-level light socket faulty. Wire 59 faulty. "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p522_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 522, "text": "ight socket faulty.Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 50 is \nfaulty.3\nIs voltage present on wire 50 \nwhere wire 50 connects to \nlight socket? YESNORepair wire 50 \n(Para 8-48).2\nIs continuity present between \nindicator light center connector and ground?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page. YESNOReplace light\n(Para 8-9).", "snippet": "ight socket faulty.Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p523_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 523, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-471CENTER\nCONDUCTOROUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORINDICATOR\nLIGHTENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nLIGHT\nSOCKET\nWIRE 50\nWIRE 59• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Remove indicator light from socket. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of indicator light. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \noutside conductor of indicator light. (a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-471CENTER\nCONDUCTOROUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORINDICATOR\nLIGHTENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCH\nLIGHT\nSOCKET\nWIRE 50\nWIRE 59• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before wo"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p523_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 523, "text": "positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of indicator light. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \noutside conductor of indicator light. (a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, replace \nlamp (Para 8-9). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from left-hand \ninstrument panel. (2) Raise panel out to reach auto-level \nlight socket. (3) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (4) Set multimeter to dc.(5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 50 where wire 50 connects to socket. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (7) Connect negative battery cable (1) to \nnegative side of battery (2) (Para 8-42). (8) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, repair \nwire 50 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "positive lead (+) to \ncenter conductor of indicator light. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \noutside conductor of indicator light. (a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p523_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 523, "text": "RT ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, repair \nwire 50 (Para 8-48).\n(10) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).TR01748", "snippet": "RT ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, repair \nwire 50 (Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p524_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 524, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47232. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level light socket faulty. Wire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty.Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty.Connector P4 faulty. Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is present, auto-level \nlight socket is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK. Auto-level light socket OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47232. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level light socket faulty. Wire 59 faulty. Auto-le"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p524_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 524, "text": " POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs voltage present on wire 59 \nwhere wire 59 connects to \nauto-level li ght socket? YESNOReplace auto-level \nlight socket \n(Para 8-9). 5\nIs voltage present on wire 59 \nwhere wire 59 connects to \nauto-level switch? YESNOGo to Step 11 of \nthis fault.", "snippet": " POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 59 faulty. Auto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Auto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p525_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 525, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-473WIRE 58WIRE 59\nWIRE 57WIRE 65\nWIRE 64\nAUTO LEVEL\nSELECT SWITCHDASH\nPANELCENTER\nCONDUCTOROUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORINDICATOR\nLIGHT\nENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHLIGHT\nSOCKET\nWIRE 50\nWIRE 59VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 59 where wire 59 connects to \nauto-level light socket. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 5 \nof this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-473WIRE 58WIRE 59\nWIRE 57WIRE 65\nWIRE 64\nAUTO LEVEL\nSELECT SWITCHDASH\nPANELCENTER\nCONDUCTOROUTSIDE\nCONDUCTORINDICATOR\nLIGHT\nENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHLIGHT\nSOCKET\nWIRE 50\nWIRE 59VOLTAGE"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p525_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 525, "text": "6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 5 \nof this fault.\n(b) If voltage is not present, replace \nauto-level light socket (Para 8-9). (8) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 59 where wire 59 connects to \nauto-level switch. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 6 \nof this fault.", "snippet": "6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 5 \nof this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p525_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 525, "text": "6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 6 \nof this fault.\n(b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).TR01749", "snippet": "6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 6 \nof this fault."}
