{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p528_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 528, "text": "o-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, auto-level \ncircuit card faulty.8\nIs voltage present on wire 50 \nwhere wire 50 connects to \nauto-level circuit card? YESNOGo to Step 15 of \nthis fault. 9\nIs voltage present on wire 64 \nwhere wire 64 connects to \nauto-level circuit card? YESNOReplace auto-level \ncircuit card \n(Para 8-19).", "snippet": "o-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level circuit card faulty. Auto-level sensor faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p529_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 529, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-477AUTO\u001f\nLEVELER\u001f\nCABLE\nAUTO LEVELER\u001f\nCIRCUIT BOARD\nAUTO LEVELER\u001f\nCIRCUIT BOARDBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001f\nBOX \n65\u001f\n(-)2\u001f\n(-)50\u001f\n(+)64\u001f\n(+)VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 50 where wire 50 connects to \nauto-level circuit card. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-477AUTO\u001f\nLEVELER\u001f\nCABLE\nAUTO LEVELER\u001f\nCIRCUIT BOARD\nAUTO LEVELER\u001f\nCIRCUIT BOARDBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001f\nBOX \n65\u001f\n(-)2\u001f\n(-)50\u001f\n(+)64\u001f\n(+)VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cabl"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p529_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 529, "text": " ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault.\n(8) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 64 where wire 64 connects to auto-level circuit card. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nauto-level circuit card (Para 8-19).", "snippet": " ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 15 of this fault."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p529_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 529, "text": "930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nauto-level circuit card (Para 8-19).\n(8) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). TR01751", "snippet": "930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 10 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nauto-level circuit card (Para 8-19)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p530_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 530, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47832. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks.\nLight OK.\nWire 50 OK.Auto-level light socket OK.\nWire 59 OK.\nAuto-level switch OK.Connector J1 OK.\nConnector P1 OK.\nConnector J4 OK.Connector P4 OK.\nAuto-level circuit card OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level sensor faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.10\nIs voltage present on auto-\nlevel sensor connector where \nconnector c onnects to \nelectrical junction box?\nYESNOGo to Step 11 of \nthis fault.\nReplace auto-leveler sensor (Para 8-20).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-47832. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks.\nLight OK.\nWire 50 OK.Auto-level light socket OK.\nWire 59 OK.\nAuto-level switch OK.Connector J1 "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p531_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 531, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-479AUTO\u001f\nLEVELER\u001f\nCABLE\nAUTO LEVELER\u001f\nCIRCUIT BOARDBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001f\nBOX \nA\nDC EFB GROUND\nUNUSED\n+\n++VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nauto-level sensor connectors A, D, and \nE where connectors connect to \nelectrical junction box. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, replace \nsensor (Para 8-20). (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 11 of this faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-479AUTO\u001f\nLEVELER\u001f\nCABLE\nAUTO LEVELER\u001f\nCIRCUIT BOARDBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001f\nBOX \nA\nDC EFB GROUND\nUNUSED\n+\n++VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of bat"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p531_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 531, "text": " ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, replace \nsensor (Para 8-20). (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 11 of this faulty.\n(8) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). TR01752", "snippet": " ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, replace \nsensor (Para 8-20). (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 11 of this faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p532_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 532, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48032. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK.Auto-level light socket OK. Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Connector J4 OK.Connector P4 OK. Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test\nSTE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK. Auto-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card OK.Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48032. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK.Auto-level light socket OK. Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK.Connector J1 "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p532_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 532, "text": "l light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card OK.Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector P1, connector J4 and/or wire 64 or 65 are faulty.11\nIs voltage present at auto-\nlevel switch where wire 64 \nand 65 connect to auto-level switch? YESNOGo to Step 12 of \nthis fault. 12\nIs continuity present between \nwire 64 and 65 at auto-level \nswitch and connector J1-36 and connector J1-35? YESNORepair wire 64 or \n65 or connector J1 \n(Para 8-48).Replace auto-level \nswitch (Para 8-20).", "snippet": "l light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card OK.Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p533_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 533, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-481CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1P1-35\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP1P1-36P1-37J1-35J1-36J1-37WIRE 58WIRE 59\nWIRE 57WIRE 65\nWIRE 64\nAUTO\u001f\n LEVEL\u001f\nSELECT\u001f\nSWITCHDASH PANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 64 and wire 65 where wire 64 and \nwire 65 connect to auto-level switch. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, replace auto-\nlevel switch (Para 8-20).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-481CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1P1-35\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP1P1-36P1-37J1-35J1-36J1-37WIRE 58WIRE 59\nWIRE 57WIRE 65\nWIRE 64\nAUTO\u001f\n LEVEL\u001f\nSELECT\u001f\nSWITCHDASH PANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1)"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p533_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 533, "text": "ine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, replace auto-\nlevel switch (Para 8-20).\n(b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (8) Turn auto-level switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 64 and 65 where wire 64 and 65 \nconnect to auto-level switch. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-35 or connector J1-36.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 13 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 64 or 65 and/or connector J1 \n(Para 8-48).TR01753", "snippet": "ine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Turn auto-level switch to ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, replace auto-\nlevel switch (Para 8-20)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p534_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 534, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48232. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK.Auto-level light socket OK. Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK.Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector P1, connector J4, and/or wire 64 and 65 are faulty. KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK. Auto-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48232. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Wire 50 OK.Auto-level light socket OK. Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK.Auto-level ci"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p534_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 534, "text": "t socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector P1, connector J4 and/or wire 64, 65 are faulty.13\nIs continuity present between \nconnector J4-R and J4-P and \nconnector P1-36 and P1-35? YESNORepair wire 64 or \n65 and/or \nconnectors P1, and \nJ4 (Para 8-48). 14\nIs continuity present between \nwire 64 and 65 at electrical \njunction box and connector P4-R and P4-P? YESNORepair wire 64, 65 \nand/or connector J1, J4 (Para 8-49), \n(Para 8-50). Replace auto-level \nswitch (Para 8-20).", "snippet": "t socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nAuto-level switch faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p535_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 535, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-483CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1P1-35\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP1P1-36P1-37J1-35J1-36J1-37\nCONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP4J4-R J4-PJ4-NCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (4) Disconnect connector J4 from \nconnector P4. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector J4-P and J4-R where wire 64 and 65 connect. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-35 and P1-36.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 14 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 64 or 65 and/or connector P1, connector J4 (Para 8-49), \n(Para 8-50).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-483CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1P1-35\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP1P1-36P1-37J1-35J1-36J1-37\nCONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP4J4-R J4-PJ4-NCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cabl"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p535_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 535, "text": "nnector P1-35 and P1-36.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 14 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 64 or 65 and/or connector P1, connector J4 (Para 8-49), \n(Para 8-50).\nCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 64 and 65 where wire 64 and 65 connect to electrical junction box. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P4-R and P4-P.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nauto-level switch (Para 8-20). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 64 or 65 and/or connector J1 \n(Para 8-49), (Para 8-50). (6) Connect connector J1 to connector P1. (7) Connect connector J4 to connector P4. TR01754", "snippet": "nnector P1-35 and P1-36.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 14 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 64 or 65 and/or connector P1, connector J4 (Para 8-49), \n(Para 8-50)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p536_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 536, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48432. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Auto-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card OK.Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 50 fautly.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector J1 and/or wire 50 is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Auto-level light socket OK. Wire 59 OK.Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 50 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48432. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks. Light OK. Auto-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK. Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p536_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 536, "text": " Wire 59 OK.Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 50 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector P1, connector J4 and/or wire 50 faulty.15\nIs continuity present between \nwire 50 at circuit breaker CB5 \nand connector J1-37? YESNORepair wire 50 \nand/or connector J1 (Para 8-48). 16\nIs continuity present on wire \n50 between connector P1-37 \nand connector J4-N? YESNORepair wire 50 \nand/or connectors P1, J4 (Para 8-49), \n(Para 8-50).", "snippet": " Wire 59 OK.Auto-level switch OK. Auto-level circuit card OK. Auto-level sensor OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 50 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p537_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 537, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-485SCREWPANEL\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1P1-35\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP1P1-36P1-37J1-35J1-36J1-37\nCONNECTOR J4J4-R J4-PJ4-NWIRE 50\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nP4CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (4) Remove four screws from access \npanel. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 50 where wire 50 connects to circuit breaker CB6. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-37.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 16 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 50 and/or connector J1 (Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Disconnect connector J4 from \nconnector P4.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-485SCREWPANEL\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1P1-35\nCONNECTOR P1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP1P1-36P1-37J1-35J1-36J1-37\nCONNECTOR J4J4-R J4-PJ4-NWIRE 50\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nP4CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect ne"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p537_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 537, "text": "to \nStep 16 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 50 and/or connector J1 (Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Disconnect connector J4 from \nconnector P4.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P1-37 where wire 50 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J4-N.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 17 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 50 and/or connectors P1, J4 \n(Para 8-49), (Para 8-50). TR01755", "snippet": "to \nStep 16 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 50 and/or connector J1 (Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.(2) Disconnect connector J4 from \nconnector P4."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p538_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 538, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48632. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks.\nLight OK.\nAuto-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK.\nAuto-level switch OK.\nAuto-level sensor OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 50 faulty.\nAuto-level circuit card faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nConnector J4 faulty.\nConnector P4 faulty.Wire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity Test\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector P1, connector J4 and/or wire 50 faulty.17\nIs continuity present on wire \n50 between connector P4-N \nand auto-level circuit card?\nYESNO\nReplace auto-level \ncircuit card \n(Para 8-19).Repair wire 50 and/\nor connector P4 (Para 8-50).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-48632. FORK AUTO-LEVELER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nJoystick moves forks.\nLight OK.\nAuto-level light socket OK.Wire 59 OK.\nAuto-level switch OK.\nAuto-level sensor OK.\nPO"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p539_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 539, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-487CONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP4J4-R J4-PJ4-NCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P4-N where wire 50 \nconnects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nauto-level circuit card.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nauto-level circuit card (Para 8-19).\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 50 and/or connector P4 \n(Para 8-50).\n(4) Connect connector J4 to connector P4.\n(5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(6) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).(7) Install electrical junction box cover and \ntighten four screws.\nTR01756", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-487CONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP4J4-R J4-PJ4-NCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nconnector P4-N where wire 50 \nconnects.\n(3) Con"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p540_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 540, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-4882\n33. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CO NTROL DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nJoystick faulty.Connector J3 faulty.Connector P3 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty. Wire 51 faulty.Wire 52 faulty. Wire 53 faulty. Wire 54 faulty.Wire 55 faulty. Wire 56 faulty. Fork leveler mode switch faulty.Wire 57 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-4882\n33. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CO NTROL DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appen"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p540_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 540, "text": "nector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty. Wire 51 faulty.Wire 52 faulty. Wire 53 faulty. Wire 54 faulty.Wire 55 faulty. Wire 56 faulty. Fork leveler mode switch faulty.Wire 57 faulty.\nWire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 50 is \nfaulty.1\nIs voltage present at electric \njoystick where wire 50 \nconnects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNOGo to Step 2 of this \nfault. Go to Step 3 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "nector P1 faulty.Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty. Wire 51 faulty.Wire 52 faulty. Wire 53 faulty. Wire 54 faulty.Wire 55 faulty. Wire 56 faulty. Fork leveler mode switch faulty.Wire 57 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p541_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 541, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-489• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklaces, and any \nother jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can \ncatch on equipment and cause injury or short across electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical \nshock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always wear eye \nprotection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws and access panel \nfrom side console. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectric joystick te rminal boards 2 and 3 \npin + where wire 50 connects (one at a time). (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-489• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklaces, and any \nother jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can \ncatch on equipment and cause injury or short across electrica"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p541_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 541, "text": ". (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectric joystick te rminal boards 2 and 3 \npin + where wire 50 connects (one at a time). (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (8) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 2 of this fault. (9) Turn engine start switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). JOYSTICK\u001f\nTERMINAL\u001f\nBOARD\n WIRE 50SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL\n2 50 55 56-+ A BX\nTR01654", "snippet": ". (5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectric joystick te rminal boards 2 and 3 \npin + where wire 50 connects (one at a time). (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p542_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 542, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49033. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK.\nAuto-leveler OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nJoystick faulty.\nConnector J3 faulty.\nConnector P3 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nConnector J4 faulty.\nConnector P4 faulty.Wire 51 faulty.\nWire 52 faulty.\nWire 53 faulty.Wire 54 faulty.\nWire 55 faulty.\nWire 56 faulty.Fork leveler mode switch faulty.\nWire 57 faulty.\nWire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 50 \nor connector P3 is faulty.2\nIs continuity present on wire \n50 between connector P3-A \nand joystick terminal board pin +?\nYESNORepair wire 50 \nand/or connector P3 (Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49033. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK.\nAuto-leveler OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nJoystick faulty.\nConnector J3 faulty.\nConnector P3 fa"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p543_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 543, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-491SCREW\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP3\n WIRE 502 50 55 56-+ A BXCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Remove four screws from joystick \ncover plate.\n(4) Lift cover plate and joystick out to reach \nboth places where wire 50 connects at \npin +.\n(5) Disconnect connector P3 from \nconnector J3. Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to joystick terminal board where wire 50 connects (one at a \ntime).\n(6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P3-A.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 50 and/or connector P3 \n(Para 8-48).\nTR01655", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-491SCREW\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP3\n WIRE 502 50 55 56-+ A BXCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p544_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 544, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49233. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nJoystick faulty. Connector J3 faulty. Connector P3 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Connector J4 faulty. Connector P4 faulty.Wire 51 faulty. Wire 52 faulty. Wire 53 faulty.Wire 54 faulty. Wire 55 faulty. Wire 56 faulty.Fork leveler mode switch faulty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. Table 2-5.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49233. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nJoystick faulty. Connector J3 faulty. Connector P3 fa"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p544_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 544, "text": "lty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. Table 2-5.\nElectric Joystick Connections\nJoystick \nConnector WireMain\nConnectorBoom \nConnectorJoystick Terminal Board \nand Pin Function\nButton Out\nP3-C 2 J2-2 P2-2 TB1-C, TB2-__, and TB-3__ Ground\nP3-E 51 J1-27 P1-27 J4-K P4-K TB1-B Fork Ground\nP3-G 53 Fork Leveler Switch TB2-A Fork Tilt Up\nP3-D 54 Fork Leveler Switch TB2-B Fork Tilt Down\nP3-J 55 J1-31 P1-31 J4-X P4-X TB3-A Attachment Raise\nP3-F 56 J1-32 P1-32 J4-L P4-L TB3-B Attachment Lower\n57 J1-33 P1-32 J4-M P4-M Fork Tilt Up\n58 J1-34 P1-34 J4-S P4-S Fork Tilt Down\nButton In\nP3-C 2 J2-2 P2-2 TB1-C, TB2-__, and TB3-__ Ground\nP3-H 52 J1-28 P1-28 J4-H P4-H TB2-A Attachment Ground\nP3-G 53 J1-29 P1-29 J4-J P4-J TB2-A Left Fork In\nP3-D 54 J1-30 P1-30 J4-A P4-A TB2-B Left Fork Out\nP3-J 55 J1-31 P1-31 J4-X P4-X TB3-A Right Fork In\nP3-F 56 J1-32 P1-32 J4-L P4-L TB3-B Right Fork Out3\nIs voltage present at specified \npin in Table 2-5 for \nappropriate function?", "snippet": "lty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. Table 2-5."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p544_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 544, "text": "A TB2-B Left Fork Out\nP3-J 55 J1-31 P1-31 J4-X P4-X TB3-A Right Fork In\nP3-F 56 J1-32 P1-32 J4-L P4-L TB3-B Right Fork Out3\nIs voltage present at specified \npin in Table 2-5 for \nappropriate function?\nYESNOGo to Step 4 of this \nfault. Go to Step 5 of this fault.", "snippet": "A TB2-B Left Fork Out\nP3-J 55 J1-31 P1-31 J4-X P4-X TB3-A Right Fork In\nP3-F 56 J1-32 P1-32 J4-L P4-L TB3-B Right Fork Out3\nIs voltage present at specified \npin in Table 2-5 for \nappropriate function?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p545_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 545, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-493 JOYSTICK\u001f\nTERMINAL\u001f\nBOARDSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \njoystick terminal board pin for appropriate function.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 5 \nof this fault.\n(b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 4 of this fault.\n(6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\nTR01656", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-493 JOYSTICK\u001f\nTERMINAL\u001f\nBOARDSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \njoystick terminal board pin for appropria"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p546_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 546, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49433. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK.\nAuto-leveler OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nJoystick faulty.\nConnector J3 faulty.\nConnector P3 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nConnector J4 faulty.\nConnector P4 faulty.Wire 51 faulty.\nWire 52 faulty.\nWire 53 faulty.Wire 54 faulty.\nWire 55 faulty.\nWire 56 faulty.Fork leveler mode switch faulty.\nWire 57 faulty.\nWire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire \nassociated with appropriate function is faulty.4\nIs continuity present between \nspecified pin in Table 2-5 and \nconnector P3 for appropriate function?\nYESNORepair wire and/or \nconnector P3 (Para \n8-48).\nReplace electric joystick (Para 8-18).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49433. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK.\nAuto-leveler OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nJoystick faulty.\nConnector J3 faulty.\nConnector P3 fa"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p547_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 547, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-495CONNECTOR \u001f\nP3JOYSTICK\u001f\nTERMINAL\u001fBOARDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Disconnect connector P3 from \nconnector J3.\n(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \njoystick terminal board pin for appropriate function.\n(5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector pin for appropriate function.(a) If continuity is present, replace \nelectric joystick (Para 8-18).\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector P3 (Para 8-48).\n(6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(7) Connect connector J3 to connector P3.\n(8) Install four screws to secure access \npanel to side console.\nTR01657", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-495CONNECTOR \u001f\nP3JOYSTICK\u001f\nTERMINAL\u001fBOARDCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Disconn"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p548_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 548, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49633. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J4 faulty.Connector P4 faulty.Wire 51 faulty. Wire 52 faulty. Wire 53 faulty.Wire 54 faulty. Wire 55 faulty. Wire 56 faulty.Fork leveler mode switch faulty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. Table 2-6.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49633. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p548_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 548, "text": "lty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. Table 2-6.\nElectrical Junction Box Connections\nWireElectrical Junction Box Connector Boom \nConnector Main Connector Function In Out\nButton Out\n2 TB1-16 TB1-32 Ground\n51 TB2-14 TB2-32, 31, 30, and 29 J4-K P4-K J1-27 P1-27 Attachment Ground\n53 TB1-4 TB1-20 Fork Leveler Switch Fork Tilt Up\n54 TB1-5 TB1-21 Fork Leveler Switch Fork Tilt Down\n55 TB1-7 TB1-23 J4-X P4-X J1-31 P1-31 Attachment Raise\n56 TB1-9 TB1-25 J4-L P4-L J1-32 P1-32 Attachment Lower\n57 TB1-15 TB1-31 J4-M P4-M J1-33 P1-33 Fork Tilt Up\n58 TB1-11 TB-127 J4-S P4-S J1-34 P1-34 Fork Tilt Down\nButton In\n2 TB1-16 TB1-32 Ground\n52 TB2-14 TB2-3, 17, 18, and 19 J4-H P4-H J1-28 P1-28 Attachment Ground\n53 TB1-4 TB1-20 J4-J P4-J J1-29 P1-29 Left Fork In\n54 TB1-5 TB1-21 J4-A P4-A J1-30 P1-30 Left Fork Out\n55 TB1-7 TB1-23 J4-X P4-X J1-31 P1-31 Right Fork In\n56 TB1-9 TB1-25 J4-L P4-L J1-32 P1-32 Right Fork Out5\nIs voltage present at \nnumbered connector in \nelectrical junction box for specified wire/function as \nlisted in Table 2-6?", "snippet": "lty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues. Table 2-6."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p548_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 548, "text": "-31 P1-31 Right Fork In\n56 TB1-9 TB1-25 J4-L P4-L J1-32 P1-32 Right Fork Out5\nIs voltage present at \nnumbered connector in \nelectrical junction box for specified wire/function as \nlisted in Table 2-6?\nYESNOGo to Step 6 of this \nfault. Go to Step 7 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "-31 P1-31 Right Fork In\n56 TB1-9 TB1-25 J4-L P4-L J1-32 P1-32 Right Fork Out5\nIs voltage present at \nnumbered connector in \nelectrical junction box for specified wire/function as \nlisted in Table 2-6?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p549_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 549, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-497BOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1\nTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB2VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectrical junction box terminal board pin for appropriate function.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 7 \nof this fault.\n(b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 6 of this fault.\n(6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nTR01658", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-497BOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1\nTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB2VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectrical junction box term"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p550_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 550, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49833. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J4 faulty.Connector P4 faulty.Wire 51 faulty. Wire 52 faulty. Wire 53 faulty.Wire 54 faulty. Wire 55 faulty. Wire 56 faulty.Fork leveler mode switch faulty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector for appropriate function. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK. Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-49833. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p550_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 550, "text": "on. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK. Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK.\nWire 54 OK.Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFork leveler mode switch faulty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 53 or \n54 is faulty.6\nIs continuity present between \nboom connector and \nelectrical junction box terminal board connection as \nlisted in Table 2-6 for \nappropriate wire/function? YESNORepair wire and/or \nconnector \n(Para 8-50). 7\nIs voltage present at fork \nleveler mode switch where \nwire 53 or 54 connects? YESNORepair wire 53 or \n54 (Para 8-50).", "snippet": "on. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK. Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p551_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 551, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-499BOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1\nTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector P3 from \nconnector J3. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectrical junction box terminal board \npin for appropriate function. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nboom connector pin for appropriate function. (a) If continuity is present, go to Step 7 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector (Para 8-50). (5) Connect connector J3 to connector P3. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectrical junction box TB1-4 or TB1-5 \nfor appropriate function. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-499BOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1\nTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector P3 from \nconnector J3. (3) Connect multimeter pos"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p551_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 551, "text": "t multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectrical junction box TB1-4 or TB1-5 \nfor appropriate function. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 8 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, repair wire \n53 or 54 (Para 8-50). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01659", "snippet": "t multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nelectrical junction box TB1-4 or TB1-5 \nfor appropriate function. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p552_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 552, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50033. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK.Wire 51 OK. Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK.Wire 54 OK. Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFork leveler mode switch faulty. Wire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, fork mode \nleveler switch is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK. Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK. Wire 54 OK.Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. Fork leveler mode switch OK.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50033. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p552_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 552, "text": ". Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK. Wire 54 OK.Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. Fork leveler mode switch OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire \nand/or connector are faulty.8\nIs voltage present at fork \nleveler mode switch where \nwire 57 and 58 connect? YESNOReplace fork mode \nleveler switch \n(Para 8-20). 9\nIs continuity present between \nmain connector and fork \nleveler mode switch where wire 57 and 58 connect? YESNORepair wire and/or \nconnector \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": ". Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK. Wire 54 OK.Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. Fork leveler mode switch OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p553_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 553, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-501CONNECTOR J1\nP1-34\nP1-33\nCONNECTOR P1WIRE 58WIRE 59\nWIRE 57WIRE 64\nWIRE 65\nAUTOMATIC\u001f\nFORK LEVEL\u001f\nSWITCHDASH\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfork leveler mode switch where wire 57 and 58 connect. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Turn fork leveler mode switch to \nMANUAL position (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nfork leveler mode switch \n(Para 8-20). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-501CONNECTOR J1\nP1-34\nP1-33\nCONNECTOR P1WIRE 58WIRE 59\nWIRE 57WIRE 64\nWIRE 65\nAUTOMATIC\u001f\nFORK LEVEL\u001f\nSWITCHDASH\u001f\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect mul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p553_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 553, "text": "a) If voltage is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nfork leveler mode switch \n(Para 8-20). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfork leveler mode switch where wire 57 \nand 58 connect. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nmain connector pin 33 and 34 for appropriate wire.(a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 10 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector \n(Para 8-48). TR01660", "snippet": "a) If voltage is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nfork leveler mode switch \n(Para 8-20). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p554_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 554, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50233. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK.Wire 51 OK. Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK.Wire 54 OK. Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK.Fork leveler mode switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 57 faulty.Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire \nand/or connector are faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK. Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK. Wire 54 OK.Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. Fork leveler mode switch OK.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50233. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK. Auto-leveler OK. Joystick OK.Connector J3 OK. Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p554_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 554, "text": ". Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK. Wire 54 OK.Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. Fork leveler mode switch OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 57 faulty. Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire \nand/or connector are faulty.10\nIs continuity present between \nmain connector and boom \nconnector where wire 57 and 58 connect? YESNORepair wire and/or \nconnector\n(Para 8-50). 11\nIs continuity present between \nboom connector and \nelectrical junction box where wire 57 and 58 connect? YESNORepair wire and/or \nconnector\n(Para 8-50).", "snippet": ". Connector J3 OK.Connector P3 OK. Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK.Connector J4 OK. Connector P4 OK. Wire 51 OK.Wire 52 OK. Wire 53 OK. Wire 54 OK.Wire 55 OK. Wire 56 OK. Fork leveler mode switch OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p555_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 555, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-503CONNECTOR J1\nP1-34\nP1-33\nCONNECTOR P1CONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP4PIN SPIN M\nBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect connector J4 from \nconnector P4. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nboom connector pin M and S for \nappropriate wire. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nmain connector pin 33 and 34 for appropriate wire. (a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 11 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector (Para 8-50). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nboom connector pin M and S for \nappropriate wire.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-503CONNECTOR J1\nP1-34\nP1-33\nCONNECTOR P1CONNECTOR J4\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nP4PIN SPIN M\nBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect conn"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p555_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 555, "text": "ot present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector (Para 8-50). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nboom connector pin M and S for \nappropriate wire.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nelectrical juncti on box TB1-10 and \nTB1-11 for appropriate wire. (a) If continuity is present, go to \nStep 12 of this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector \n(Para 8-50). (4) Connect connector J1 to connector P1. (5) Connect connector J4 to connector P4. TR01661", "snippet": "ot present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector (Para 8-50). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nboom connector pin M and S for \nappropriate wire."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p556_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 556, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50433. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK.\nAuto-leveler OK.\nJoystick OK.Connector J3 OK.\nConnector P3 OK.\nConnector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK.\nConnector J4 OK.\nConnector P4 OK.Wire 51 OK.\nWire 52 OK.\nWire 53 OK.Wire 54 OK.\nWire 55 OK.\nWire 56 OK.Fork leveler mode switch OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 57 faulty.Wire 58 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.\nSTE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire \nand/or connector are faulty.12\nIs continuity present between \nfork tilt valve connector and \nelectrical junction box where wire 57 and 58 connect?\nYESNORepair wire and or \nconnector\n(Para 8-50).\nReplace fork tilt valve (Para 18-14).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50433. ELECTRIC JOYSTICK CONTROL DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic system OK.\nAuto-leveler OK.\nJoystick OK.Connector J3 OK.\nConnector P3 OK.\nConnector J1 OK.Connector"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p557_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 557, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-505CONNECTORATTACHMENT\u001f\nCONTROL\u001f\nVALVE\nFORK TILT\u001f\nVALVE\nBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect appropriate connector for \nappropriate wire. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfork tilt valve for appropriate wire. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nelectrical junction  box TB1-10 or \nTB1-11 for appropriate wire.(a) If continuity is present, replace fork \ntilt valve (Para 18-14). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nfaulty wire and/or connector \n(Para 8-50). (5) Connect connector to appropriate fork \ntilt valve. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).(8) Install four screws to secure joystick to \nside console.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-505CONNECTORATTACHMENT\u001f\nCONTROL\u001f\nVALVE\nFORK TILT\u001f\nVALVE\nBOOM\u001f\nELECTRICAL\u001fBOXTERMINAL\u001fBOARD\u001fTB1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to ohms. (2) Disconnect appropriate connector for"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p557_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 557, "text": "priate fork \ntilt valve. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).(8) Install four screws to secure joystick to \nside console.\nTR01662", "snippet": "priate fork \ntilt valve. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).(8) Install four screws to secure joystick to \nside console."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p558_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 558, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5062\n34. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5062\n34. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p558_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 558, "text": "y.Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, service or \nreplace battery cable (Para 8-42).1\nIs 24 vdc present at motor \nstarter solenoid where wire 9 \nconnects?START\nYESNOService battery \ncable (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "y.Connector P2 faulty.Connector J2 faulty. Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty.Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p559_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 559, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-507STARTER SOLENOID\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(3) Set multimeter to volts dc.(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nstarter solenoid where wire 9 connects.\n(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 2 of \nthis fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, service \nbattery cable (Para 8-42).\nTR01546", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-507STARTER SOLENOID\nSTARTER SOLENOIDWIRE 9VISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p560_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 560, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50834. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate.\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.\nWire 1 faulty.\nRun relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty.\nCircuit breaker CB1 faulty.\nWire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 \nfaulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present on wire 9 \nwhere wire 9 connects to \ncircuit breaker CB6?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.\nYESNOGo to step 8 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-50834. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate.\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p561_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 561, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-509SCREW\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9ACCESS\u001f\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Remove four screws and access panel. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB6. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-509SCREW\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9ACCESS\u001f\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p561_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 561, "text": "anel. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB6. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 8 of this fault. (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01546", "snippet": "anel. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB6. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p562_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 562, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51034. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK.Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB6 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cabl e OK. Wire 9 OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Fuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51034. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK.Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit brea"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p562_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 562, "text": "nector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Fuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.Fuel level transducer faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 1 \nfaulty.3\nIs 24 vdc present on wire 1 \nwhere wire 1 connects to \ncircuit breaker CB6? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB6 (Para 8-11). 4\nIs 24 vdc present on wire 1 \nwhere wire 1 connects to run \nrelay? YESNORepair wire 1 (Para \n8-48).", "snippet": "nector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Fuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p563_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 563, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-511WIRE 1CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER\u001f\nCB6\nRELAY K1\nWIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 1 where wire 1 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB6. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB6 (Para 8-11). (6) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 1 where wire 1 connects to run relay.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-511WIRE 1CIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER\u001f\nCB6\nRELAY K1\nWIRE 1VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) C"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p563_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 563, "text": "t negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 1 where wire 1 connects to run relay.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 1 (Para 8-48). (5) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01547", "snippet": "t negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 1 where wire 1 connects to run relay."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p564_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 564, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51234. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK.Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nRun relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty.Fuel gage faulty. Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty. Fuel level transducer faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, run relay \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK. Wire 9 OK.Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51234. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK.Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p564_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 564, "text": ".Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 3 \nfaulty.5\nIs 24 vdc present on wire 3 \nwhere wire 3 connects to run \nrelay? YESNOReplace run relay \n(Para 8-23). 6\nIs 24 vdc present on wire 3 \nwhere wire 3 connects to \ncircuit breaker CB1? YESNORepair wire 3 (Para \n8-48).", "snippet": ".Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK.Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p565_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 565, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-513WIRE 3CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nRELAY K1\nWIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 3 where wire 3 connects to run relay. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-513WIRE 3CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nRELAY K1\nWIRE 3VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 3 where wire 3 connects to run relay. ("}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p565_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 565, "text": "vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 3 where wire 3 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB1. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01548", "snippet": "vdc is not present, replace run \nrelay (Para 8-23). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p566_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 566, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51434. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate.\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.Wire 9 OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 OK.\nRun relay OK.Wire 3 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB1 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB1 faulty.7\nIs 24 vdc present on wire 10 \nwhere wire 10 connects to \ncircuit breaker CB1?\nYESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB1 (Para 8-11).\nRepair wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51434. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate.\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.Wire 9 OK.\nConnector P2 OK.\nConnector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK.\nWire 1 "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p567_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 567, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-515WIRE 10CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nENGINE START\nSWITCH\nWIRE 10FUEL\nGAGEVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 10 where wire 10 connects to \ncircuit breaker CB1.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, repair wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB1 (Para 8-11).\n(6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(7) Install access panel and four screws.\n(8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01549", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-515WIRE 10CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nENGINE START\nSWITCH\nWIRE 10FUEL\nGAGEVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 10 where wire 10 "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p568_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 568, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51634. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty. Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty.Wire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector J2 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK. Wire 9 OK.Connector J2 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Fuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-51634. NONE OF THE GAGES OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nGages do not operate. Battery OK. Battery cable OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty. Connector P2 faulty. Connector J2 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p568_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 568, "text": "PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Fuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.Fuel level transducer faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 9 \nor connector P2 faulty.8\nIs continuity present on wire 9 \nbetween wire 9 and \nconnector J2-1? YESNORepair wire 9 or \nconnector J2 \n(Para 8-48). 9\nIs continuity present on wire 9 \nbetween starter motor \nsolenoid and connector P2-1? YESNO\nGo to Step 3 of this \nfault.Repair wire 9 or \nconnector P2 \n(Para 8-49).", "snippet": "PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.Circuit breaker CB6 faulty.Wire 1 faulty. Run relay faulty. Wire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Fuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p569_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 569, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-517CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1 P2-1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9STARTER SOLENOID\nWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (3) Set multimeter to ohms. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to circuit \nbreaker CB6. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J2-1.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector J2 (Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to starter motor solenoid.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-517CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-1 P2-1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCIRCUIT BREAKER CB6WIRE 9STARTER SOLENOID\nWIRE 9CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nneg"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p569_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 569, "text": "a 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to starter motor solenoid.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P2-1.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 9 or connector P2 (Para 8-49). TR01551", "snippet": "a 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2. (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 9 where wire 9 connects to starter motor solenoid."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p570_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 570, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5182\n35. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P.\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.\nWire 10 faulty.Voltage gage faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.\nSTE/ICE-R.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nDo any of the other gages \nwork?START\nYESNOGo to Fault 34, \nNone of the gages operate.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5182\n35. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimete"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p571_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 571, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-519GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCHVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If the other gages are operating, go \nto Step 2 of this fault.\n(b) If all gages are not operating, go to \nFault 34, None of the gages \noperate.\n(2) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\nTR01513", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-519GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCHVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If the other gages are operating, go \n"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p572_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 572, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52035. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.\nVoltage gage faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 10 \nfaulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at voltage \ngage where wire 10 \nconnects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.\nYESNORepair wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52035. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.\nVoltage gage faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTI"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p573_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 573, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-521SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE START\nSWITCHVOLTMETERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach voltage gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nvoltage gage where wire 10 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-521SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE START\nSWITCHVOLTMETERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch o"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p573_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 573, "text": "om instrument \npanel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach voltage gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nvoltage gage where wire 10 connects.\n(7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (8) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (9) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 10 (Para 8-48). (10) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01514", "snippet": "om instrument \npanel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach voltage gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nvoltage gage where wire 10 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p574_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 574, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52235. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.Voltage gage faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, voltage \ngage faulty.3\nIs voltage present at voltage \ngage where wire 2 connects?\nYESNOReplace voltage \ngage (Para 8-6).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52235. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.Voltage gage faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltag"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p575_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 575, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-523SCREW\nWIRE 2ENGINE START\n SWITCHVOLTMETERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nvoltage gage where wire 2 connects.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault.\n(b) If voltage is not present, replace \nvoltage gage (Para 8-6).\n(5) Turn engine start switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\nTR01515", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-523SCREW\nWIRE 2ENGINE START\n SWITCHVOLTMETERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nvoltage gage where wire 2 c"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p576_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 576, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52435. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nVoltage gage OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.4\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nwhere wire 2 connects to \nvoltage gage and negative battery cable?\nYESNOGo to Step 5 of this \nfault.\nService or replace battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52435. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nVoltage gage OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuit"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p577_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 577, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-525WIRE 2NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nVOLTMETERCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 2 where wire 2 connects to voltage \ngage.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nnegative battery cable.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42).\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault.\nTR01520", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-525WIRE 2NEGATIVE\u001f\nBATTERY\u001f\nCABLE\nVOLTMETERCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Conne"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p578_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 578, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52635. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nVoltage gage OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 2 \nor connector J2 faulty.5\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween voltage gage and \nconnector J2-2?\nYESNORepair wire 2 or \nconnector J2(Para 8-48).\nGo to Step 6 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52635. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nVoltage gage OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.\nConnector P2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuit"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p579_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 579, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-527WIRE 2VOLTMETER\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-2\nP2-1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 2 where wire 2 connects to voltage \ngage. \n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J2-2.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 6 \nof this fault.\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 or connector J2 (Para 8-48).\n(5) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews.\nTR01521", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-527WIRE 2VOLTMETER\nCONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2J2-2\nP2-1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Co"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p580_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 580, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52835. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nVoltage gage OK.\nConnector J2 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 2 \nor connector P2 faulty.6\nIs continuity present on wire 2 \nbetween negative battery \ncable and connector P2-2?\nYESNORepair wire 2 or \nconnector P2\n(Para 8-49).\nService or replace \nbattery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-52835. VOLTMETER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nWire 10 OK.\nVoltage gage OK.\nConnector J2 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity te"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p581_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 581, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-529CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-2WIRE 2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect connector J2 from \nconnector P2.\n(3) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 2 where wire 2 connects to \nnegative battery cable. \n(5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P2-2.(a) If continuity is present, service or \nreplace battery (Para 8-42).\n(b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 2 or connector P2 (Para 8-49).\n(6) Connect connector J2 to connector P2.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01522", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-529CONNECTOR P2\nCONNECTOR \u001f\nJ2\nCONNECTOR P2P2-2WIRE 2CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Disconnect connector J2"}
