{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p583_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 583, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-531GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCH\nVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If the other gages are operating, go \nto Step 2 of this fault.\n(b) If all gages are not operating, go to \nFault 34, None of the gages operate.\n(2) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\nTR01523", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-531GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCH\nVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If the other gages are operating, go "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p584_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 584, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-53236. ENGINE HOUR METER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNo movement of hour meter.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.\nHour meter faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 10 \nfaulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at hour \nmeter where wire 10 \nconnects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.\nYESNORepair wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-53236. ENGINE HOUR METER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNo movement of hour meter.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.\nHour meter faul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p585_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 585, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-533SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHHOUR\nMETERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Left instrument panel out to reach hour \nmeter. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nhour meter where wire 10 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-533SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHHOUR\nMETERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p585_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 585, "text": " four screws from instrument \npanel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Left instrument panel out to reach hour \nmeter. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nhour meter where wire 10 connects.\n(7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (8) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (9) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 10 (Para 8-48). (10) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01524", "snippet": " four screws from instrument \npanel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Left instrument panel out to reach hour \nmeter. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nhour meter where wire 10 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p586_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 586, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-53436. ENGINE HOUR METER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNo movement of hour meter.\nWire 10 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.\nHour meter faulty.\nWire 2 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, hour \nmeter faulty.3\nIs voltage present at hour \nmeter where wire 2 connects?\nYESNOReplace hour meter \n(Para 8-10).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-53436. ENGINE HOUR METER DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNo movement of hour meter.\nWire 10 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P2 faulty.\nConnector J2 faulty.\nHour meter faulty."}
