{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p595_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 595, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-543GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCH\nVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If the other gages are operating, go \nto Step 2 of this fault.\n(b) If all gages are not operating, go to \nFault 34, None of the gages \noperate.\n(2) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\nTR01543", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-543GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCH\nVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If the other gages are operating, go "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p596_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 596, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-54437. FUEL GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nLow fuel.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty.\nFuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.Fuel level transducer faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 10 \nfaulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at fuel gage \nwhere wire 10 connects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.\nYESNORepair wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-54437. FUEL GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nLow fuel.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty.\nFuel gage faulty.Wire 12 faulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.\nConnector P1 faulty.Fuel le"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p597_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 597, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-545SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE START\nSWITCHFUEL\nGAGEINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\n• Remove rings bracelets watc hes, necklaces, and any other \njewelry before working around vehi cle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short across electr ical circuit \nand cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always wear eye \nprotection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws from right-hand \ninstrument panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach fuel gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfuel gage where wire 10 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-545SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE START\nSWITCHFUEL\nGAGEINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\n• Remove rings bracelets watc hes, necklaces, and any other \njewelry before working around vehi cle. Jewelry can catc"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p597_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 597, "text": "ght-hand \ninstrument panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach fuel gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfuel gage where wire 10 connects.\n(7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (8) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (9) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 10 (Para 8-48). (10) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01544", "snippet": "ght-hand \ninstrument panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach fuel gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfuel gage where wire 10 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p598_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 598, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-54637. FUEL GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLow fuel. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFuel gage faulty. Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Fuel level transducer faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, fuel gage \nfaulty. KNOWN INFO\nLow fuel. Wire 10 OK. Fuel gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Fuel level transducer faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs voltage present at fuel gage \nwhere wire 12 connects? YESNOReplace fuel gage \n(Para 8-6). 4\nIs voltage present at fuel level \ntransducer where wire 12 \nconnects?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-54637. FUEL GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLow fuel. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFuel gage faulty. Wire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.Fuel level"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p598_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 598, "text": "s where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs voltage present at fuel gage \nwhere wire 12 connects? YESNOReplace fuel gage \n(Para 8-6). 4\nIs voltage present at fuel level \ntransducer where wire 12 \nconnects?\nYESNOGo to Step 5 of this \nfault. Repair fuel level \ntransducer \n(Para 8-38).", "snippet": "s where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs voltage present at fuel gage \nwhere wire 12 connects? YESNOReplace fuel gage \n(Para 8-6). 4\nIs voltage present at fuel level \ntransducer where wire 12 \nconnects?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p599_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 599, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-547SCREW\nENGINE START\nSWITCHFUEL\nGAGE\nWIRE 12\nWIRE 12TRANSDUCERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfuel gage where wire 12 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nfuel gage (Para 8-6). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-547SCREW\nENGINE START\nSWITCHFUEL\nGAGE\nWIRE 12\nWIRE 12TRANSDUCERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfuel gag"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p599_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 599, "text": "tage is not present, replace \nfuel gage (Para 8-6). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Remove four screws and cap from fuel \nlevel transducer. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nfuel level transducer where wire 12 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, replace fuel \nlevel transducer (Para 8-38). (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault. (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (9) Install cap and four screws for fuel level \ntransducer. TR01545", "snippet": "tage is not present, replace \nfuel gage (Para 8-6). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p600_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 600, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-54837. FUEL GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLow fuel. Wire 10 OK. Fuel gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 12 \nor connector J1 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nLow fuel. Fuel gage OK. Wire 10 OK. Connector J1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P1 faulty. Wire 12 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test. STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 12 \nor connector P1 faulty.5\nIs continuity present on \nwire 12 between fuel gage and \nconnector J1-16? YESNORepair wire 12 or \nconnector J1 \n(Para 8-48). 6\nIs continuity present on \nwire 12 between fuel level \ntransducer and \nconnector P1-16?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-54837. FUEL GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nLow fuel. Wire 10 OK. Fuel gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 12 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nC"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p600_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 600, "text": " present on \nwire 12 between fuel gage and \nconnector J1-16? YESNORepair wire 12 or \nconnector J1 \n(Para 8-48). 6\nIs continuity present on \nwire 12 between fuel level \ntransducer and \nconnector P1-16?\nYESNORepair wire 12 or \nconnector P1 (Para 8-49). Replace fuel level \ntransducer \n(Para 8-38).", "snippet": " present on \nwire 12 between fuel gage and \nconnector J1-16? YESNORepair wire 12 or \nconnector J1 \n(Para 8-48). 6\nIs continuity present on \nwire 12 between fuel level \ntransducer and \nconnector P1-16?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p601_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 601, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-549CONNECTOR P1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR P1P1-16J1-16WIRE 12\nWIRE 12TRANSDUCERCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 12 where wire 12 connects to fuel \ngage. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-16.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 6 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 12 or connector J1 \n(Para 8-48). (5) Connect connector J1 to connector P1. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 12 where wire 12 connects to fuel \nlevel transducer.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-549CONNECTOR P1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR P1P1-16J1-16WIRE 12\nWIRE 12TRANSDUCERCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to oh"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p601_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 601, "text": "r P1. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 12 where wire 12 connects to fuel \nlevel transducer.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-16.(a) If continuity is present, replace fuel \nlevel transducer (Para 8-38). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 12 or connector P1 \n(Para 8-49). (5) Connect connector J1 to connector P1. (6) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. (7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42). TR01552", "snippet": "r P1. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 12 where wire 12 connects to fuel \nlevel transducer."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p602_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 602, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5502\n38. TEMPERATURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nNo temperature reading. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty. Temperature gage faulty. Wire 15 faulty.Engine water temperature \ntransducer faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.STE/ICE-R.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5502\n38. TEMPERATURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMu"}
