{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p605_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 605, "text": "d \ninstrument panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach temperature gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ntemp gage where wire 10 connects.\n(7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (8) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (9) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 10 (Para 8-48). (10) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01534", "snippet": "d \ninstrument panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach temperature gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ntemp gage where wire 10 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p606_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 606, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-55438. TEMPERATURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNo temperature reading. Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK.Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nTemperature gage faulty.Wire 15 faulty.Engine water temperature \ntransducer faulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, \ntemperature gage faulty. KNOWN INFO\nNo temperature reading. Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK. Wire 10 OK.Temperature gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 15 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-55438. TEMPERATURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNo temperature reading. Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p606_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 606, "text": "ector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK. Wire 10 OK.Temperature gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 15 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.\nEngine water temperature \ntransducer faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs voltage present at \ntemperature gage where \nwire 15 connects? YESNOReplace temp gage \n(Para 8-6). 4\nIs voltage present at engine \nwater temperature transducer \nwhere wire 15 connects? YESNOGo to Step 5 of this \nfault. Replace engine \nwater temperature \ntransducer (Para 8-36).", "snippet": "ector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK. Wire 10 OK.Temperature gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 15 faulty.Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p607_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 607, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-555SCREW\nENGINE START\nSWITCHTEMPERATURE\nGAGE\nWIRE 15\nWIRE 15TRANSDUCERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ntemp gage where wire 15 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \ntemp gage (Para 8-6). (5) Turn engine start switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nengine water temperature transducer \nwhere wire 15 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-555SCREW\nENGINE START\nSWITCHTEMPERATURE\nGAGE\nWIRE 15\nWIRE 15TRANSDUCERINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nt"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p607_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 607, "text": "1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nengine water temperature transducer \nwhere wire 15 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, replace temp. transducer (Para 8-36). (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 5 of this fault. (5) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). TR01535", "snippet": "1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nengine water temperature transducer \nwhere wire 15 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p608_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 608, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-55638. TEMPERATURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNo temperature reading. Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK.Wire 10 OK. Temperature gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 15 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 15 \nor connector J1 faulty. KNOWN INFO\nNo temperature reading. Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK. Connector J2 OK.Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK. Wire 10 OK.Connector J1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P1 faulty.Wire 15 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-55638. TEMPERATURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNo temperature reading. Wire 9 OK. Connector P2 OK.Connector J2 OK. Circuit breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK.Run relay OK. Wi"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p608_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 608, "text": " breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK. Wire 10 OK.Connector J1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P1 faulty.Wire 15 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, wire 15 \nor connector P1 faulty.5\nIs continuity present on \nwire 15 between temp gage \nand connector J1-10? YESNORepair wire 15 \n(Para 8-48) or \nconnector J1 (Para 8-48). 6\nIs continuity present on \nwire 15 between water temp \ntransducer and \nconnector P1-10? YESNORepair wire 15\n(Para 8-49) or\nconnector P1(Para 8-49). Replace engine \nwater temperature \ntransducer (Para 8-36).", "snippet": " breaker CB6 OK. Wire 1 OK. Run relay OK.Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB1 OK. Wire 10 OK.Connector J1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector P1 faulty.Wire 15 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p609_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 609, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-557CONNECTOR P1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR P1P1-10J1-10WIRE 15\nWIRE 15TRANSDUCERCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (3) Set multimeter to ohms. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 15 where wire 15 connects to \ntemp gage. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-10.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 6 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 15 or connector J1 \n(Para 8-48). (6) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to ohms.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-557CONNECTOR P1CONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR\u001f\nJ1\nCONNECTOR P1P1-10J1-10WIRE 15\nWIRE 15TRANSDUCERCONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Pa"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p609_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 609, "text": "is not present, repair \nwire 15 or connector J1 \n(Para 8-48). (6) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to ohms.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nwire 15 where wire 15 connects to engine water temperature transducer. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-16).(a) If continuity is present, replace \nwater temp. transducer \n(Para 8-36). (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 15 or connector P1 (Para 8-49). (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery. (6) Install battery cover (Para 8-42). TR01542", "snippet": "is not present, repair \nwire 15 or connector J1 \n(Para 8-48). (6) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect connector J1 from \nconnector P1. (2) Set multimeter to ohms."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p610_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 610, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5582\n39. OIL PRESSURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nNo oil pressure reading. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty. Oil pressure gage faulty. Wire 17 faulty.Engine oil pressure transducer \nfaulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.STE/ICE-R.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5582\n39. OIL PRESSURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nM"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p610_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 610, "text": "ng. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty. Oil pressure gage faulty. Wire 17 faulty.Engine oil pressure transducer \nfaulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.STE/ICE-R.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nDo any of the other gages \nwork?START\nYESNOGo to Fault 34, \nNone of the gages operate.", "snippet": "ng. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty. Oil pressure gage faulty. Wire 17 faulty.Engine oil pressure transducer \nfaulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.STE/ICE-R."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p611_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 611, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-559GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCHVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If the other gages are operating, go \nto Step 2 of this fault.\n(b) If all gages are not operating, go to \nFault 34, None of the gages \noperate.\n(2) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\nTR01493", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-559GAGEENGINE START\nSWITCHVISUAL INSPECTION\n(1) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If the other gages are operating, go \nt"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p612_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 612, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-56039. OIL PRESSURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNo oil pressure reading.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty.\nOil pressure gage faulty.Wire 17 faulty.\nEngine oil pressure transducer \nfaulty.\nConnector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 10 \nfaulty.2\nIs 24 vdc present at engine oil \npressure gage where wire 10 \nconnects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.\nYESNORepair wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-56039. OIL PRESSURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nNo oil pressure reading.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty.\nOil pressure gage faulty.Wire 17 faulty.\nEngine oil pressu"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p613_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 613, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-561SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE\nSTART\n SWITCHOIL\nPRESSURE\nGAGEINSTRUMENT\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws from right-hand \ninstrument panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach oil pressure gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noil pressure gage where wire 10 \nconnects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-561SCREW\nWIRE 10ENGINE\nSTART\n SWITCHOIL\nPRESSURE\nGAGEINSTRUMENT\nPANEL• Remove rings bracelets watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry ca"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p613_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 613, "text": "ent panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach oil pressure gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noil pressure gage where wire 10 \nconnects.\n(7) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (8) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (9) Turn engine start switch to START \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 10 (Para 8-48). (10) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (11) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01494", "snippet": "ent panel. (4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Lift right-hand instrument panel out to \nreach oil pressure gage. (6) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noil pressure gage where wire 10 \nconnects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p614_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 614, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-56239. OIL PRESSURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNo oil pressure reading. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nOil pressure gage faulty. Wire 17 faulty. Engine oil pressure transducer \nfaulty. Connector J1 faulty.Connector P1 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, \ntemperature gage faulty. KNOWN INFO\nNo oil pressure reading. Wire 10 OK. Oil pressure gage OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 17 faulty. Connector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Engine oil pressure transducer \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs voltage present at oil \npressure gage where wire 17 \nconnects?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-56239. OIL PRESSURE GAGE DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nNo oil pressure reading. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nOil pressure gage faulty. Wire 17 faulty. Engine oil pressure "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p614_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 614, "text": "e test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs voltage present at oil \npressure gage where wire 17 \nconnects?\nYESNOReplace oil pressure \ngage (Para 8-6). 4\nIs voltage present at engine \noil pressure transducer where \nwire 17 connects? YESNOGo to Step 5 of \nthis fault. Replace engine oil pressure transducer (Para 8-35).", "snippet": "e test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.3\nIs voltage present at oil \npressure gage where wire 17 \nconnects?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p615_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 615, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-563SCREW\nENGINE START\nSWITCH\nWIRE 17\nWIRE 17TRANSDUCEROIL\nPRESSURE\nGAGEINSTRUMENT\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \noil pressure gage where wire 17 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Turn engine start switch to START \nposition, (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace oil \npressure gage (Para 8-6). (5) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nengine oil pressure transducer where \nwire 17 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-563SCREW\nENGINE START\nSWITCH\nWIRE 17\nWIRE 17TRANSDUCEROIL\nPRESSURE\nGAGEINSTRUMENT\nPANELVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \no"}
