{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p628_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 628, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57641. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty.Wire 91 faulty. Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.Emergency steering relay faulty. Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector J1 or wire 10 is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57641. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p628_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 628, "text": "draulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.\nEmergency steering relay faulty.Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity testSTE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector P1 or wire 10 is faulty.2\nIs continuity present on \nwire 10 between circuit \nbreaker CB1 and connector J1-23? YESNORepair wire 10 and/\nor connector J1 (Para 8-48). 3\nIs continuity present on wire \n10 between hydraulic \npressure sensor and connector P1-23? YESNORepair wire 10 \nand/or connector \nP1 (Para 8-49).", "snippet": "draulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p629_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 629, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57791 10\nNC\nC\nNOWIRE\u001f\n10HYDRAULIC\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nSENSORSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELCIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nCONNECTOR J1J1-23P1-23WIRE 10\nCONNECTOR P1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Remove four screws and access panel. (3) Set multimeter to ohms.(4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB1 where wire 10 connects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-23.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 10 and/or connector J1 (Para 8-48). (6) Install access panel and four screws. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57791 10\nNC\nC\nNOWIRE\u001f\n10HYDRAULIC\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nSENSORSCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANELCIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nCONNECTOR J1J1-23P1-23WIRE 10\nCONNECTOR P1CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p629_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 629, "text": "ot present, repair \nwire 10 and/or connector J1 (Para 8-48). (6) Install access panel and four screws. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nhydraulic pressure sensor where wire \n10 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-23.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 10 and/or connector P1 \n(Para 8-49). TR01554", "snippet": "ot present, repair \nwire 10 and/or connector J1 (Para 8-48). (6) Install access panel and four screws. CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p630_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 630, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57841. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty.Wire 91 faulty. Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.Emergency steering relay faulty. Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, hydraulic \npressure sensor is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-57841. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p630_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 630, "text": "draulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.\nEmergency steering relay faulty.Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 91 is \nfaulty.4\nIs voltage present at hydraulic \npressure sensor where \nwire 91 connects? YESNO\n5\nIs voltage present at \nemergency steering switch \nwhere wire 91 connects? YESNOGo to Step 6 of this \nfault.Repair hydraulic pressure sensor \n(Para 8-53). Go to Step 8 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "draulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p631_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 631, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-579EMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSWITCH91 10\nNC\nC\nNOWIRE\u001f\n91\nWIRE\u001f\n91HYDRAULIC\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nSENSORVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nhydraulic pressure sensor where \nwire 91 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 5 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nhydraulic pressure sensor \n(Para 8-53). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-579EMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSWITCH91 10\nNC\nC\nNOWIRE\u001f\n91\nWIRE\u001f\n91HYDRAULIC\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nSENSORVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p631_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 631, "text": "to Step 5 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nhydraulic pressure sensor \n(Para 8-53). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering switch where wire \n91 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 8 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 6 of this fault. (6) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).TR01555", "snippet": "to Step 5 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nhydraulic pressure sensor \n(Para 8-53). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p632_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 632, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58041. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty.Wire 91 faulty. Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.Emergency steering relay faulty. Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector J1 or wire 91 is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58041. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p632_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 632, "text": "draulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.\nEmergency steering relay faulty.Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nContinuity test.STE/ICE-R #91. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf continuity is not present, \nconnector P1 or wire 91 faulty.6\nIs continuity present on wire \n91 between hydraulic \npressure sensor and conector J1-22? YESNORepair wire 91 and/\nor connector J1 \n(Para 8-48). 7\nIs continuity present on wire \n91 between emergency \nsteering switch and connector P1-22? YESNORepair wire 91 \nand/or connector \nP1 (Para 8-49).", "snippet": "draulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty. Wire 91 faulty.Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p633_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 633, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58191 10\nNC\nC\nNOWIRE\u001f\n91HYDRAULIC\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nSENSOR\nCONNECTOR J1J1-22P1-22\nCONNECTOR P1\nEMERGENCY \u001f\nSTEERING\u001f\nSWITCH\nWIRE\u001f\n10CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nhydraulic pressure sensor where wire \n91 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector J1-22.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 7 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 91 and/or connector J1 \n(Para 8-48). CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering switch where wire 91 connects.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58191 10\nNC\nC\nNOWIRE\u001f\n91HYDRAULIC\u001f\nPRESSURE\u001f\nSENSOR\nCONNECTOR J1J1-22P1-22\nCONNECTOR P1\nEMERGENCY \u001f\nSTEERING\u001f\nSWITCH\nWIRE\u001f\n10CONTINUITY TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p633_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 633, "text": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering switch where wire 91 connects.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nconnector P1-22.(a) If continuity is present, go to Step 8 \nof this fault. (b) If continuity is not present, repair \nwire 91 and/or connector P1 (Para 8-49). TR01556", "snippet": " Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to ohms.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering switch where wire 91 connects."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p634_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 634, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58241. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK.Hydraulic pressure sensor OK. Wire 91 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Emergency steering switch faulty. Wire 92 faulty.Emergency steering relay faulty. Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, \nemergency steering switch is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. Hydraulic pressure sensor OK.Wire 91 OK. Emergency steering switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Wire 92 faulty. Emergency steering relay faulty.Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58241. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK.Hydraulic pressure sensor OK. Wire 91 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnecto"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p634_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 634, "text": "ring switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Wire 92 faulty. Emergency steering relay faulty.Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 92 is \nfaulty.8\nIs voltage present at \nemergency steering switch \nwhere wire 92 connects with the emergency steering \nswitch ON? YESNOReplace emergency \nsteering switch (Para 8-7). 9\nIs voltage present at \nemergency steering solenoid \nwhere wire 92 connects with the emergency steering \nswitch ON? YESNOGo to Step 10 of \nthis fault. Go to Step 12 of \nthis fault.", "snippet": "ring switch OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nConnector J1 faulty. Connector P1 faulty. Wire 92 faulty. Emergency steering relay faulty.Emergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p635_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 635, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-583EMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSWITCH\nWIRE\u001f\n92\nEMERGENCY \u001f\nSTEERING\u001f\nSOLENOID\nWIRE 92VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering switch where \nwire 92 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn emergency steering switch ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 9 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nemergency steering switch (Para 8-7). (7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-583EMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSWITCH\nWIRE\u001f\n92\nEMERGENCY \u001f\nSTEERING\u001f\nSOLENOID\nWIRE 92VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Se"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p635_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 635, "text": "t present, replace \nemergency steering switch (Para 8-7). (7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering switch where \nwire 92 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn emergency steering switch ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 12 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, go to \nStep 10 of this fault. (6) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01557", "snippet": "t present, replace \nemergency steering switch (Para 8-7). (7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
