{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p638_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 638, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58641. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK.Hydraulic pressure sensor OK. Wire 91 OK. Emergency steering switch OK.Connector J1 OK. Connector P1 OK. Wire 92 OK.Emergency steering relay OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nEmergency steering solenoid \nfaulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, \nemergency steering solenoid is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK. Hydraulic pressure sensor OK.Wire 91 OK. Emergency steering switch OK. Connector J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. Wire 92 OK. Emergency steering relay OK.Emergency steering solenoid OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.Emergency steering motor faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58641. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK. Gages OK. Wire 10 OK.Hydraulic pressure sensor OK. Wire 91 OK. Emergency steering switch "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p638_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 638, "text": " J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. Wire 92 OK. Emergency steering relay OK.Emergency steering solenoid OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.Emergency steering motor faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 9 is \nfaulty.12\nIs voltage present at \nemergency steering solenoid \nwhere ground wire connects? YESNOReplace emergency \nsteering solenoid \n(Para 8-22). 13\nIs voltage present at \nemergency steering motor \nwhere wire 9 connects? YESNORepair wire 9 (Para \n8-49).", "snippet": " J1 OK.Connector P1 OK. Wire 92 OK. Emergency steering relay OK.Emergency steering solenoid OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 9 faulty.Emergency steering motor faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p639_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 639, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-587GROUNDEMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSOLENOID\nWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering solenoid where \nground wire connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn emergency steering switch ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 13 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nemergency steering solenoid (Para 8-22). (7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-587GROUNDEMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSOLENOID\nWIRE 9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Con"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p639_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 639, "text": "resent, replace \nemergency steering solenoid (Para 8-22). (7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering motor where wire 9 connects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn emergency steering switch ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 14 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, repair \nwire 9 (Para 8-49). (7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01559", "snippet": "resent, replace \nemergency steering solenoid (Para 8-22). (7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p640_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 640, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58841. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK.\nGages OK.\nWire 10 OK.Hydraulic pressure sensor OK.\nWire 91 OK.\nEmergency steering switch OK.Connector J1 OK.\nConnector P1 OK.\nWire 92 OK.Emergency steering relay OK.\nEmergency steering solenoid OK.\nWire 9 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nEmergency steering motor faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, \nemergency steering motor is faulty.14\nIs voltage present at \nemergency steering motor \nwhere ground wire connects with the emergency steering \nswitch ON?\nYESNOReplace emergency \nsteering motor \n(Para 8-22).\nRepair ground wire \n(Para 8-49).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-58841. EMERGENCY STEERING PUMP DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nHydraulic Systems OK.\nGages OK.\nWire 10 OK.Hydraulic pressure sensor OK.\nWire 91 OK.\nEmergency steering switch "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p641_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 641, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-589EMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSWITCH\nEMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001f\nSOLENOIDGROUNDVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nemergency steering motor where \nground wire connects.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(6) Turn emergency steering switch ON \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If voltage is present, repair ground \nwire (Para 8-49).\n(b) If voltage is not present, replace \nemergency steering motor \n(Para 8-22).\n(7) Turn emergency steering switch OFF \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).\nTR01560", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-589EMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001fSWITCH\nEMERGENCY\u001f\nSTEERING\u001f\nSOLENOIDGROUNDVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(2) Set multimeter"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p642_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 642, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5902\n42. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Parking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Hydraulic steering select valve OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB9 faulty.Wire 83 faulty. Steering select switch faulty. Wire 84 faulty.Wire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5902\n42. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanics: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p642_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 642, "text": "eering select valve OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB9 faulty.Wire 83 faulty. Steering select switch faulty. Wire 84 faulty.Wire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 3 is \nfaulty.1\nIs voltage present at circuit \nbreaker CB9 where wire 3 \nconnects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNORepair wire 3\n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "eering select valve OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty.Circuit breaker CB9 faulty.Wire 83 faulty. Steering select switch faulty. Wire 84 faulty.Wire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p643_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 643, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-591WIRE 3\nCIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER CB9SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws and access panel.(4) Set multimeter to volts dc.(5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB9 where wire 3 connects. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-591WIRE 3\nCIRCUIT\u001f\nBREAKER CB9SCREWACCESS\u001f\nPANEL• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipme"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p643_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 643, "text": " and access panel.(4) Set multimeter to volts dc.(5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB9 where wire 3 connects. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (8) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 2 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01586", "snippet": " and access panel.(4) Set multimeter to volts dc.(5) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB9 where wire 3 connects. (6) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p644_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 644, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59242. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB9 faulty. Wire 83 faulty. Steering select switch faulty.Wire 84 faulty. Wire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage TestSTE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB9 is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB9 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 83 faulty. Steering select switch faulty. Wire 84 faulty.Wire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 83 is \nfaulty.2\nIs voltage present at circuit \nbreaker CB9 where wire 83 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB9\n(Para 8-11).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59242. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB9 faulty. Wire 83 faulty. St"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p644_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 644, "text": "st.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 83 is \nfaulty.2\nIs voltage present at circuit \nbreaker CB9 where wire 83 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB9\n(Para 8-11).\n3\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect switch where wire 83 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 83\n(Para 8-48). Go to Step 4 (crab) \nor Step 5 (4 wheel) \nof this fault.", "snippet": "st.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 83 is \nfaulty.2\nIs voltage present at circuit \nbreaker CB9 where wire 83 \nconnects? YESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB9\n(Para 8-11)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p645_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 645, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-593SCREW\nWIRE 83\nSTEERING\nSELECTSWITCHENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nSTEERING\nSELECT\nSWITCH\nWIRE 83\nCIRCUITBREAKER CB9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \ncircuit breaker CB9 where wire 83 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (a) If voltage is present, go to Step 3 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB9 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-593SCREW\nWIRE 83\nSTEERING\nSELECTSWITCHENGINE\nSTART\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nSTEERING\nSELECT\nSWITCH\nWIRE 83\nCIRCUITBREAKER CB9VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connec"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p645_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 645, "text": " present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB9 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(8) Install access panel and four screws. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove four screws from instrument \npanel. (2) Raise instrument panel out to reach \nsteering select switch. (3) Set multimeter to volts dc. (4) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nsteering select switch where wire 83 \nconnects. (5) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (6) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (7) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage is present, go to Step 4 \nof this fault. (b) If voltage is not present, repair \nwire 83 (Para 8-48). (8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). TR01587", "snippet": " present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB9 (Para 8-11). (6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p646_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 646, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59442. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB9 OK. Wire 83 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nSteering select switch faulty. Wire 84 faulty. Wire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, steering \nselect switch is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB9 OK.Wire 83 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nSteering select switch faulty.Wire 84 faulty.Wire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, steering \nselect switch is faulty.4\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect switch where wire 84 \nconnects? YESNOReplace steering \nselect switch \n(Para 8-7).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59442. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB9 OK. Wire 83 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nSteering se"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p646_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 646, "text": "SON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, steering \nselect switch is faulty.4\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect switch where wire 84 \nconnects? YESNOReplace steering \nselect switch \n(Para 8-7).\n5\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect switch where wire 85 \nconnects? YESNOReplace steering \nselect switch\n(Para 8-7).Go to Step 6 of this \nfault. Go to Step 7 of this \nfault.", "snippet": "SON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, steering \nselect switch is faulty.4\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect switch where wire 84 \nconnects? YESNOReplace steering \nselect switch \n(Para 8-7)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p647_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 647, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-595SCREW\nWIRE 85\nWIRE 84STEERING\nSELECTSWITCHENGINE \nSTART\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nSTEERING\nSELECT\nSWITCHVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Raise instrument panel out to reach \nsteering select switch. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc. (3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nsteering select switch where wire 84 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Switch steering select switch to CRAB \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nsteering select switch (Para 8-7).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-595SCREW\nWIRE 85\nWIRE 84STEERING\nSELECTSWITCHENGINE \nSTART\nSWITCHINSTRUMENT\nPANEL\nSTEERING\nSELECT\nSWITCHVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Raise instrument panel out to reach \nsteering select swit"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p647_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 647, "text": " (7) Switch steering select switch to CRAB \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nsteering select switch (Para 8-7).\n(8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Raise instrument panel out to reach \nsteering select switch. (2) Set multimeter to volts dc.(3) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nsteering select switch where wire 85 \nconnects. (4) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (7) Switch steering select switch to 4 \nWHEEL position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nsteering select switch (Para 8-7).", "snippet": " (7) Switch steering select switch to CRAB \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, go to Step 6 of \nthis fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nsteering select switch (Para 8-7)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p647_chunk_2", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 647, "text": ") Switch steering select switch to 4 \nWHEEL position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nsteering select switch (Para 8-7).\n(8) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (9) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (10) Install instrument panel and four \nscrews.TR01588", "snippet": ") Switch steering select switch to 4 \nWHEEL position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, go to Step 7 of \nthis fault. (b) If voltage is not present, replace \nsteering select switch (Para 8-7)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p648_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 648, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59642. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB9 OK. Wire 83 OK. Steering select switch OK.Wire 85 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 84 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test. STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 84 \nand/or connector is faulty. KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK. Circuit breaker CB9 OK.Wire 83 OK. Steering select switch OK. Wire 84 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 85 faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage Test.STE/ICE-R #89. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 85 \nand/or connector is faulty.6\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect valve where wire 84 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 84 \nand/or connector\n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-59642. STEERING SELECT SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nWipers OK. Steering select valve OK. Wire 3 OK.Circuit breaker CB9 OK. Wire 83 OK. Steering select switch OK.Wir"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p648_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 648, "text": "N FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 85 \nand/or connector is faulty.6\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect valve where wire 84 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 84 \nand/or connector\n(Para 8-48).\n7\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect valve where wire 85 \nconnects. YESNORepair wire 85\nand/or connector(Para 8-48).Replace steering select valve\n(Para 14-10). Replace steering \nselect valve(Para 14-10).", "snippet": "N FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 85 \nand/or connector is faulty.6\nIs voltage present at steering \nselect valve where wire 84 \nconnects? YESNORepair wire 84 \nand/or connector\n(Para 8-48)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p649_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 649, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-597WIRE 85\nWIRE 84VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nsteering select valve where wire 84 connects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Switch steering select switch to CRAB \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, replace steering \nselect valve (Para 14-10). (b) If voltage is not present, repair wire \n84 and/or connector (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-597WIRE 85\nWIRE 84VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc. (2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nsteering select valve where wire 84 connects. (3) Connect multimeter n"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p649_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 649, "text": "sent, repair wire \n84 and/or connector (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.(2) Connect multimeter positive lead (+) to \nsteering select valve where wire 85 \nconnects. (3) Connect multimeter negative lead (–) to \nknown good ground. (4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10). (6) Switch steering select switch to 4 \nWHEEL position (TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If voltage present, replace steering \nselect valve (Para 14-10). (b) If voltage is not present, repair wire \n85 and/or connector (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Install battery cover (Para 8-42).TR01589", "snippet": "sent, repair wire \n84 and/or connector (Para 8-48). (7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42)."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p650_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 650, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5982\n43. PARKING BRAKE SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F)\nMultimeter, Digital (Item 9, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)Personnel Required\nTwo\nReferences\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P. KNOWN INFO\nBattery OK. Battery cable OK. Run relay K1 OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Parking brake switch faulty.Wire 75 faulty. Parking brake solenoid faulty. Ground faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-5982\n43. PARKING BRAKE SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nSTE/ICE-R (Item 17, Appendix F"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p650_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 650, "text": "LE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Parking brake switch faulty.Wire 75 faulty. Parking brake solenoid faulty. Ground faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nThis question eliminates possible \nproblems and determines where troubleshooting continues.1\nIs voltage present at circuit \nbreaker CB1 where wire 3 \nconnects?WARNING\nRead WARNING on\nfollowing page.START\nYESNORepair wire 3 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "LE PROBLEMS\nWire 3 faulty. Circuit breaker CB1 faulty. Wire 10 faulty. Parking brake switch faulty.Wire 75 faulty. Parking brake solenoid faulty. Ground faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.STE/ICE-R #89."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p651_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 651, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-599WIRE 10WIRE 3CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nENGINE START \u001f\nSWITCHWARNING\n• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can catch on \nequipment and cause injury or short ac ross electrical circuit and cause severe burns or electrical shock. • Battery acid is harmful to skin and eyes. Always  wear eye protection when working with batteries. VOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove battery cover (Para 8-42). (2) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (3) Remove four screws and access panel.(4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead to \nwire 3 where wire 3 connects to circuit \nbreaker (CB1). (6) Connect multimeter negative lead to \nknown good ground.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-599WIRE 10WIRE 3CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nENGINE START \u001f\nSWITCHWARNING\n• Remove rings, bracelets, watches, necklac es, and any other jewelry before working around vehicle. Jewelry can "}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p651_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 651, "text": "ccess panel.(4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead to \nwire 3 where wire 3 connects to circuit \nbreaker (CB1). (6) Connect multimeter negative lead to \nknown good ground.\n(7) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42). (8) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 2 of \nthis fault. (b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 3 (Para 8-48). (9) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10). (10) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "ccess panel.(4) Set multimeter to volts dc. (5) Connect multimeter positive lead to \nwire 3 where wire 3 connects to circuit \nbreaker (CB1). (6) Connect multimeter negative lead to \nknown good ground."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p652_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 652, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-60043. PARKING BRAKE SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.\nRun relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB1 faulty.Wire 10 faulty.Parking brake switch faulty.\nWire 75 faulty.\nParking brake solenoid faulty.Ground faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, circuit \nbreaker CB1 is faulty.2\nIs voltage present at circuit \nbreaker CB1 where wire 10 \nconnects?\nYESNOReplace circuit \nbreaker CB1 \n(Para 8-11)", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-60043. PARKING BRAKE SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.\nRun relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCircuit breaker CB1 faulty.Wire 10 faul"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p653_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 653, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-601WIRE 10WIRE 3CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nENGINE START\nSWITCHVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead to \nwire 10 where wire 10 connects to circuit breaker CB1.\n(3) Connect multimeter negative lead to \nknown good ground.\n(4) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(5) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 3 of \nthis fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, replace \ncircuit breaker CB1 (Para 8-11).\n(6) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(7) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(8) Install access panel and four screws.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-601WIRE 10WIRE 3CIRCUIT BREAKER CB1\nENGINE START\nSWITCHVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(2) Connect multimeter positive lead to \nwire 10 where wire 10 connects to cir"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p654_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 654, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-60243. PARKING BRAKE SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.\nRun relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB1 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty.\nParking brake switch faulty.\nWire 75 faulty.\nParking brake solenoid faulty.Ground faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVoltage test.\nSTE/ICE-R #89.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf voltage is not present, wire 10 is \nfaulty.3\nIs voltage present at parking \nbrake switch where wire 10 \nconnects?\nYESNORepair wire 10 \n(Para 8-48).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-60243. PARKING BRAKE SWITCH DOES NOT OPERATE (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nBattery OK.\nBattery cable OK.\nRun relay K1 OK.Wire 3 OK.\nCircuit breaker CB1 OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nWire 10 faulty."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p655_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 655, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-603\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove screws a nd console access \npanel to access switch.\n(2) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead to \nwire 10 where wire 10 connects to \nparking brake switch.\n(4) Connect multimeter negative lead to \nknown good ground.\n(5) Connect negative battery cable to \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).\n(6) Turn engine start switch to ON position, \nBUT DO NOT START ENGINE, \n(TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(a) If 24 vdc is present, go to Step 4 of \nthis fault.\n(b) If 24 vdc is not present, repair \nwire 10 (Para 8-48).\n(7) Turn engine start switch to OFF \nposition (TM 10-3930-673-10).\n(8) Disconnect negative battery cable from \nnegative side of battery (Para 8-42).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-603\nVOLTAGE TEST\n(1) Remove screws a nd console access \npanel to access switch.\n(2) Set multimeter to volts dc.\n(3) Connect multimeter positive lead to \nwire 10 where wire 10 con"}
