{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p818_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 818, "text": ". Light ON, switch OK. Air conditioner belt OK. Lines and fittings OK.Condenser OK. Filter-drier OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nEvaporator obstructed, damaged. Compressor faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf evaporator in cab is obstructed or \ndamaged, evaporator will not function properly.4\nAre condenser fins free to \nradiate captured heat? Is \ncondenser free from signs of \ndamage? YESNOClean dirt and \ndebris from \ncondenser fins, or replace damaged \ncondenser. 5\nIs there an adequate flow of \nair across evaporator fins? Is \nevaporator free from signs of \ndamage? YESNOClean evaporator \nfins or replace damaged \nevaporator.", "snippet": ". Light ON, switch OK. Air conditioner belt OK. Lines and fittings OK.Condenser OK. Filter-drier OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nEvaporator obstructed, damaged. Compressor faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p819_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 819, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-767HEATER EVAPORATORCONDENSER\nVISUAL INSPECTION\nVisually inspect condens er fins for dirt and \ndebris or signs of damage. (a) If condenser fins are free to radiate \nheat and condenser is free from \nsigns of damage, go to Step 5 of \nthis fault. (b) If condenser fins are blocked by \ndirt and debris, clean condenser with water or air (under pressure). (c) If condenser shows signs of \ndamage, notify Direct Support Maintenance. EVAPORATOR\nVISUAL INSPECTION\nVisually inspect evapora tor fins for dirt and \ndebris, and for signs of damage. (a) If evaporator fins are clean and \nfree from damage, go to Step 6 of this fault. (b) If evaporator fins obstructed with \ndirt and debris, clean fins.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-767HEATER EVAPORATORCONDENSER\nVISUAL INSPECTION\nVisually inspect condens er fins for dirt and \ndebris or signs of damage. (a) If condenser fins are free to radiate \nheat and cond"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p819_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 819, "text": " for dirt and \ndebris, and for signs of damage. (a) If evaporator fins are clean and \nfree from damage, go to Step 6 of this fault. (b) If evaporator fins obstructed with \ndirt and debris, clean fins.\n(c) If evaporator shows signs of \ndamage, repair or replace \nevaporator.TR01477RADIATORCONDENSOR\nCONNECTIONS", "snippet": " for dirt and \ndebris, and for signs of damage. (a) If evaporator fins are clean and \nfree from damage, go to Step 6 of this fault. (b) If evaporator fins obstructed with \ndirt and debris, clean fins."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p820_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 820, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-76826. AIR CONDITIONER DOES  NOT COOL CAB (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nAir conditioner does  not cool cab.\nLight ON, switch OK.\nAir conditioner belt OK.Lines and fittings OK.\nCondenser OK.\nFilter-drier OK.Evaporator OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nCompressor faulty.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf compressor is leaking or faulty, \ncompressor will not function properly.6\nDoes compressor run \nsmoothly without unusual \nnoise? Is compressor free from signs of leaks?\nYESNONotify DIrect \nSupport to repair or \nreplace faulty \ncompressor.\nNotify Direct Support of this fault.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-76826. AIR CONDITIONER DOES  NOT COOL CAB (CONT).\nKNOWN INFO\nAir conditioner does  not cool cab.\nLight ON, switch OK.\nAir conditioner belt OK.Lines and fittings OK.\nCondenser OK."}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p821_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 821, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-769\nCOMPRESSOR\nVISUAL INSPECTION\nCheck compressor (clutch, shaft, and \nmounting components, for example) for \nunusual noise. Leak check compressor.\n(a) If compressor runs smoothly and is \nfree from signs of leaks, notify Direct Support about this fault.\n(b) If compressor runs with unusual \nnoise and/or shows signs of leaks, notify Direct Support to repair \nfaulty components or replace compressor. \nTR01479", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-769\nCOMPRESSOR\nVISUAL INSPECTION\nCheck compressor (clutch, shaft, and \nmounting components, for example) for \nunusual noise. Leak check compressor.\n(a) If compressor runs smoothl"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p822_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 822, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-770     Change 12\n27. ARCTIC HEATER DOES NOT OPERATE CORRECTLY\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nRefrigerant Leak Detect or (Item 13, Appendix F)\nEquipment Condition\nEngine shut down (TM 10-3930-673-10)\nParking brake on (TM 10-3930-673-10)Wheels chocked (TM 10-3930-673-10)References\nTM 10-3930-673-10TM 9-4910-571-12&P\nKNOWN INFO\nNone.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nBlown fuse.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nTo determine the condition of the \nfuses.1\nIs arctic heater assembly in- \nline fuse okay?START\nYESNOReplace fuse (Para 20-\n4).If fuse blows again, replace arctic heater assembly wiring harness (Para 20-4).\nIf fuse blows again, replace arctic heater \nassembly (Para 20-2).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-770     Change 12\n27. ARCTIC HEATER DOES NOT OPERATE CORRECTLY\nINITIAL SETUP\nTools and Special Tools\nTool Kit, General Mechanic’s: Automotive\n(Item 18, Appendix F)\nRefrigerant Le"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p823_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 823, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\nChange  1       2-770.1KNOWN INFO\nFuse is OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nLines restricted, leaking, or \ndamaged.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf cooling system does not operate \ncorrectly, the arctic heater will not \noperate.\nKNOWN INFO\nCoolant lines are OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nFuel line damaged, restricted, or \nleaking.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf the fuel line is damaged the \nheater will not operate.\nTR014752\nAre coolant lines to arctic \nheater assembly restricted, \nleaking, or damaged?\nNOYESRepair or replace \ncoolant lines to \nheater assembly.\n3\nIs fuel line to arctic heater \nassembly restricted, leaking, \nor damaged?\nYES\nNOReplace fuel line to \nheater assembly.", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\nChange  1       2-770.1KNOWN INFO\nFuse is OK.\nPOSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nLines restricted, leaking, or \ndamaged.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection.\nREASON FOR QUESTION\nIf cooling system does no"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p824_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 824, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-770.2      Change 127. ARCTIC HEATER DOES NOT OPERATE CORRECTLY (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nFuel line is OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nDebris blocking the intake.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf the intake is blocked, the heater \nwill not operate. KNOWN INFO\nIntake is OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nExhaust is plugged.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf exhaust is plugged the heater will \nnot operate correctly.4\nIs intake port on bottom of \narctic heater assembly \nblocked or damaged? YES\nNOIf debris is blocking \nthe intake port, clear it away. 5\nIs exhaust port and tube on \nbottom of arctic heater \nassembly blocked or damaged?", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\n2-770.2      Change 127. ARCTIC HEATER DOES NOT OPERATE CORRECTLY (CONT). KNOWN INFO\nFuel line is OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nDebris blocking the intake.TEST OPTIONS\nVisual inspection. R"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p824_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 824, "text": "bottom of \narctic heater assembly \nblocked or damaged? YES\nNOIf debris is blocking \nthe intake port, clear it away. 5\nIs exhaust port and tube on \nbottom of arctic heater \nassembly blocked or damaged?\nYES\nNOIf debris is blocking \nthe exhaust tube or \nport clear it away.If intake port appears to be damaged, \nreplace arctic heater \nassembly (Para 20-2). If exhaust tube appears to be damaged, replace \nexhaust tube (Para \n20-2). If exhaust port appears to be damaged, replace \nheater assembly \n(Para 20-2).", "snippet": "bottom of \narctic heater assembly \nblocked or damaged? YES\nNOIf debris is blocking \nthe intake port, clear it away. 5\nIs exhaust port and tube on \nbottom of arctic heater \nassembly blocked or damaged?"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p825_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 825, "text": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\nChange  1       2-770.3 \nKNOWN INFO\nExhaust is OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nHeater wiring harness is damaged.TEST OPTIONS\nMultimeter. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf the harness is damaged the \nheater will not operate. KNOWN INFO\nHeater is getting power. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nOpen ground.TEST OPTIONS\nMultimeter. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf the ground is open the heater will \nnot operate. TR014766\nIs there power to heater \nassembly? (1) Place battery disconnect switch \nin OFF position. (2) Disconnect cannon plug to \narctic heater assembly. (3) Place battery disconnect switch \nin ON position. (4) Using multimeter, measure \nvoltage between cannon plug \npin H harness side (red wire) \nand ground. Is there battery voltage present? Replace arctic heater assembly \nwiring harness (Para 20-4).", "snippet": "TM 10-3930-673-20-1\nChange  1       2-770.3 \nKNOWN INFO\nExhaust is OK. POSSIBLE PROBLEMS\nHeater wiring harness is damaged.TEST OPTIONS\nMultimeter. REASON FOR QUESTION\nIf the harness is damaged the \nhe"}
{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p825_chunk_1", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 825, "text": "on. (4) Using multimeter, measure \nvoltage between cannon plug \npin H harness side (red wire) \nand ground. Is there battery voltage present? Replace arctic heater assembly \nwiring harness (Para 20-4).\n7\nIs the arctic heater assembly \nground wire okay? Using a multimeter, measure \nresistance between cannon plug pin 1 harness side (brown wire) and \nground. Is there battery voltage present? YESReplace arctic \nheater assembly \nwiring harness \n(Para 20-4).NO\nYES\nNO", "snippet": "on. (4) Using multimeter, measure \nvoltage between cannon plug \npin H harness side (red wire) \nand ground. Is there battery voltage present? Replace arctic heater assembly \nwiring harness (Para 20-4)."}
