75 ±225 Crank on the GO DCA-CABLE W1 0 0-100 100 MILLIOHMS/\nSECOND\nAlternator Output Voltage 82 — 2,000 RPM DCA-CABLE W1 24 24-28.5 28.5 VOLTS DC\nAlternator Negative Cable   Voltage Drop84 — Idle DCA-CABLE W1 0 0-1 1 VOLTS DC\nFuel Return Pressure 50 ±150 2,000 RPM DCA-CABLE W1, W4 0 0-20 20 PSI", "snippet": " Fuel Level\n2. Oil Level 5. Batteries3. Coolant LevelPOWERING UP VTM\n1.Connect VTM to W1 cable. W1 cable attaches to batteries. 2. Enter VID into VTM using test 60.3. Perform confidence test, test 66."}
