{"id": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf_p1044_chunk_0", "source": "TM-10-3930-673-20-1.pdf", "page": 1044, "text": "This fine document... Was brought to you by me:\n   Liberated Manuals -- free army and government manuals\nWhy do I do it? I am tired of sleazy CD-ROM sellers, who take publicly \navailable information, slap “watermarks” and other junk on it, and sell it. Those masters of search engine manipulation make sure that their sites that \nsell free information, come up first in search engines. They did not create it... They did not even scan it... Why should they get your money? Why are not \nletting you give those free manuals to your friends? I am setting this document FREE. This document was made by the US \nGovernment and is NOT protected by Copyright. Feel free to share, \nrepublish, sell and so on. I am not asking you for donations, fees or handouts.", "snippet": "This fine document... Was brought to you by me:\n   Liberated Manuals -- free army and government manuals\nWhy do I do it? I am tired of sleazy CD-ROM sellers, who take publicly \navailable information, "}
