{"id": "Carrier small hvac.pdf_p4_chunk_0", "source": "Carrier small hvac.pdf", "page": 4, "text": "4REMOTE CONTROL\nFig. 3 − Remote Contr oller\nFUNCTION BUTTONS\nBefore you begin using your new air conditioner, make sure to familiarize yourself with the remote control. The following is a brief\nintroduction to the remote control. FP\nActivate/Disable freeze\nprotection functionON/OFF \nTurns the unit on or off\nMODE\nScrolls through operation \nmodes as follows: \nAUT O \n/b2right \nCOOL \n/b2right \nDR Y\n /b2right\n HEA T \n/b2right \nFAN\nFAN/SLC  \nSelects fan speeds in the\nfollowing order: \nAUT O /b2right LOW /b2right\n MED /b2right\n HIGH\nSLEEP  \nSaves energy during Hold down this button for\n2 seconds to activate theSilence function. sleeping hours\nTURBO \nEnables unit to reach \npreset temperature in\nshortest possible time TEMP/triangleup\n/triangleupIncreases temperature in \nO1 F (1 °C) increments\nMax.", "snippet": "4REMOTE CONTROL\nFig. 3 − Remote Contr oller\nFUNCTION BUTTONS\nBefore you begin using your new air conditioner, make sure to familiarize yourself with the remote control. The following is a brief\nintrod"}
