{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p1_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 1, "text": "MRI Technical Operations Manual\n\nDocument Version  Final  v3.0; 27-Jul-2021   \nSponsor  Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nProtocol Identifier  002 \nProtocol Version Version 1. 2, 01-Feb-2021  \nProtocol Description  The Parkinson’s Progression Markers Initiative (PPMI) Clinical -  \nEstablishing a Deeply Phenotyped PD Cohort", "snippet": "MRI Technical Operations Manual\n\nDocument Version  Final  v3.0; 27-Jul-2021   \nSponsor  Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nProtocol Identifier  002 \nProtocol Version Version 1. 2, 01-Feb-2021  \nProtocol Desc"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p1_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 1, "text": "otocol Identifier  002 \nProtocol Version Version 1. 2, 01-Feb-2021  \nProtocol Description  The Parkinson’s Progression Markers Initiative (PPMI) Clinical -  \nEstablishing a Deeply Phenotyped PD Cohort\nConfidential  \nThe information provided in this document is strictly confidential and is intended solely for the guidance \nof the clinical investigation. Reproduction or disclosure of this document – whether in part or in full – to \nparties not associated with the clinical investigation or its use for any other purpose without the prior \nwritten consent of the Sponsor is not permitted.  This document may be disclosed to appropriate \ninstitutional review boards, independent ethics committees, or duly authorized representatives of the US \nFood and Drug Administration (United States), the Bureau of Pharmaceutical Assessment (Canada), the \nEU C linical Trials Register (Europe), or other regulatory bodies.", "snippet": "otocol Identifier  002 \nProtocol Version Version 1. 2, 01-Feb-2021  \nProtocol Description  The Parkinson’s Progression Markers Initiative (PPMI) Clinical -  \nEstablishing a Deeply Phenotyped PD Cohort"}
