{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p22_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 22, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 22 of 38\nTable 7: NM -MT Sequence  \n2D Gradient recalled echo  with MT preparation   \nSeries Description  2D GRE -MT \nPlane  Oblique, follow instructions  \nSlice thickness (mm)  1.5 mm \nNumber of slices  16 \nPhase encode dir. Right -Left (RL)  \nMatrix  440x 440  \nFOV (mm)  220x220  \nVoxel Size  (mm)  0.5 x 0.5 x 1.5  \nRepetition Time (ms)  ~ 465 ms  \nTE Minimum (< 5  ms)  \nFlip angle  40 \nMT Puls e FA 300° \nMT offset Frequency  1.5 kHz (3.0  T) \nMT pulse dura tion 10 ms \nMeasurements  5 \nScan Time  ~ 10 minutes  \nReceive Band Width  <500 Hz/Pixel  \nPlease note:  Exact parameters for th e sequence may differ slightly by site and will be decided \nas part of site set- up. 5.6 DTI Sequence \nPlease instruct the participant  to keep still during the entire scan.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 22 of 38\nTable 7: NM -MT Sequence  \n2D Gradient recalled"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p22_chunk_2", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 22, "text": ":  Exact parameters for th e sequence may differ slightly by site and will be decided \nas part of site set- up. 5.6 DTI Sequence \nPlease instruct the participant  to keep still during the entire scan.\nDTI should be acquired with \n32 directions. Slices should cover top of the brain down to base of cerebellum. Two sequences \nwith reversed phase encoding direction should be acquired in full to correct for susceptibility  \ninduced distortions. If acquiring a phantom scan, only one sequence with reverse phase \nencoding direction should be acquired. The following parameters  in Table 8 should be used.", "snippet": ":  Exact parameters for th e sequence may differ slightly by site and will be decided \nas part of site set- up. 5.6 DTI Sequence \nPlease instruct the participant  to keep still during the entire scan."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p23_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 23, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 23 of 38", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 23 of 38"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p23_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 23, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 23 of 38\nTable 8: Diffusion Sequence  \n2D Diffusion -weighted EPI  \nSeries Description  DTI_RL (and D TI_LR for the repeated scan with reverse PE)  \nPlane  Straight Axial  \nSlice thickness (mm)  2.0 with no gap  \nNumber of Slices  ~ 80 \nPhase encode dir.  R >> L  \nMatrix  128x128*   \nFOV 256x256  mm \nRepetition Time (ms)  ~10000  \nEcho Time (ms)  ~80 \nFlip angle  90 \nSlice order  Interleaved  \nNumber of directions  32 \nB-VALUE  0 and 1000  s/mm2 (B=0 images interleaved throughout if possible in \nproduct sequence)  \nInstructions  Keep still  \nScan Time  ~ 8 minutes  \nNote:  Phantoms and participant study scans will use the parameters detailed in this table.\n\nFigure 7: Example of D TI acquisition with different phase encoding direction\n\nNote the differences in the distortion pattern in Figure 7.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 23 of 38\nTable 8: Diffusion Sequence  \n2D Diffusion -wei"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p24_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 24, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 24 of 38", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 24 of 38"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p24_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 24, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 24 of 38\nPlease n ote: On GE systems reconstructed final images will be 256x256 – to prevent \ninterpolation for 128x128 matrix, you need to set USER CVs (rhrcyres = 128, \nrhrcxres=128,rhimsize=128)  \nPlease note: Exact parameters for the sequence may differ slightly by site and will be decided as part of site set- up. 5.7 3D T2 FLAIR Sequence \nA high-resolution 3D T2 FLAIR sequence will be acquired in the sagittal plane, with a slice thickness \nof 1.2 mm or less , for assessment of white matter disease, and other pathology. Additional required \nparameters are listed See Table 9 for parameters.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 24 of 38\nPlease n ote: On GE systems reconstructed final"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p24_chunk_2", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 24, "text": "d in the sagittal plane, with a slice thickness \nof 1.2 mm or less , for assessment of white matter disease, and other pathology. Additional required \nparameters are listed See Table 9 for parameters.\nTable 9: 3D T2 FLAIR Sequence  \n3D T2 FLAIR Sequence   \nSeries Description  3D T2 FLAIR  \nPlane  Sagittal  \nSlice thickness (mm)  1.0 – 1.2 (slice thickness must remain consistent)  \nNumber of slices  192 (please adjust slice thickness up to 1.2 mm to cover brain, not the \nnumber of slices) \nVoxel size (mm)  1.0*1.0  mm in plane resolution  \nPhase encode dir. Anterior -Posterior (AP)  \nMatrix  256 x 256 (the use of interpolation, zero -filling or a ZIP factor is not \npermitted)  \nTR/TE/FA/other \nparamete rs Will be defined by Invicro according to the scanner  \nFOV 256 mm (full FOV required, no rectangular FOV)  \nScan Time  ~ 7 minutes  \nNote:  Phantoms and participant study scans will use the parameters detailed in this table.", "snippet": "d in the sagittal plane, with a slice thickness \nof 1.2 mm or less , for assessment of white matter disease, and other pathology. Additional required \nparameters are listed See Table 9 for parameters."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p24_chunk_3", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 24, "text": "cro according to the scanner  \nFOV 256 mm (full FOV required, no rectangular FOV)  \nScan Time  ~ 7 minutes  \nNote:  Phantoms and participant study scans will use the parameters detailed in this table.\nThe FOV must include the entire brain anatomy including the vertex, cerebellum and pons. To avoid \nartifacts, position the participant such that there is sufficient empt y space around the head: \napproximately 1.5 cm of air or more above the top of the head, and leave 1  - 2 blank slices on top of \nthe head. Avoid nose ghosting.  \nPlease note : Parallel imaging may be utilized to reduce scan time. Please adhere to \nmanufacturer r ecommendations when incorporating this scan technique (GRAPPA for \nSiemens and ASSET for GE ). \nPlease note: Exact parameters for the sequence may differ slightly by site and will be decided \nas part of site set- up.", "snippet": "cro according to the scanner  \nFOV 256 mm (full FOV required, no rectangular FOV)  \nScan Time  ~ 7 minutes  \nNote:  Phantoms and participant study scans will use the parameters detailed in this table."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p25_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 25, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 25 of 38", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 25 of 38"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p25_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 25, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 25 of 38\n5.8 MRI Series Description \nThe Series Description for each sequence should be labeled as described in Table 10. Table 10: MRI Series Description  \nSequence Name  Series Description  \nT1-weighted, 3D volumetric sequence  3D T1 -weighted  \n2D Gradient -echo T2* -weighted EPI  (BOLD)  rsfMRI _RL \nRepeat 2D Gradient -echo T2* -weighted EPI  (BOLD)  rsfMRI_LR  \nNM-MT 2D GRE -MT \nDTI DTI_RL  \nRepeat  DTI DTI_LR  \n3D T2 FLAIR  3D T2 FLAIR  \n6 Image Data Archiving and Submission \n6.1 Data Submission Checklist  \nAll imaging metadata and data files should be sent through iPACS. Modality specific electronic \nsubmission forms are required to be completed within iPACS for each data submission.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 25 of 38\n5.8 MRI Series Description \nThe Series Descript"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p25_chunk_2", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 25, "text": "mission Checklist  \nAll imaging metadata and data files should be sent through iPACS. Modality specific electronic \nsubmission forms are required to be completed within iPACS for each data submission.\nPlease \nreference Section 1.3.3 of this document, and the clinical protocol for details on the schedule of \nassessments. • Image data for uploading into the submission form  \n• Imaging procedure and participant visit information for entry into the submission form (an \nexample of the electronic submission forms utilized for this study is provided in the appendices of this manual).", "snippet": "mission Checklist  \nAll imaging metadata and data files should be sent through iPACS. Modality specific electronic \nsubmission forms are required to be completed within iPACS for each data submission."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p26_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 26, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 26 of 38\n\n6.2 Image Data Submission\n\n1 Access the submission portal  using the web address  \nprovided below:  \nhttps://corelab- submission.ipacs.invicro.com/\n\n2 Log in : a unique username and password is provided to \npersonnel responsible for data submission.  \n3 Upon successful login, you will be directed to the Submission Dashboard.  Click Add Submission  \nto create a new submission.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 26 of 38\n\n6.2 Image Data Submission\n\n1 Access the submis"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p26_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 26, "text": "and password is provided to \npersonnel responsible for data submission.  \n3 Upon successful login, you will be directed to the Submission Dashboard.  Click Add Submission  \nto create a new submission.\nImaging data will be transferred to Invicro using the iPACS web submission \nportal. Invicro's  portal uses an electronic transmittal form to capture all relevant \nscan information, and programmatically de- identifies images in DICOM format \nduring upload.  Invicro will provide each user at the imaging site with a unique \nusername and password to access  Invicro’s iPACS web -based upload tool. In \nthe event there are questions regarding the submission you may be contacted \nby a member of the Invicro team.  \nFollow the steps outlined below to perform an iPACS data submission:", "snippet": "and password is provided to \npersonnel responsible for data submission.  \n3 Upon successful login, you will be directed to the Submission Dashboard.  Click Add Submission  \nto create a new submission."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p27_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 27, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 27 of 38\n\n4 Click on Site/Protocol  to create a Submission drop- down listing and select the appropriate \nstudy/clinical site to submit under.  \n5 The submission form  will display a set of study and modality specific parameter fields to be \ncompleted. The file upload section is displayed on the right -hand side of the submission page for \nuploading of image data and other required documentation.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 27 of 38\n\n4 Click on Site/Protocol  to create a Submissi"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p27_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 27, "text": " modality specific parameter fields to be \ncompleted. The file upload section is displayed on the right -hand side of the submission page for \nuploading of image data and other required documentation.\n6 Fill in the submission form with the requested study -specific  and modality information. Use the free \ntext Comments  field to provide any explanatory not es related to the data submission and acquisition \nprocedures.  \nPlease Note: It is very important that the correct cohort designation and visit number for each \nscan are entered in the submission form, as this determines the processing pipeline used for \nthe scan. Participants enrolled in PPMI 001 will start at the equivalent visit in PPMI Clinical . \n• Current PPMI 001 participants will be divided into the following: \no Healthy Control  \no PD", "snippet": " modality specific parameter fields to be \ncompleted. The file upload section is displayed on the right -hand side of the submission page for \nuploading of image data and other required documentation."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p28_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 28, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 28 of 38\n\no Prodromal  \n• Newly enrolled PPMI Clinical  participants will be divided into the following:  \no Healthy Control  \no PD \no Prodromal  \n7 Prepare your image data folder for uploading into the submission form. P rior to uploading place \nyour files in a compressed (zipped) folder.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 28 of 38\n\no Prodromal  \n• Newly enrolled PPMI Clinical  "}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p29_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 29, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 29 of 38\n\n8 Drag and drop the compressed zipped folder containing the files or click Select Files to search for \nand select the files for import.\n\n9 To complete the submission, click on the Submit button. You will be prompted to enter your \nunique user password to complete the submission.\n\nIn the event electronic submission is not available for the imaging center, physical shipment \ninformation will be provided on an as needed basis.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 29 of 38\n\n8 Drag and drop the compressed zipped folder c"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p30_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 30, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 30 of 38", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 30 of 38"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p30_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 30, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 30 of 38\n6.3 iPACS Submission Form Comments Section \n A comments section is included in the iPACS submission form. This is a text -entry field where \nexplanatory notes and useful information regarding the imaging procedure can be provided, for eg \njustification for alternate imaging or parameter variations. Comments provided are reviewed during \nQC of the data and in some cases prevent the need for a query to be issued. 6.4 Scanner QC & Maintenance Documentation \nA scanner QC section is contained within the iPACS submission form. Utilize the provided fields to \ndocument recent routine preventative maintenance, software upgrades or repairs and QC checks \nperformed.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 30 of 38\n6.3 iPACS Submission Form Comments Section \n A "}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p30_chunk_2", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 30, "text": "anner QC section is contained within the iPACS submission form. Utilize the provided fields to \ndocument recent routine preventative maintenance, software upgrades or repairs and QC checks \nperformed.\nInvicro should be notified in advance or immediately  after any scanner events which may affect the \nperformance of your MRI  scanner such as hardware/software upgrades, un- scheduled maintenance \nor repairs. In such circumstanc es, notify the Invicro study contacts provided in this TOM. 6.5 QC and Query Resolution Process \nImage data received at Invicro will undergo a rigorous quality inspection. QC checks will include the following, but are not limited to:  \n• De-identification of all participant s protected health information  \n• Accurate completion of the iPACS Submission form  \n• Completeness of image files  \n• Adherence to the imaging protocol and parameters approved by Invicro \nInvicro will generate a query within iPACS should any question arise regarding the data submission.", "snippet": "anner QC section is contained within the iPACS submission form. Utilize the provided fields to \ndocument recent routine preventative maintenance, software upgrades or repairs and QC checks \nperformed."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p30_chunk_3", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 30, "text": "ompleteness of image files  \n• Adherence to the imaging protocol and parameters approved by Invicro \nInvicro will generate a query within iPACS should any question arise regarding the data submission.\nRespond to the queries promptly within 24 hours  of receipt. Upon completion of an iPACS submission, you will receive an auto -generated \nemail notification from the corelab_support inbox confirming successful transfer. The email will display a summary of the submission details. Please \nretain a copy of this email for your records and reference. If you do not receive an email notification following submission, contact: \nCorelab_Support@invicro.com     \nFor all other technical support related to iPACS and data submission, please, contact:                                            \nCorelab_Support@Invicro.com", "snippet": "ompleteness of image files  \n• Adherence to the imaging protocol and parameters approved by Invicro \nInvicro will generate a query within iPACS should any question arise regarding the data submission."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p31_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 31, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 31 of 38\n\nDepending upon the nature of the issue, the resolution of a query may involve simple provision of \nadditional information, resending of one or more image data files, or other action to ensure the \ncompleteness of the image data files.  \nTo resolve any issues that arise, Invicro will employ the query resolution process outlined below:  \n1 You will receive an iPACS generated email notifying you \na query has been issued on one of your data submissions. The email will include a link to the portal for resolution of the \nquery.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 31 of 38\n\nDepending upon the nature of the issue, the re"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p31_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 31, "text": "d below:  \n1 You will receive an iPACS generated email notifying you \na query has been issued on one of your data submissions. The email will include a link to the portal for resolution of the \nquery.\n2 Log into the iPACS portal and navigate to the Submissions \npage. Queries will be listed in the Queries tab of the \nsubmission page.\n\n3 Select the query to be addressed and you will be brought to the Respond to Query page. The \nQuer y Details tab will show all queried categories and a description of the issue.", "snippet": "d below:  \n1 You will receive an iPACS generated email notifying you \na query has been issued on one of your data submissions. The email will include a link to the portal for resolution of the \nquery."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p32_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 32, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 32 of 38\n\n4 Navigate to the bottom section with the heading, Current Task: Acknowledge Query.  Under \nthe What would you like to do next?  section, choose Edit Submission to respond to the query \nfrom the drop- down list and then click Submit.  \nThis action will bring you bac k to the Submission Tasks page. Click on Submission Tasks. \nClick on the queried submission and fill out the queried fields. You will once again be asked to \nauthenticate the entry with your login password. Click on submit to re- submit the study to Invicro.  \n5 Example of common query types and guidance to prevent/resolve queries:", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 32 of 38\n\n4 Navigate to the bottom section with the head"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p32_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 32, "text": " once again be asked to \nauthenticate the entry with your login password. Click on submit to re- submit the study to Invicro.  \n5 Example of common query types and guidance to prevent/resolve queries:\nQuery type  Guidance to prevent/resolve queries  \nTime Point Verification Ensure the correct visit is selected when submitting \nthe data.  \nIncorrect Acquisition \nProtocol Followed  Take measures to minimize deviations to the approved \nimaging procedures and always utilize the acquisition \nprotocol approved for use by Invicro. Provide \nexplanatory comments within the Comments field.  \nMissing Series or Slices  Upload the missing data within  the query form and \nprovide a comment. Do not create a new submission.  \n6 To complete the query, you will be requested to enter your iPACS password in the Signature \nfield.", "snippet": " once again be asked to \nauthenticate the entry with your login password. Click on submit to re- submit the study to Invicro.  \n5 Example of common query types and guidance to prevent/resolve queries:"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p32_chunk_2", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 32, "text": "d the missing data within  the query form and \nprovide a comment. Do not create a new submission.  \n6 To complete the query, you will be requested to enter your iPACS password in the Signature \nfield.\n7 Invicro will notify sites by email or phone if any outstanding queries are not resolved. Once \nInvicro has determined that the query has been sufficiently resolved, the query will be closed.", "snippet": "d the missing data within  the query form and \nprovide a comment. Do not create a new submission.  \n6 To complete the query, you will be requested to enter your iPACS password in the Signature \nfield."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p33_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 33, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 33 of 38", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 33 of 38"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p33_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 33, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 33 of 38\n6.6 Archiving Instructions  \nIn compliance with GCP  guidelines (or regional requirements, whichever are a higher standard), \nmaintain an archive of all image data in a readable format, using the same format that was submitted \nto Invicro. 7 QC & Calibrations  \nQC measures are to be performed according to the center and scanner manufacturer standard \nprocedures as implemented in the center’s QC  program for the MRI  scanner. 7.1 QC Procedures \nParticipating MRI facilities  must have a quality control program in place that outlines standard QC \nprocedures. The QC program must include MRI  safety policies and a prevent ative maintenance \nprogram.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 33 of 38\n6.6 Archiving Instructions  \nIn compliance with"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p33_chunk_2", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 33, "text": "icipating MRI facilities  must have a quality control program in place that outlines standard QC \nprocedures. The QC program must include MRI  safety policies and a prevent ative maintenance \nprogram.\nQC procedures,  calibrations, prevent ative maintenance, or service that has been performed \non the scanner should also be documented within the scanner QC section of the iPACS submission \nform. 7.2 Phantom Data  \nInvicro may request a phantom scan to be acquired on the MRI  scanner intended for use in the study  \nas part of the initial set -up and qualification procedures or at any time throughout the course of a study. Phantoms may be requested if imaging centers are new to Invicro, an imaging center prefers to use a \nscanner which Invicro has not previously qualified, or the phantom data previously collected by Invicro \ndoes not meet the requirements of the study.", "snippet": "icipating MRI facilities  must have a quality control program in place that outlines standard QC \nprocedures. The QC program must include MRI  safety policies and a prevent ative maintenance \nprogram."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p33_chunk_3", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 33, "text": "ew to Invicro, an imaging center prefers to use a \nscanner which Invicro has not previously qualified, or the phantom data previously collected by Invicro \ndoes not meet the requirements of the study.\nInvicro may also request a phantom acquisition be \nperformed should a qualified MRI scanner undergo significant maintenance during the study, or if \nscanner performance issues are noticed during QC  review of study participant  data. Retain the archived image data for 25 years after completion or discontinuation of the trial or per institutional guidelines, whichever is longer. Only after this period  may data be destroyed per local regulations.", "snippet": "ew to Invicro, an imaging center prefers to use a \nscanner which Invicro has not previously qualified, or the phantom data previously collected by Invicro \ndoes not meet the requirements of the study."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p34_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 34, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 34 of 38", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 34 of 38"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p34_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 34, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 34 of 38\n8 MRI Scanner Replacement or Upgrades  \nIf your center will be replacing or upgrading your MRI scanner or acquisition software, it is critical that \nyou inform Invicro prior to the replacement or upgrade occurring, so that Invicro can take the necessary \nsteps to ensure the continuity of the imaging outcome measures in this longitudinal research study. Invicro may need to revisit the imaging center to acquire another phantom.", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 34 of 38\n8 MRI Scanner Replacement or Upgrades  \nIf your"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p34_chunk_2", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 34, "text": "o can take the necessary \nsteps to ensure the continuity of the imaging outcome measures in this longitudinal research study. Invicro may need to revisit the imaging center to acquire another phantom.\n9 Supp orting Information  \n9.1 Invicro Contacts \nNote: When contacting Invicro please remember to indicate the following to ensure your \ninquiry can be addressed appropriately and expeditiously: \n• Protocol  \n• Site number  \n• Subject number (if applicable) \nFor all questions related to iPACS image data transfer or  technical  account issues: \ncorelab_support@invicro.com\n\nFor all technical questions related to MRI protocol set -up or image QC: \n Andrea Perez  \nSr. Manager I, Imaging QC & Processing  \n+1-203-401-4315 voice \naperez@invicro.com", "snippet": "o can take the necessary \nsteps to ensure the continuity of the imaging outcome measures in this longitudinal research study. Invicro may need to revisit the imaging center to acquire another phantom."}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p34_chunk_3", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 34, "text": "orelab_support@invicro.com\n\nFor all technical questions related to MRI protocol set -up or image QC: \n Andrea Perez  \nSr. Manager I, Imaging QC & Processing  \n+1-203-401-4315 voice \naperez@invicro.com\nFor all other study related questions , including the request for credentials to upload images to iPACS \nor to check the status of an Independent review result : \nAndrew Serrano  \nProject Manager I  \n+1-203-990-1638 voice \n+1-203-789-8037  \naserrano@invicro.c om Nichole Daegele  \nDirector, Project Management  \n+1-203-401-4367 voice \n+1-203-789-8037 fax  \nndaegele@invicro.com  \nIf shipping images on CD/DVD, you must use the Invicro Fed Ex # 2295 -4740 -2 and add the study \nGlobal ID # 006892 as the Reference on the shipping bill.", "snippet": "orelab_support@invicro.com\n\nFor all technical questions related to MRI protocol set -up or image QC: \n Andrea Perez  \nSr. Manager I, Imaging QC & Processing  \n+1-203-401-4315 voice \naperez@invicro.com"}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p35_chunk_0", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 35, "text": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 35 of 38\n\n9.2 TOM Amendment History \nThe table below is intended to summarize changes from the previous approved final TOM from the \nupdates in the current amendment.  Revisions or amendments to the protocol will not require an \namendment to the TOM , unless substantive changes impact imaging methods .", "snippet": "MRI TECHNICAL OPERATIONS MANUAL   Michael J. Fox Foundation  \nFinal v3.0; 27- Jul-2021               002  \n CONFIDENTIAL AND PROPRIETARY   Page 35 of 38\n\n9.2 TOM Amendment History \nThe table below is "}
{"id": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf_p35_chunk_1", "source": "MRI_TOM_Final_v3.0_20210727.pdf", "page": 35, "text": " approved final TOM from the \nupdates in the current amendment.  Revisions or amendments to the protocol will not require an \namendment to the TOM , unless substantive changes impact imaging methods .\nVersion \nNumber Version Date  Summary of  Changes  \nFinal v1.0 11-May-2020  Original  \nFinal v2.0  07-Aug-2020  • Updated to add premature withdrawal visit Section 1.3.2 and \nSection 10 (Appendix 1)  \n• Updated data submission process (Section 6)  \n• Editorial changes (global)  \nFinal v3.0  27-Jul-2021  • Updates made to Table 1 (Section 1.3.3)  \n• Updated the iPACS MR I Submission form  (Section 11.1) \n• Updated based on Protocol 002 Version 1. 2 (global)  \n• Editorial changes (global)", "snippet": " approved final TOM from the \nupdates in the current amendment.  Revisions or amendments to the protocol will not require an \namendment to the TOM , unless substantive changes impact imaging methods ."}
